Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.19,0:00:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next wave of AI is here.\N下一波人工智能浪潮已经到来。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.47,0:00:48.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Evolving beyond thinking to acting.\N从思考进化到行动。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.53,0:00:51.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's bigger than anyone imagined.\N它的规模远超任何人的想象。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.79,0:00:52.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Except AMD.\N除了 AMD。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.13,0:01:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We recognize this agentic era would require the highest performing GPUs and CPUs working together.\N我们意识到，这一代理时代需要性能最高的 GPU 和 CPU 协同工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.67,0:01:02.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're the only ones who build both.\N所以我们是唯一一家同时自研这两者的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.31,0:01:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's how agentic AI moves from answers to action.\N这正是代理型人工智能从给出答案到付诸行动的关键。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.55,0:01:09.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pushing inference compute to tremendous scale.\N将推理计算推向前所未有的规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:16.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like an agent that frees thousands of employees from smaller tasks to focus on bigger things.\N就像一个代理，让成千上万的员工从琐碎任务中解放出来，专注于更重要的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.21,0:01:22.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,A car that safely handles a new city like a local on its first day there.\N一辆汽车，能在第一天就如本地人般安全地应对陌生城市。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.49,0:01:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And an agent that pinpoints a disease in millions of cells, then designs a cure.\N还有一个代理，能在数百万个细胞中精准定位疾病，然后设计出疗法。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.13,0:01:39.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've built more AI computing power into a single data center than existed on Earth a decade ago.\N我们在一个数据中心内构建的 AI 计算能力，超过了十年前地球上所有计算能力的总和。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.47,0:01:43.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, we're giving you the tools.\N现在，我们为您提供工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.03,0:01:47.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,So together, we advance AI.\N让我们一起推动人工智能的发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.00,0:02:08.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good morning!\N早上好！
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.94,0:02:11.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's a pretty good good morning.\N这真是个不错的早上。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.46,0:02:13.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good morning!\N早上好！
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.82,0:02:15.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good morning!\N早上好！
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.94,0:02:18.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And welcome to Advancing AI 2026.\N欢迎参加“推动人工智能 2026”大会。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.20,0:02:24.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's so great to be back here in San Francisco and to see so many friends and partners and customers.\N很高兴再次回到旧金山，见到这么多朋友、合作伙伴和客户。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.34,0:02:28.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And especially all the developers that are here with us today.\N尤其欢迎今天在场的所有开发者。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.34,0:02:33.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I want to say a big welcome to everyone who's joining us online from around the world.\N我要向全球各地在线加入我们的所有人表示热烈欢迎。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.62,0:02:37.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is my absolute favorite event of the year.\N这是我一年中最喜欢的活动。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.18,0:02:43.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's where we bring the entire AI ecosystem together to show what we've been building.\N这里汇聚了整个 AI 生态系统，展示我们所打造的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.28,0:02:44.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And where we're going next.\N以及我们接下来要去的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.24,0:02:47.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this year, this is our biggest show ever.\N今年，这是我们规模最大的一次展会。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.72,0:02:49.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we have so much to tell you.\N因为我们有太多内容要告诉你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.44,0:02:51.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's go ahead and get started.\N那么，让我们开始吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.72,0:03:01.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,At AMD, our mission is to push the boundaries of high performance in AI computing to help solve the world's most important challenges.\N在 AMD，我们的使命是推动人工智能计算高性能的边界，以帮助解决世界上最紧迫的挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.10,0:03:07.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I often say, AI is the most important technology of the last 50 years.\N我经常说，人工智能是过去50年里最重要的技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.04,0:03:12.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And frankly, the progress that we're seeing in the industry is just incredible.\N说实话，我们看到的行业进展简直令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.18,0:03:18.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, every month, every few months, we see something new that was far beyond our imagination.\N每个月，甚至每过几个月，我们都会看到一些远超我们想象的新突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.82,0:03:22.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can already see the impact across every industry.\N你已经可以看到它对每个行业产生的影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.00,0:03:27.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,In healthcare, AI is helping researchers identify new drug candidates faster.\N在医疗健康领域，人工智能正在帮助研究人员更快地发现新的药物候选。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.00,0:03:32.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,In science, we're solving problems that we didn't think were possible a few years ago.\N在科学领域，我们正在解决几年前还觉得不可能的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.52,0:03:37.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And across every industry, AI is changing the way we get work done.\N在每个行业，人工智能正在改变我们完成工作的模式。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.36,0:03:44.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the most important thing is we're still in the very, very early innings of what's possible.\N最重要的是，我们仍处于可能性的非常非常早期阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.30,0:03:48.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, just take a look at some of these charts.\N现在，请看一下这些图表。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.46,0:03:49.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we look at these every year.\N我们每年都看这些数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.10,0:03:53.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you kind of see the rate and pace of AI growth.\N你就能看出人工智能增长的速度和节奏。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.80,0:03:56.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,A couple of years ago, we were just starting.\N几年前，我们才刚刚起步。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.06,0:03:58.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,People were experimenting with chatbots.\N人们还在尝试聊天机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.32,0:04:00.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, it was really cool.\N那时候真的很酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.64,0:04:08.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you look at today, we're really seeing more than 35 quadrillion tokens consumed every single month.\N但如果你看看今天，我们每月消耗的词元已超过35千万亿。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.36,0:04:13.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's an increase of nearly 160 times in just two years.\N这仅仅两年间就增长了近160倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.20,0:04:17.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that curve is actually just getting steeper.\N而且这条曲线实际上正在变得越来越陡。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.14,0:04:18.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going to hear a lot about that today.\N今天你们会听到很多关于这一点的内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.84,0:04:22.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, just looking at, you know, where is all that demand?\N所以，简单来说，这些需求到底来自哪里？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.78,0:04:26.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, obviously, training remains incredibly important and foundational.\N我的意思是，显然，训练仍然极其重要且是基础性的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.32,0:04:36.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over the last four or five years, you know, we see the compute that's used for training advanced models continuing to increase by, let's call it, roughly 5x every year.\N在过去四五年里，我们看到用于训练先进模型的算力，每年大约增长5倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.72,0:04:38.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And those models are getting better.\N这些模型正在变得越来越好。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.26,0:04:39.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, we're all experiencing that.\N就像我们每个人都在亲身经历这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.62,0:04:40.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're seeing better reasoning.\N我们看到了更出色的推理能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.80,0:04:42.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're seeing new capabilities.\N我们看到了新的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.54,0:04:45.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're now seeing a growing number of specialized models.\N我们现在正看到越来越多的专用模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.88,0:04:50.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of the things that I really believe in is there is no one perfect model.\N我坚信的一点是，不存在一个完美的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.50,0:04:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we're all going to use a slew of different models, depending on what task you're trying to solve and which industry you're in.\N我认为我们都会根据要解决的任务和所在行业，使用大量不同的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.80,0:05:01.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the bigger shift is actually in inference.\N但更大的转变实际上发生在推理阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.24,0:05:03.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we expected this.\N我们早就预料到了这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.48,0:05:06.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,We expected that inference would grow faster than training.\N我们早就预料到推理的增长速度会超过训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.04,0:05:15.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we can say that in 2026, for the first time, the world is using more AI compute to run models than to train them.\N到2026年，全球用于运行模型的AI算力将首次超过用于训练模型的算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.20,0:05:24.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've seen that to a point where we think this year, roughly 60% of the global AI compute capacity will be used for inference.\N我们已经看到这一趋势，预计今年全球约60%的AI算力将用于推理。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.00,0:05:27.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is actually pretty simple.\N造成这一现象的原因其实相当简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.00,0:05:35.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,As billions of people every day use AI, the workload shifts from building models to putting them to work.\N随着数十亿人每天使用AI，工作负载正从构建模型转向让模型投入实际应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.02,0:05:42.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And actually, we're going to talk a lot today about agentic AI, and that's accelerating the shift even faster.\N事实上，今天我们将会大量讨论代理型AI，这正在加速这一转变。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.38,0:05:49.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you think about all of this, we see agents as the next big step for AI.\N因此，如果我们思考这一切，我们认为代理是AI发展的下一步重大飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.76,0:05:57.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the most interesting thing is this has really just started accelerating over the last, I would say, five or six months this year.\N最有趣的是，这种加速趋势实际上才刚刚开始，大概从今年五到六个月前才真正显现。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.96,0:06:01.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when we started with LLMs, they were great to answer questions.\N当我们最初开发大语言模型时，它们主要用于回答问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.80,0:06:10.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we found that to really get the power of AI, you want agents to be able to really answer full questions.\N但后来我们发现，要真正发挥AI的潜力，需要让代理能够完整地回答复杂问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.10,0:06:14.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you give it a goal, it keeps working until it's solved the problem.\N你只需设定一个目标，它就会持续工作，直到问题被解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.42,0:06:23.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what that means for us in the compute industry, it means that compute demand is growing at an incredible pace.\N这对算力行业意味着，算力需求正以惊人的速度增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.86,0:06:27.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're actually seeing a step change in compute demand.\N我们实际上正在见证算力需求的一次质的飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.84,0:06:33.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because when you ask the agent to do something, it actually has dozens of steps.\N因为当你让代理执行某项任务时，它实际上需要完成数十个步骤。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.26,0:06:37.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it has to reason, and it has to call tools, and it has to access data.\N它必须进行推理，调用工具，并访问数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.10,0:06:40.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it has to keep doing it over and over until it's solved the problem.\N它必须反复执行这些操作，直到问题得到解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.98,0:06:43.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you need lots of GPUs to do all that reasoning.\N因此你需要大量GPU来完成所有这些推理任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.60,0:06:49.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,But importantly, you also need a lot of CPUs to orchestrate every step around it.\N但更重要的是，你还需要大量CPU来协调每一个步骤。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.96,0:06:57.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you look at just what that means from a market standpoint, it's really hard to put this market data up.\N所以当你从市场角度看待这一点时，很难将这些市场数据呈现出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.80,0:07:03.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because I feel like every few months, we're changing the perspective based on what our customers are saying.\N因为我觉得每隔几个月，我们都会根据客户反馈改变视角。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.88,0:07:11.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,But what we're seeing is that the shift to agentic AI is certainly growing the AI accelerator market very significantly.\N但我们看到的是，向代理式AI的转变确实显著推动了AI加速器市场的增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.12,0:07:20.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was actually last year at this event that we called the AI accelerator market at about 500 billion by 2028.\N其实去年在本次活动中，我们就预测AI加速器市场将在2028年达到约5000亿。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.06,0:07:24.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at that time, it actually felt like a very big number.\N当时这个数字看起来非常庞大。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.44,0:07:27.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Didn't you think it was a big number?\N你不觉得这个数字很大吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.06,0:07:31.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,But honestly, you look at it today, and it looks conservative.\N但说实话，现在再看，这个预测显得有些保守了。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.80,0:07:35.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because the AI demand is just continuing to accelerate.\N因为AI需求仍在持续加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.46,0:07:37.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can see it, right?\N你能看出来，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.42,0:07:41.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Better models, more usage, more usage requires more compute.\N更好的模型，更多的使用，更多的使用需要更多的算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.62,0:07:44.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And more compute actually builds better models.\N更多的计算能力实际上能构建出更好的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.78,0:07:53.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're now expecting that by 2030, the AI accelerator market is going to reach about 1.4 trillion by 2030.\N因此我们预计到2030年，AI加速器市场规模将达到约1.4万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.82,0:07:54.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what do you think about that?\N你觉得怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.82,0:07:55.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is that a big number?\N那是很大的数字吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.38,0:08:09.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, what that means is by the end of the decade, the AI accelerator market is going to approach the size of the entire semiconductor market today.\N我的意思是，到本十年末，AI加速器市场的规模将接近当今整个半导体市场的规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.60,0:08:17.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And although there will be many different types of accelerators, you know, I'm a big believer in there's no one size fits all as it comes to chips.\N尽管会有各种不同类型的加速器，但我始终相信，芯片并不存在一种放之四海而皆准的通用方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.36,0:08:27.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do expect that GPUs are going to make up the vast majority of that market because the algorithms are still very much in their infancy, and we're still\N我们预计GPU将占据该市场绝大部分，因为相关算法仍处于非常初期的阶段，我们仍在
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.82,0:08:35.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,continuing to see the workloads change, and that favors programmability in the overall silicon ecosystem.\N持续看到工作负载的变化，这有利于整个硅基生态系统的可编程性。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.02,0:08:44.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, perhaps the most interesting part of the last six months has been, you know, GPUs are only part of this story.\N现在，过去六个月里最有趣的部分或许是，你知道的，GPU 只是这个故事的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.16,0:08:51.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we're actually seeing is agentic AI is creating an entirely new growth vector for server CPUs.\N我们实际上看到的是，代理型AI正在为服务器CPU创造一个全新的增长方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.24,0:08:57.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, I've updated this number a lot also over the last, you know, six to eight months.\N近六到八个月来，我也多次更新过这个数字。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.38,0:09:02.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,But look, we call it like we see it, and we were early.\N但我们要说的是我们看到的实际情况，而且我们很早就意识到了这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.64,0:09:12.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we saw from our largest hyperscale customers, and you're going to see some of them here today, who said, look, as AI inference is going up, we need more server CPUs.\N我们从最大的超大规模客户那里就看到了这一点，你们今天也会看到其中一些客户，他们说：随着AI推理需求上升，我们需要更多的服务器CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.72,0:09:17.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we saw growth in the server CPU market, and we said, you know,\N于是我们看到了服务器CPU市场的增长，于是我们说，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.60,0:09:24.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,last year we thought it might grow, let's call it 18 to 20% CAGR, to an overall market size of 60 billion.\N去年我们预计它可能以18%到20%的年复合增长率增长，市场规模达到600亿。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.76,0:09:31.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,But frankly, what we're seeing is that the rate and pace of agentic AI adoption is much, much faster than any of us thought.\N但坦率地说，我们看到的是，代理型AI的采用速度远比我们任何人预想的要快得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.62,0:09:44.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're talking about agents going from millions to billions, like we're able to increase all of our productivity, and that requires a tremendous amount of CPU infrastructure.\N所以我们现在看到的是，代理从数百万增长到数十亿，我们能够大幅提升所有生产力，而这需要庞大的CPU基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.02,0:09:49.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every customer conversation is telling us that this build-out is just beginning.\N每一次客户对话都在告诉我们，这场基础设施建设才刚刚开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.14,0:09:59.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So based on what we're seeing today, and we're going to talk more about how agentic AI is evolving with CPUs, we now expect the server CPU market to\N因此，基于我们今天所看到的情况，我们接下来会更多讨论代理型AI如何与CPU共同演进，我们现在预计服务器CPU市场将
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.06,0:10:03.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,grow by over 50% to over 200 billion by 2030.\N到2030年增长超过50%，达到2000亿以上。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.60,0:10:10.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's starting from today, a $25 billion market going to over 200 billion.\N也就是说，从现在的250亿市场，增长到超过2000亿。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.04,0:10:14.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there's a lot of excitement about CPUs as well.\N因此，人们对CPU也充满期待。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.02,0:10:25.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, probably one of the things that is differentiating AMD in how we think about the market is this is not just a data center opportunity.\N现在，可能有一件事让AMD在看待市场时与其他公司不同，那就是这不仅仅是一个数据中心的机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.18,0:10:34.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,As AI becomes a larger part of our daily lives, we want the intelligence to run right where the work happens.\N随着人工智能在我们日常生活中扮演越来越重要的角色，我们希望智能计算能就在工作发生的地方运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.82,0:10:40.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that means cloud is super important, but the devices that we use every day are going to be extremely important.\N这意味着云至关重要，但我们每天使用的设备也将变得极为重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.44,0:10:48.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that means that we're going to do a lot more at the edge as well with autonomous machines that sense and act in real time.\N这意味着我们还需要在边缘侧做更多事情，比如让能够实时感知和行动的自主机器发挥作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.88,0:10:52.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we really believe that you need AI to be infused everywhere.\N我们真正相信，人工智能必须无处不在。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.92,0:10:55.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what we're focused on at AMD.\N这正是AMD专注的方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.32,0:11:04.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So putting all of that together, we actually expect that the market for our high-performance and adaptive computing products to grow at roughly a 40% CAGR\N因此，综合来看，我们预计高性能和自适应计算产品市场在未来几年将以约40%的年复合增长率扩张。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.94,0:11:09.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,over the next several years, approaching a $2 trillion market by 2030.\N到2030年，市场规模将接近2万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.14,0:11:17.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And frankly, the only way you're going to be able to service a market like that is for us to work together as an ecosystem.\N诚实地讲，要服务这样一个市场，唯一的办法就是我们作为生态系统共同协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.32,0:11:25.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's no one company that can solve it all, but this is the opportunity to bring the best and brightest together.\N没有任何一家公司能独自解决所有问题，但这也是汇聚最优秀人才的绝佳机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.82,0:11:29.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have never been in a better position to lead.\N而我们从未处于如此有利的位置来引领这一进程。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.68,0:11:31.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have the broadest product portfolio.\N我们拥有最广泛的产品组合。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.90,0:11:34.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have the strongest roadmaps we've ever had.\N我们拥有有史以来最强劲的产品路线图。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.70,0:11:41.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the thing that I'm most proud of is we have the deepest partnerships with the companies that are building this future.\N我最自豪的是，我们与正在构建未来的公司建立了最深入的合作关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.76,0:11:45.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a little bit about our strategy.\N所以简单说一下我们的战略。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.26,0:11:47.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we've been very consistent.\N我认为我们一直非常一致。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.40,0:11:52.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've talked about our multi-year strategy, and it's really built around three priorities.\N我们一直在谈论多年度战略，它主要围绕三个重点展开。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.56,0:11:55.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first is just compute leadership.\N第一个是计算领导力。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.68,0:12:01.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're building the broadest set of compute engines in the industry so that we have the right compute for the right workload.\N我们正在打造业界最广泛的一系列计算引擎，以确保为各类工作负载提供合适的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.18,0:12:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Second, it's going to be about open platforms.\N第二个重点是开放平台。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.30,0:12:08.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want everyone to come together in an open ecosystem.\N我们希望所有人都能汇聚到一个开放的生态系统中。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.08,0:12:16.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We believe an open ecosystem is essential to the future of AI, and that's how we get the force multiplier of everyone coming together.\N我们相信，开放生态系统对人工智能的未来至关重要，这正是让所有人协同发力的关键。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.32,0:12:22.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's open on hardware, in terms of hardware standards, as well as open on software.\N这种开放既体现在硬件标准上，也体现在软件层面。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.94,0:12:26.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why we're investing so heavily in our ROCm software.\N这就是我们为何在ROCm软件上投入如此巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.62,0:12:35.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you're going to see that AI has been a tremendous multiplier in this great pace of progress that we're making in ROCm and in software.\N你会看到，人工智能极大地加速了我们在ROCm和软件领域取得的进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.12,0:12:45.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it really means that if we put all of this together, we can have our customers deploy on AMD hardware faster than ever.\N这意味着，如果我们把所有这些整合起来，客户就能比以往更快地在AMD硬件上部署应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.56,0:12:51.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the third piece is we're going to get a chance to talk to you about powering AI everywhere.\N第三部分，我们将有机会与你们探讨如何让人工智能无处不在。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.38,0:12:53.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's AI in enterprise.\N这是企业级的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.80,0:12:55.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's AI at the PC.\N这是个人电脑上的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.48,0:12:57.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's AI in the physical world.\N这是物理世界中的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.96,0:13:01.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's adding new capabilities across all of our products.\N这将为我们的所有产品带来全新的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.18,0:13:03.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,So today you're going to see all of that in action.\N所以今天你们将亲眼看到这一切的实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.12,0:13:06.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to start with compute for the agentic era.\N我们将从智能体时代的计算开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.10,0:13:08.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to show you a lot of hardware.\N我将向你们展示大量硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.50,0:13:15.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we're going to talk about some software and then our overall products from a platform standpoint.\N然后我们将讨论一些软件，以及从平台角度出发的我们整体产品。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.62,0:13:22.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're honored to have some really special guests who are going to join us to really help bring the technology to life.\N我们非常荣幸能有几位特别嘉宾加入我们，帮助真正让这项技术生动呈现。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.00,0:13:24.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's start with the data center.\N那么，让我们从数据中心开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.30,0:13:29.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, AMD EPYC runs on the most important workloads in the world.\N如今，AMD EPYC 正运行在全球最重要的工作负载上。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.34,0:13:32.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,We power the largest cloud providers.\N我们为最大的云服务提供商提供动力。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.48,0:13:40.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,We power the digital platforms that billions of people use every day and the most important critical systems that are used by the largest businesses,\N我们为数十亿人每天使用的数字平台，以及大型企业所依赖的最重要关键系统提供支持，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.62,0:13:45.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,including more than 60% of the Fortune 100 are using AMD EPYC.\N包括超过 60% 的财富 100 强企业正在使用 AMD EPYC。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.74,0:13:47.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that momentum is just building.\N这股势头正在不断增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.62,0:13:59.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Last quarter, we reached a record 46% revenue share in the server market and we're continuing to see every major customer move more workloads to EPYC.\N上个季度，我们在服务器市场的收入份额达到创纪录的 46%，并且我们持续看到所有主要客户将更多工作负载迁移到 EPYC。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.72,0:14:05.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And on the GPU side, our Instinct adoption has also accelerated.\N在 GPU 方面，我们的 Instinct 采用速度也显著加快。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.08,0:14:11.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a broad set of customers across the largest AI labs, cloud providers,\N我们在最大的 AI 实验室、云服务提供商、
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.84,0:14:19.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,leading AI startups, as well as some of the national labs and sovereign AI opportunities are being built on AMD Instinct.\N领先的 AI 初创公司，以及一些国家实验室和主权 AI 项目中，都有广泛客户在使用 AMD Instinct。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.92,0:14:22.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we really appreciate that opportunity.\N我们非常珍惜这一机遇。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.74,0:14:27.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, AI computes become a lot more complicated.\N现在，人工智能计算变得复杂得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.06,0:14:35.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we're seeing with Frontier AI is it's really raising the bar for what infrastructure needs to do.\N我们在前沿人工智能中看到的情况是，它真正提高了基础设施所需达到的标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.04,0:14:39.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,It takes more than a single chip or a single server.\N单一芯片或单台服务器已经不够了。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.98,0:14:44.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,You actually have to design the entire rack as one system.\N你实际上必须将整个机架设计为一个系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.96,0:14:55.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that requires leading CPUs, that requires leading GPUs, that requires high-speed networking that connects everything inside the rack and across the data center.\N这需要顶级的CPU，需要顶级的GPU，还需要高速网络，以连接机架内部以及数据中心之间的所有组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.78,0:15:00.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just as importantly, this is about making these systems super easy to use.\N同样重要的是，这些系统必须非常易于使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.28,0:15:05.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so they need to be easy to deploy, easy to service, and very reliable.\N因此，它们需要易于部署、易于维护，并且非常可靠。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.22,0:15:09.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that is exactly what we built with Helios.\N这正是我们为Helios所打造的。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.76,0:15:17.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So today, I'm super excited to launch Helios, the industry's highest performance AI rack.\N所以今天，我非常激动地推出Helios，这是业界性能最高的AI机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.92,0:15:28.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, Helios is built to train and run the most demanding Frontier models in the world at massive scale.\N现在，Helios专为在大规模下训练和运行全球最苛刻的前沿模型而打造。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.48,0:15:31.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I have a lot of show and tell for you.\N我有很多展示和演示要和大家分享。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.32,0:15:36.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for those of you who know me, you know that I love holding up chips.\N所以，对于了解我的人来说，你们知道我特别喜欢举起芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.22,0:15:41.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,I call myself sometimes the Vanna White of chips.\N有时候我自称为芯片界的维娜·怀特。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.32,0:15:46.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it turns out with Helios, there are lots and lots of components.\N但事实上，Helios包含了大量的组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.94,0:15:50.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you can see, these are the chips inside the Helios rack.\N你可以看到，这些是Helios机架内的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.68,0:15:53.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are the Instinct...\N这些是Instinct...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.78,0:15:55.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.84,0:16:06.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is Instinct, EPYC, and then the Pensando chips for networking that are inside each rack.\N这是Instinct、EPYC，以及每个机架内用于网络的Pensando芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.62,0:16:09.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every one of these chips is part of the system.\N每一颗芯片都是系统的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.60,0:16:12.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So MI455 is the engine.\N所以MI455是核心引擎。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.06,0:16:15.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the highest performance GPU in the industry.\N它是业界性能最高的GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.48,0:16:21.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Venice, which drives it, is the world's fastest CPU cores.\N驱动它的Venice，是世界上最快的CPU核心。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.04,0:16:29.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Pensando DPUs and NICs actually connect them with leadership programmability and scale-out bandwidth.\N而Pensando的DPUs和NICs实际上以领先的可编程性和扩展带宽将它们连接起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.62,0:16:33.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I have a few more props to show you.\N所以我还有几个道具要展示给你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.12,0:16:37.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's kind of take a look at how these things fit into the overall system.\N我们来大致看一下这些组件如何融入整个系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.36,0:16:48.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So first, this is now the MI455 accelerator, which is mounted on what we call an Enhanced Accelerator Module, or EAM.\N这是现在的MI455加速器，安装在我们称之为增强型加速器模块（EAM）的载体上。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.10,0:16:54.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a production module that goes into Helios, and it is much more than the GPU package.\N这是一个用于Helios的生产模块，远不止是一个GPU封装。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.28,0:17:05.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,The EAM actually integrates the GPU, memory, power delivery, high-speed interfaces, system management, cold plates for liquid cooling,\NEAM实际上集成了GPU、内存、供电系统、高速接口、系统管理以及液冷用的冷板，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.92,0:17:09.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,all into one compact, serviceable module.\N所有这些都整合在一个紧凑且可维护的模块中。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.08,0:17:11.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pretty cool, right?\N非常酷，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.64,0:17:23.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, if I just give you some of the specs, we're talking about 320 billion transistors.\N如果我只给你们一些规格参数，这颗芯片拥有3200亿个晶体管。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.48,0:17:28.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is built with TSMC's leading 2-nanometer and 3-nanometer process technology.\N它采用台积电领先的2纳米和3纳米制程技术制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.50,0:17:34.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And most importantly, it brings together nearly a decade of AMD chiplet innovation.\N最重要的是，它汇集了AMD近十年的芯片小片（chiplet）创新成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.34,0:17:38.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it allows us to combine 12 compute and I/O.\N因此我们可以将12个计算和I/O芯片小片与432GB的内存结合在一起，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.06,0:17:45.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,chiplets with 432 gigabytes of memory, all connected by leading industry 3D chip stack packaging.\N所有部件通过业界领先的3D芯片堆叠封装技术连接。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.26,0:17:51.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I can say for sure, it's the highest performance AI accelerator in the industry.\N我可以肯定地说，这是目前行业内性能最高的AI加速器。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.36,0:18:02.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so this is the CPU board that's inside the Helios compute tray.\N好的，这是位于 Helios 计算托盘内部的 CPU 板。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.34,0:18:04.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm going to talk a lot about CPUs later.\N我稍后会详细讨论 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.86,0:18:11.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,But just to give you a high-level view, it's high-speed, 96-core EPYC processor,\N但先给大家一个整体概览：这是一颗高速的 96 核 EPYC 处理器，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.70,0:18:17.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,DDR5 memory, all the I/O that's needed to feed the GPUs, all in a single motherboard.\NDDR5 内存，以及为 GPU 供电所需的所有 I/O 接口，全部集成在一块主板上。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.66,0:18:20.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we also have our Salina DPU.\N我们还有自己的 Salina DPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.98,0:18:32.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a critical part of the networking infrastructure, and it really allows us to deliver both front-end as well as the scale-out and scale-across bandwidth overall.\N这是网络基础设施的关键部分，真正让我们能够实现前端以及横向扩展和跨域扩展的整体带宽。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.08,0:18:35.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is our Vulcano AI NIC.\N这是我们推出的 Vulcano AI 网络接口卡。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.72,0:18:42.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can see this actually allows us to really have up to six Vulcano NICs on a board.\N你可以看到，这实际上允许我们在一块板上部署多达六块 Vulcano 网卡。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.54,0:18:45.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it uses the open ultra Ethernet standard.\N它采用开放的超以太网标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.54,0:18:55.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So each Helios compute tray includes two of these Vulcano boards, and that allows us to have the scale-out and the scale-up networking overall.\N每个 Helios 计算托盘包含两块这样的 Vulcano 板，从而实现横向扩展和纵向扩展的网络连接。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.20,0:19:04.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you put all that inside the rack, and we have an additional six dedicated networking trays that handle the scale-up networking.\N你把这些全部放进机架后，我们还额外配备了六个专用网络托盘，用于处理纵向扩展网络。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.58,0:19:11.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And those are all connecting 75 GPUs together with UA-Link over Ethernet with silicon from our partners.\N这些托盘通过合作伙伴的硅芯片，利用 UA-Link 通过以太网将 75 块 GPU 连接在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.86,0:19:14.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's what we mean by an open ecosystem.\N这就是我们所说的开放生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.00,0:19:21.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you bring this all together, I want to say Helios is simply the best AI rack in the world.\N所以当你们把这一切结合起来时，我想说，Helios 是世界上最好的 AI 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.11,0:19:31.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, let's take a look at some numbers.\N现在，让我们来看一些数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.11,0:19:34.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Clearly, it's a very competitive world out there.\N显然，这是一个非常具有竞争力的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.89,0:19:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you compare Helios to the competition, we're delivering 15% more compute, 50% more HBM4 memory capacity and memory bandwidth, and 50% more scale-out bandwidth.\N因此，当我们将 Helios 与竞争对手对比时，我们提供的计算能力多出 15%，HBM4 内存容量和内存带宽多出 50%，扩展带宽也多出 50%。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.25,0:20:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what that means is that every Helios can deliver more performance for the largest models, more capacity for longer context, and the bandwidth to scale across thousands of racks.\N意味着每个 Helios 都能为最大模型提供更高的性能，为更长上下文提供更大的容量，并具备跨数千个机架扩展所需的带宽。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.77,0:20:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now we can kind of come over here and take a look at another very large piece of hardware.\N现在我们可以过来看一下另一件非常大型的硬件设备。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.21,0:20:15.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is now the production hardware that customers are deploying, and you can see more of that as you go through the exhibit center.\N这是客户现在正在部署的生产级硬件，你们在参观展览中心时可以看到更多。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.85,0:20:22.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And each one of these weighs more than 160 pounds and stands less than two inches tall.\N每个设备重量超过 160 磅，高度不到两英寸。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.01,0:20:28.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's just an extraordinary amount of technology when you look at what's in one of these trays.\N当你看到其中一个托盘里的技术含量时，这简直令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.07,0:20:32.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you bring these things together, the numbers are just incredible.\N当把这些东西组合在一起时，数据简直惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.27,0:20:41.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,More than 18,000 CDNA5 GPU compute units, over 4,600 Zen6 CPU cores, and 31\N超过 18,000 个 CDNA5 GPU 计算单元，超过 4,600 个 Zen6 CPU 核心，以及 31
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.67,0:20:45.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,terabytes of HBM4 memory, all in a single rack.\N单个机架内配备海量HBM4内存。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.31,0:20:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what it takes to run agentic AI at scale.\N这就是实现规模化代理AI运行所需的条件。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.59,0:20:56.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So today I'm excited to announce that Helios is in full production.\N因此今天我很激动地宣布，Helios已全面投入生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.00,0:21:11.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have shipments on track to start at the end of the third quarter and ramping into the fourth quarter in the second half of the year.\N我们的出货计划正按预期进行，将于第三季度末开始，并在下半年第四季度逐步提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.54,0:21:15.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I can tell you customer demand for Helios is extremely strong.\N我可以告诉你们，客户对Helios的需求非常强烈。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.92,0:21:21.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're extremely proud of the work that we have done across the leading AI labs to adopt Helios.\N我们非常自豪，能在领先的AI实验室中推动Helios的采用。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.24,0:21:24.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so let's start with some of our guests.\N那么，让我们先从一些嘉宾开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.60,0:21:30.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today I'm excited to be joined by our newest Instinct partner and one of the leaders in Frontier AI.\N今天我很激动地欢迎我们最新的Instinct合作伙伴，同时也是前沿AI领域的领军者。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.90,0:21:37.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,To share more about what we're doing together, please welcome Anthropic co-founder and chief compute officer Tom Brown.\N为了更多了解我们合作的进展，请欢迎Anthropic联合创始人兼首席计算官汤姆·布朗。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.05,0:21:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello, Tom.\N你好，汤姆。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.07,0:21:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is so great to have you here.\N你来到这里真是太好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.81,0:21:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it is really such an honor to be working with Anthropic.\N与Anthropic合作真是莫大的荣幸。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.61,0:21:56.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had a big week this week.\N本周我们度过了一个非常充实的一周。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.59,0:21:57.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did, yeah.\N是的，确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.73,0:22:02.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So look, Anthropic has just had incredible success over the last few years.\N所以你看，近年来，Anthropic 取得了非凡的成功。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.31,0:22:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, Claude has made such a big impact on the overall industry.\N你知道，Claude 对整个行业产生了巨大的影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.07,0:22:10.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compute is such an important factor in the progress.\N计算能力是推动进步的关键因素。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.41,0:22:15.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you just talk a little bit about your compute strategy and just how things have been evolving?\N你能简单谈一下你们的计算策略，以及这些年来的发展情况吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.97,0:22:16.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Yeah.\N嗯，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.45,0:22:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And first, thank you so much.\N首先，非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.85,0:22:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,A hard act to follow with Helios.\N要接替 Helios 的表现可真不容易。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.39,0:22:19.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Amazing.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.59,0:22:31.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,So with Anthropic, as you mentioned, the scale that we're growing just as an industry is enormous.\N就 Anthropic 而言，正如你提到的，我们整个行业正在以惊人的规模增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.61,0:22:42.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we have been working to make sure that we have the best, like different chips, and we can use the best chips for the best workloads.\N因此，我们一直在努力确保拥有最佳的各类芯片，并能为最佳的工作负载选用最合适的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.81,0:22:46.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah. And look, I think you've been really leading in that area.\N是的。而且说实话，我觉得你在这一领域一直走在前列。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.55,0:22:52.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, I'm happy to say that I've always wanted to be as part of your infrastructure.\N而且你知道，我很高兴能说，我一直希望成为你们基础设施的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.37,0:22:55.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I remember the early times we talked as you were starting Anthropic.\N我记得我们早期交谈的时候，你正开始创办 Anthropic。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.53,0:22:57.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we had a big announcement this week.\N但本周我们有一个重大宣布。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.27,0:23:00.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're honored that you will be deploying up to 2 gigawatts of Helios.\N我们非常荣幸，你们将部署高达2吉瓦的 Helios。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.29,0:23:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why now?\N为什么是现在？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.39,0:23:03.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,What was the key reason?\N关键原因是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.63,0:23:10.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah. So I think that the first thing was just Helios is an amazing machine.\N是的。我认为首先，Helios 是一台了不起的机器。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.89,0:23:13.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's absolutely fantastic.\N简直太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.71,0:23:14.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do we like that?\N我们喜欢这个吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.79,0:23:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Does that work for us?\N这对我们管用吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.11,0:23:26.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then I think the thing that we were thinking about originally was whenever we're bringing up a new hardware platform, it's a big effort.\N然后我想，我们最初考虑的是，每当我们要启动一个新硬件平台时，都是一个巨大的工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.03,0:23:28.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like a huge thing.\N就像一件巨大的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.45,0:23:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so as part of the...\N所以作为其中的一部分……
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.25,0:23:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,as we were thinking about this, we started doing our own evaluation of MI355.\N当我们思考这个问题时，我们开始对MI355进行自己的评估。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.35,0:23:39.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You guys generously got us a rack to start working.\N你们慷慨地给了我们一个机架来开始工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.35,0:23:43.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we expected this to be kind of a big process.\N我们原本预计这会是一个相当大的过程。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.21,0:23:48.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our actual experience was we had one engineer start doing it.\N我们的真实体验是，只有一位工程师开始操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.01,0:23:56.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,They spun up... they connected it to Claude, asked him, hey, bring up this machine, left it going over the weekend.\N他们启动了……连接到Claude，问他，嘿，把这台机器启动起来，然后让它运行整个周末。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.37,0:24:04.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we ended up with a graph of the actual performance of our leading model on it just going up and up and up over the weekend.\N我们最终得到了一张图，显示我们领先模型在上面的实际性能，整个周末持续上升。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.05,0:24:05.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, yeah.\N所以，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.71,0:24:19.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that that's a testament to the open platform that you guys have made where anyone like human or AI can now build real models on your platform.\N我认为这证明了你们打造的开放平台，现在任何人，无论是人类还是AI，都可以在你们的平台上构建真实模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.47,0:24:21.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tom, I kid you not.\N汤姆，我可没开玩笑。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.65,0:24:28.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,When my team told me that you had an engineer working on MI355, I said, hey, are we making sure we help them?\N当我的团队告诉我你们有工程师在开发MI355时，我说，嘿，我们得确保在帮他们。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.27,0:24:31.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they're like, they say they don't need any help.\N他们说他们不需要任何帮助。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.51,0:24:32.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,They got it all covered.\N他们自己都能搞定。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.77,0:24:35.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I was like, hey, that's a wonderful story.\N我当时就想，嘿，这真是个精彩的故事。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.95,0:24:36.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for that.\N谢谢你分享。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.05,0:24:46.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we're also super excited about the work we're doing together because one of the most valuable parts of this partnership is Claude and using Claude within AMD.\N现在，我们对双方合作的工作也感到非常兴奋，因为这项合作最有价值的部分之一就是使用 Claude，以及在 AMD 内部集成 Claude。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.31,0:24:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're big believers in the fact that AI is this force multiplier and the more we're able to have the leading foundational models really familiar with the AMD\N我们坚信 AI 是一种强大的倍增器，我们越能让领先的基础模型充分熟悉 AMD 的架构，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.11,0:24:59.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,architecture, the better we're going to be able to service the overall market.\N我们就越能更好地服务整个市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.75,0:25:07.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you just talk a little bit about how you're seeing Claude really evolve in these types of highly engineering-specific workloads?\N所以你能简单说说你如何看待 Claude 在这类高度工程化工作负载中的发展吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.53,0:25:15.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so I think this is a great place for collaboration where the bread and butter of Claude is doing software engineering.\N是的，我认为这是合作的绝佳切入点，因为 Claude 的核心优势在于软件工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.33,0:25:27.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now more and more we're seeing it help out with the type of workloads that you guys are doing also, like design, layout, which is not quite the normal software engineering, but is adjacent.\N现在我们越来越多地看到它在你们正在做的工作类型中发挥作用，比如设计和布局，这虽然不是典型的软件工程，但密切相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.47,0:25:34.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I do think that that is the place where we can work together to make the next generation of chips even better.\N我认为这正是我们能够携手合作，让下一代芯片变得更出色的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.81,0:25:43.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think, and also on the software side, I think the work that we've seen with Claude and the kernel development has been just incredible.\N是的，我认为在软件层面也是如此，我们看到 Claude 在内核开发方面的成果简直令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.47,0:25:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Tom, one of the things for our audience here, we like to talk about the present, but it's actually most of us are working on the future.\N所以，汤姆，对我们现场的观众来说，我们喜欢谈论当下，但实际上我们大多数人都在为未来工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.09,0:25:58.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is really the beginning of what we believe is a very strong multi-year partnership.\N所以这确实是我们相信的一段非常稳固的多年合作的开端。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.67,0:26:03.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you talk a little bit about, number one, what are you most excited about in the industry?\N你能谈谈，第一，你对行业最兴奋的是什么吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.97,0:26:13.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then number two, like, what can we do more together to really make sure that we're satisfying those key opportunities?\N然后第二，我们还能如何进一步合作，以确保真正把握住这些关键机遇？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.95,0:26:15.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's a great question.\N是的，这是个很好的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.89,0:26:27.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think the working together for the scale-up seems like it's probably the biggest thing that I'm most excited for, where it does seem like we see\N我认为，最让我兴奋的是，我们共同推动规模扩张，这似乎是最关键的一点，因为我们可以持续看到
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.45,0:26:36.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,consistently using more better compute results in better models that then add more value to all the folks using it downstream.\N更多、更好的计算带来更优的模型，进而为所有下游使用者创造更多价值。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.05,0:26:38.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think that's the biggest thing.\N所以我认为这是最重要的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.75,0:26:42.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then I think one thing now that we're investing more and more with you guys,\N然后我认为，现在我们正越来越多地与你们合作，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.01,0:26:53.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,too, and I think we can continue to, is security, where that's a place where now, as the machines are getting more complex, we can work together to secure\N同样，我们也可以继续加强的是安全领域，因为随着机器变得越来越复杂，我们可以在芯片层、服务器层、机架层、整个网络层面
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.09,0:27:01.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,things at the chip layer, the server level, the rack, the whole network, and that'll help out, like, not just us, but the entire industry stay safe.\N通力合作，确保安全，这不仅对我们有利，也能让整个行业保持安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.73,0:27:03.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I think you're completely right.\N不，我认为你说得完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.45,0:27:14.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are super focused on the idea of, you know, how can we use AI to improve every aspect of our product, whether it's performance, power, software, and security, as you said.\N我们非常专注于如何利用人工智能提升我们产品的各个方面，无论是性能、功耗、软件还是安全，正如你所说。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.77,0:27:21.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So really, Tom, huge thank you for the opportunity to work very closely with you and your team.\N所以，汤姆，非常感谢你给予我们与你们团队紧密合作的机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.97,0:27:26.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our team loves working with you guys, and we look forward to everything that we're going to do together.\N我们的团队非常喜欢与你们合作，也期待我们接下来共同完成的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.65,0:27:27.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.\N非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.59,0:27:29.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.13,0:27:46.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alright, so look, Tom talked about how important performance is, and we have been laser focused on ensuring that the real-world performance of MI455 and Helios\N好的，汤姆提到了性能的重要性，我们一直专注于确保 MI455 和 Helios 在实际系统表现上真正达到预期。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.93,0:27:51.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,really comes true when we look at, you know, system results.\N当我们查看系统实际结果时，这一点尤为明显。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.57,0:27:53.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's take a look at some of those results.\N那么，让我们来看一些具体结果。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.09,0:27:56.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So here's an example.\N这是一个例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.59,0:28:04.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're running DeepSeek V4 Flash, one of the latest reasoning models, and we are actually comparing MI455 to MI355.\N我们正在运行 DeepSeek V4 Flash，这是最新的一款推理模型，我们实际上是在将 MI455 与 MI355 进行对比。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.15,0:28:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, the key thing is with every generation, we want to make huge leaps in performance.\N重要的是，每一代我们都希望在性能上实现巨大飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.49,0:28:17.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're seeing that at lower concurrency that MI455 delivers 4x the throughput of MI355.\N因此我们看到，在较低并发情况下，MI455 的吞吐量是 MI355 的 4 倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.15,0:28:23.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,But clearly what you see with, you know, large users across the board,\N但显然，从各个领域的大型用户来看，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.95,0:28:29.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,that you want to increase the number of simultaneous users, you want to increase the amount of work that you can do at the same time.\N你们希望增加同时在线的用户数量，希望在同一时间处理更多的工作量。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.73,0:28:37.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so at the highest concurrency, we're seeing Helios deliver up to 34x more throughput than our prior generation.\N因此在最高并发情况下，我们看到 Helios 的吞吐量比上一代产品最高提升了 34 倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.63,0:28:45.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what that means is more users, much faster response, and much better efficiency at scale.\N这意味着更多用户、更快的响应速度，以及在大规模应用下的更高效率。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.45,0:28:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And performance is just one aspect of it, right?\N性能只是其中一个方面，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.95,0:28:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other aspect and, you know, what I should have mentioned when Tom was on stage is every one of us in the enterprise is seeing our AI budgets go up every single month.\N另一个方面，也是我刚才在汤姆上台时本该提到的，我们企业中的每个人都在看到每月 AI 预算都在增加。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.73,0:28:58.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is that right?\N是这样吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.59,0:28:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you seeing some of that?\N你们有看到这种情况吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.37,0:29:04.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so customers really care about cost per token.\N因此客户非常关注每个词元的成本。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.79,0:29:08.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with every generation of Instinct, we're driving the cost per token down.\N每一代 Instinct，我们都在降低每个词元的成本。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.35,0:29:13.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's with more memory, more bandwidth, and much more compute.\N而且这是在拥有更多内存、更高带宽以及更强计算能力的前提下实现的。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.67,0:29:25.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're taking another major step with MI455, delivering up to 18x more tokens per dollar, so customers can serve far more users with the same investment.\N我们在 MI455 上又迈出了一大步，每美元可处理的词元数量最多提升 18 倍，因此客户可以用相同的投入服务更多用户。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.25,0:29:33.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as you think about how that comes together in a rack, many of our data centers right now are really limited by power.\N当你考虑这些组件如何整合到一个机架中时，我们目前许多数据中心的瓶颈主要在于供电能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.05,0:29:36.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So power is kind of the maximum limiter.\N因此，供电能力基本上是最大的限制因素。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.83,0:29:44.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we tested Helios over a full range of workloads where you have a fixed rack power compared to the competition.\N我们在各种工作负载下对 Helios 进行了测试，与竞争对手相比，机架的供电功率是固定的。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.79,0:29:52.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we're seeing is across the highest throughput workloads, the most interactive applications, all of these leading inference workloads, we're seeing\N我们观察到，在最高吞吐量的工作负载、最互动的应用程序以及所有领先的推理工作负载中，
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.89,0:29:57.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Helios an average of 10-15% more performance than the competition.\NHelios 的平均性能比竞争对手高出 10% 到 15%。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.37,0:30:03.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that comes with all of the system work that we've done in the overall system.\N这得益于我们在整个系统上所做的大量系统级优化工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.27,0:30:07.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how that translates to a customer is cost.\N这对客户而言，体现为成本优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.23,0:30:18.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we expect is the Helios rack delivers more performance, and it also delivers up to 30% more tokens per dollar than the competition.\N我们预计，Helios 机架不仅性能更高，而且每美元可处理的词元数量比竞争对手最多高出 30%。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.33,0:30:22.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think that's a pretty good overall value proposition.\N所以我认为这是一个相当不错的整体价值主张。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.36,0:30:34.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, I'm happy to say that the customer demand for Helios is extremely strong.\N现在我很高兴地告诉大家，客户对 Helios 的需求非常强烈。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.00,0:30:45.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,From the largest AI labs to hyperscale and NeoCloud providers, we are working across the entire ecosystem to enable Helios together with our OEM and ODM partners.\N从最大的 AI 实验室到超大规模和 NeoCloud 服务商，我们正与整个生态系统中的 OEM 和 ODM 合作伙伴携手，共同推动 Helios 的落地。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.92,0:30:51.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of our deepest and earliest partners deploying Helios is OpenAI.\N我们最早且最深入的合作伙伴之一，正在部署 Helios 的是 OpenAI。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.74,0:31:00.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,To talk about where AI is headed and the work we're doing together, please welcome to the stage OpenAI's Head of Infrastructure, Sachin Katti.\N为了探讨人工智能的发展方向以及我们正在共同推进的工作，请欢迎 OpenAI 基础设施负责人萨钦·卡蒂登台。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.92,0:31:08.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, thank you, thank you.\N谢谢，谢谢，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.82,0:31:09.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Sachin.\N谢谢你，萨钦。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.82,0:31:11.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's so great to have you here.\N很高兴你今天能来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.80,0:31:15.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And most importantly, we are so thankful for the partnership with OpenAI.\N最重要的是，我们非常感谢与 OpenAI 的合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.16,0:31:18.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've been through so much on this journey together.\N我们在这段共同的旅程中经历了太多。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.02,0:31:22.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you're really operating on the frontier of AI.\N所以你实际上正处在人工智能的最前沿。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.76,0:31:28.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you just tell us a little bit of what you're seeing and just what compute looks like for you?\N你能简单跟我们说说你看到了什么，以及你们所看到的计算能力是什么样的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.84,0:31:29.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks, great to be here.\N谢谢，很高兴来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.36,0:31:34.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was thinking about this event over the last two years.\N我一直在思考这个活动，过去两年里。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.38,0:31:38.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,It feels like the attendance at this event is following scaling laws.\N这个活动的参与人数看起来正遵循着规模增长规律。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.24,0:31:42.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's been doubling every year over the last two years.\N过去两年里，参与人数每年都在翻倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.80,0:31:53.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,But more seriously, to your question, we've always predicted that models will evolve where they will start as chatbots, then they become reasoners, then they\N但更严肃地说，针对你的问题，我们一直预测，这些模型将不断演进，从聊天机器人开始，然后变成推理引擎，再然后
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.66,0:31:55.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,become agents, then they become interns.\N成为代理，然后他们就成为实习生。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.36,0:31:58.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the trajectory has kept up with that.\N而且这一趋势一直保持同步。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.98,0:32:06.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we are all seeing that models are becoming a lot more capable, more agentic, and able to do very long-running tasks.\N所以我们都能看到，模型正变得越来越强大，更具主动性，能够执行长时间运行的任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.68,0:32:08.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let them go and they just take care of it.\N让他们去处理，他们自己会搞定的。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.08,0:32:13.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so all that really means is we need to keep scaling compute.\N所以归根结底，我们只需要持续扩大计算规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.76,0:32:18.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,The more compute we scale and throw at training, the more capabilities emerge,\N我们投入的计算资源越多，训练时的算力越强，涌现的能力也就越多，
Dialogue: 0,0:32:19.22,0:32:26.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,the more compute we scale and provide it to distributing intelligence to the world, the more people want to do with it.\N我们提供的计算能力越强，并将智能分发到全球，人们就越想用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.44,0:32:29.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is what we see with exploding token budgets.\N这就是我们看到的词元预算激增的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.40,0:32:34.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've seen internally, for example, in OpenAI, that not just engineering,\N我们内部看到，例如在 OpenAI，不仅仅是工程领域，
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.08,0:32:39.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,but every aspect of the enterprise is beginning to use agents for every part of the work.\N但企业中的每个方面都开始使用代理来完成工作的各个部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.88,0:32:50.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is why we need platforms like yours that can scale with how quickly the capabilities of these models are scaling, as well as how quickly the whole world is\N这就是为什么我们需要你们这样的平台，能够随着这些模型能力的快速提升，以及全世界发展速度的加快而同步扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.18,0:32:52.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,beginning to embrace what these things can do.\N开始真正认识到这些技术所能带来的改变。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.32,0:32:57.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, Sachin, I don't think I've ever spoken to you where you haven't asked me for more compute.\N嗯，萨钦，我想我从未和你聊过天，而你没有向我要更多算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.34,0:33:00.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,So he's actually very, very consistent.\N所以他实际上非常一致。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.38,0:33:04.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Look, our teams have been working really closely together.\N看，我们的团队一直紧密合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.60,0:33:09.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's been a true journey when we think about just all of the technology that we've been doing.\N当我们回顾我们所做的一切技术时，这确实是一段真正的旅程。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.34,0:33:19.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Last year, we announced a really landmark partnership where you're going to deploy up to six gigawatts of AMD infrastructure.\N去年，我们宣布了一项具有里程碑意义的合作，你们将部署高达六吉瓦的AMD基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.44,0:33:25.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're one of the first, I think you're the first to actually have MI455 racks a few months ago.\N你们是最早部署MI455机架的公司之一，我想你们是第一家在几个月前就实际部署了该设备的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.64,0:33:27.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you talk a little bit about the journey?\N那你能谈谈这段历程吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.22,0:33:30.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, it's been a phenomenal partnership.\N不，这是一段非凡的合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.82,0:33:38.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you mentioned, we were first to bet on AMD, and we are really thrilled with how that bet is turning out for us.\N正如你提到的，我们是最早押注AMD的公司，现在我们对这一决策的成果感到非常兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.54,0:33:43.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,It got started on MI300 and expanded very quickly to 355.\N这始于MI300，并迅速扩展到MI355。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.86,0:33:56.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's been really fun for our team to see how it was possible to optimize the software stack, the networking and everything, and deploy our models running on AMD infrastructure.\N我们的团队非常享受看到如何优化软件栈、网络以及所有相关部分，并成功将我们的模型部署在AMD基础设施上运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.60,0:34:05.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as Lisa mentioned, we just got hands on the Helios racks three months ago, and the collaboration has gone to the next level.\N正如丽莎提到的，我们三个月前才首次接触到Helios机架，合作已经迈上了新台阶。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.52,0:34:15.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our engineers are working side by side with AMD engineers to optimize the software stack and run GPT class workloads on Helios already.\N我们的工程师正与 AMD 工程师并肩合作，优化软件栈，并已在 Helios 上运行 GPT 类工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.34,0:34:22.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Phil will probably be on stage later talking about how productive and fast that collaboration is.\N菲尔稍后可能会上台，谈谈这次合作有多高效、多迅速。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.14,0:34:27.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we are really excited about the capabilities Helios is already showing us,\N所以我们对海利俄斯已经展现出的能力感到非常兴奋，
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.08,0:34:36.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we expect that we'll be deploying Helios at massive scale starting towards the end of this year and then accelerating throughout 2027.\N我们预计将在今年年底开始大规模部署Helios，并在2027年加速推进。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.48,0:34:37.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I said, I know, more faster.\N就像我说的，我知道，更快。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.98,0:34:39.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need it earlier.\N我们需要更早地得到它。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:42.08,0:34:48.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Sachin, the other thing is, one of the most exciting parts of our collaboration is actually some of the research work.\N所以，萨钦，另一件令人兴奋的事是，我们的合作中有一部分是研究工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.20,0:34:59.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So very thankful for the opportunity to spend really bringing our best engineers together with your researchers to talk about how AI should be really implemented\N非常感谢这次机会，能让我们最优秀的工程师与你们的研究人员齐聚一堂，深入探讨人工智能的真正落地方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.66,0:35:03.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,and used for future both silicon and software.\N并用于未来的硅片和软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.02,0:35:05.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you talk a little bit about that work?\N你能稍微谈一下那项工作吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.34,0:35:14.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think one of our key bets, and I think for a lot of us in AI, is about recursion, right?\N是的，我认为我们的一项关键押注，也是我们很多人在人工智能领域关注的重点，就是递归，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.36,0:35:22.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI recursively improving the systems it needs to run on and eventually, obviously, AI doing the research itself, right?\N人工智能不断自我优化运行所需的系统，最终显然会自己开展研究，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.20,0:35:28.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, expert engineers spend an enormous amount of time optimizing kernels,\N如今，专家工程师花费大量时间优化内核，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.48,0:35:35.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,figuring out how to translate new models to run them efficiently on different hardware, dealing with all the usual things you think about, compilers,\N研究如何将新模型高效地移植到不同硬件上运行，还要处理所有常规问题，比如编译器、
Dialogue: 0,0:35:36.08,0:35:38.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,communications, libraries, system configurations.\N通信、库和系统配置。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.80,0:35:51.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we've been super excited and encouraged by the work we are doing with you is now AI showing the potential and demonstrating it in production to automate\N我们非常兴奋并受到鼓舞的是，我们与你们合作的工作现在展现出人工智能的潜力，并在生产环境中证明了其能力，能够自动化
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.52,0:35:55.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,a significant portion of the work when anyone programs to an AMD GPU.\N任何人针对 AMD GPU 编程时的大量工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.08,0:36:08.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it dramatically has shortened the path from a new model coming up to an efficient production deployment and something that we can much more easily tune to changing workload requirements, right?\N这极大地缩短了从新模型诞生到高效生产部署的路径，并让我们能更轻松地根据不断变化的工作负载需求进行调整，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.00,0:36:10.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's a big deal.\N这意义重大。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:10.76,0:36:20.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So one of the other things that's super exciting for us is because AMD is built around an open software ecosystem, all these things that we are now inventing\N另一件让我们非常兴奋的事是，由于 AMD 建立在开放软件生态之上，我们现在为自身用途所开发的这些技术，
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.62,0:36:30.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,internally for our own use, we believe can, we can also bring it to the whole world and allow the whole world to use it for all of the AI models out there, not just our models.\N我们相信也能推广到全世界，让全世界都能使用这些技术来支持所有的人工智能模型，而不仅仅是我们的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.72,0:36:33.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think super excited about that.\N我对此感到非常兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.26,0:36:37.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the idea is that it's really the tide that lifts all boats, right?\N我认为这个理念真正做到了让所有船只都随之上升，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.30,0:36:41.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,As we work, it helps our work together, but it really helps the overall ecosystem.\N我们在合作时，这有助于我们共同的工作，更关键的是，它真正促进了整个生态系统的进步。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.76,0:36:43.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a little bit of your crystal ball.\N所以，稍微预测一下未来。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.38,0:36:48.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Looking forward, I think we all know that compute is super critical.\N展望未来，我认为我们都明白，计算能力至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.92,0:36:51.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you need from the next generation AI infrastructure?\N下一代AI基础设施，您需要什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.96,0:36:58.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what can we do as really a key partner to help you accomplish that mission?\N我们作为关键合作伙伴，能做些什么来帮助您完成这一使命？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.80,0:37:02.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you haven't heard already, I need more compute more quickly.\N如果你还没听说，我需要更快地获得更多的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.56,0:37:05.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,At least he's consistent.\N至少他保持了一致性。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:08.52,0:37:15.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the thing that the whole industry is realizing is it's a systems problem at a data center scale.\N我认为整个行业正在意识到，这在数据中心规模上是一个系统性问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.84,0:37:25.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think we obviously very quickly internalized that AI was a rack level problem, but now it is very clear that it's not just a rack level problem, it's a rack in a data center.\N所以我认为我们显然很快意识到，AI 是一个机架级别的问题，但现在很清楚，它不仅仅是机架级别问题，而是整个数据中心的机架问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.96,0:37:27.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the whole data center is a system.\N所以整个数据中心就是一个系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.08,0:37:38.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have to think about how we design the future based on what we know about our workloads, what's coming down the line, but co-design it with you from CPUs to\N我们必须基于我们对工作负载的了解、未来的发展趋势，与你们共同设计，从CPU到
Dialogue: 0,0:37:38.10,0:37:44.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPUs to memory, networking, storage, power distribution in a data center, and the cooling systems that go with it.\NGPU、内存、网络、存储、数据中心的电力分配，以及配套的冷却系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.78,0:37:48.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are all intertwined and they all have to be co-designed.\N这些因素相互关联，必须协同设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.80,0:38:00.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of the really fun parts about what we do with you and your team is how easy and productive it is for us to work with you and give you insight into how we\N我们与你们及你们团队合作时，最有趣的部分之一就是我们与你们协作起来如此轻松高效，能够向你们提供洞察。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.82,0:38:04.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,expect the world to change in the future from what our workload needs are,\N关于我们工作负载需求所预示的未来世界将如何变化，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.50,0:38:12.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,what our models are, and how quickly your team responds in turning those insights into better chips, better systems, better software.\N我们的模型是什么，以及你们团队如何迅速将这些洞察转化为更好的芯片、更好的系统、更好的软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:13.10,0:38:22.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's what worked really well with MI400 and left shifted a lot of the engineering work that we needed to do to bring this up online quickly.\N这正是 MI400 项目之所以非常成功的原因，也让我们能将大量工程工作前置，快速将系统上线。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.74,0:38:27.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why we are very confident we can productionize those systems very quickly.\N这也正是我们非常有信心能迅速实现这些系统的量产化的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.48,0:38:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so really looking forward to accelerating that with MI500 and beyond and increasingly using AI to actually do that work for us rather than being limited by humans.\N因此，我们非常期待通过 MI500 及后续产品进一步加速这一进程，并越来越多地利用 AI 来实际完成这些工作，而不是受限于人力。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.86,0:38:41.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's fantastic, Sachin.\N太棒了，萨钦。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.32,0:38:44.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And look, we really do recognize that input is so, so valuable.\N而且，我们确实认识到你们的输入是如此宝贵。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.36,0:38:49.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I have to say thank you again for just the extraordinary partnership,\N所以我必须再次感谢你们所展现出的非凡合作，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:49.80,0:38:56.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,the amount of work that our joint teams are doing together, and we couldn't be more excited about the opportunities in front of us.\N我们联合团队共同努力所投入的工作量，以及我们对眼前机遇的无比兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.28,0:38:57.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Sachin.\N谢谢你，萨钦。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:57.22,0:38:57.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.\N非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.12,0:39:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes. Alright.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.09,0:39:07.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now let's turn to the world of CPUs.\N那么现在我们转向 CPU 的世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.99,0:39:17.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's been a lot of talk about CPUs recently, and I can say that this has been the foundation of our AMD data center strategy for the longest time.\N近期关于 CPU 的讨论非常多，我可以告诉大家，这一直是 AMD 数据中心战略的基石，时间最长。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.67,0:39:22.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We launched EPYC in 2017, and we've been on a very, very clear mission.\N我们在 2017 年推出了 EPYC，一直有着非常明确的目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.23,0:39:30.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every generation, more performance, more efficiency, more capability for a wider range of workloads.\N每一代都带来更高的性能、更高的效率、更强的能力，支持更广泛的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.45,0:39:32.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, Naples was our first generation.\N现在，Naples 是我们的第一代产品。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:33.41,0:39:38.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It established the foundation, but Rome and Milan really changed the economics in the data center.\N它奠定了基础，但 Rome 和 Milan 才真正改变了数据中心的经济格局。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.77,0:39:44.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did more than what people expected in terms of adding core count and adding throughput.\N我们在核心数量和吞吐量方面所实现的，远超人们的预期。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:44.91,0:39:53.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then Turin set... Genoa expanded our performance, and then Turin set a new bar for density, throughput, and total cost of ownership.\N然后 Turin 推出了……Genoa 进一步提升了性能，而 Turin 则在密度、吞吐量和总拥有成本方面树立了新标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.63,0:39:55.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's really been the EPYC formula.\N这正是 EPYC 的成功公式。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.55,0:40:03.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,A clear roadmap and very consistent execution, and leadership that actually grows with every generation.\N清晰的路线图和一贯的执行，以及每一代都在持续提升的领导力。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.33,0:40:09.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is why, if you look today, 5th Gen EPYC Turin is the best server CPU in the world.\N这就是为什么，如果你今天查看，第五代 EPYC Turin 是全球最佳的服务器 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.29,0:40:21.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,With up to 192 cores and 384 threads, Turin delivers leadership performance across a broad range of cloud, enterprise, and HPC workloads.\NTurin 最多可提供 192 个核心和 384 个线程，在云、企业及高性能计算等多种工作负载中均表现出领先性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:21.81,0:40:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the thing about the data center is compute never stands still.\N但数据中心的计算能力从来不会停滞不前。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.95,0:40:34.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,With agentic AI, it's actually creating a whole new class of infrastructure, and the CPU matters now more than ever.\N有了代理式 AI，实际上正在催生一类全新的基础设施，而 CPU 的重要性如今比以往任何时候都更大。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.79,0:40:37.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what we built Venice for.\N这正是我们打造 Venice 的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.63,0:40:42.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, there's been a lot of talk about agentic AI, but it's actually a very new field.\N因此，关于代理式 AI 的讨论很多，但事实上这是一个非常新的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.31,0:40:49.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we see is that server computing is actually splitting across a couple of different workloads.\N我们看到的是，服务器计算实际上正在向几类不同的工作负载分化。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.89,0:40:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the first section is GPU servers, and that's fairly well known.\N第一个部分是 GPU 服务器，这一点大家已经很熟悉。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.09,0:41:00.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's where the CPU's job is basically to drive the GPUs.\N在这里，CPU 的主要任务就是驱动 GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:01.23,0:41:04.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the job there is all about speed.\N因此，这里的重点完全在于速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.03,0:41:10.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want the highest frequency cores, we want the fastest IO, and we want to keep the GPUs fully fed.\N我们需要最高频率的核心，最快的 I/O，还要确保 GPU 始终得到充分供给。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:11.85,0:41:18.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the biggest middle part, this is the largest growth, is actually in agent servers, or what we call agent sandboxes.\N现在，最大的中间部分，也就是增长最快的领域，实际上是代理服务器，或我们所说的代理沙盒。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.79,0:41:21.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is actually a whole new class of workload.\N而这实际上是一个全新的工作负载类别。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:22.01,0:41:31.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here, you execute code, you actually call a bunch of tools, you actually query data that's outside the model, you have a whole bunch of things around it.\N在这里，你执行代码，实际调用大量工具，实际查询模型外部的数据，周围还有一系列其他功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:31.65,0:41:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in this place, the priority is actually density.\N在这个领域，优先考虑的是密度。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.39,0:41:42.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we want the highest performing cores per watt to run thousands of agents at once.\N因此，我们希望每瓦特功耗下拥有最高性能的核心，以同时运行数千个代理。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.77,0:41:47.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we have our traditional general purpose servers that run the enterprise.\N然后我们还有传统的通用服务器，用于运行企业级应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:47.09,0:41:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here, you're going to have a diversity of workloads.\N在这里，你将面对多样化的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.15,0:41:55.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's all about efficiency, it's running the applications, it's running databases, it's running data services.\N这一切关乎效率，是运行应用程序，运行数据库，运行数据服务。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.73,0:42:01.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that is what we traditionally say is general purpose server.\N所有这些就是我们传统意义上所说的通用服务器。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.83,0:42:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, with these different workloads, you actually need the right CPU for the right workload.\N因此，面对这些不同的工作负载，你实际上需要为每种工作负载配备合适的CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.89,0:42:12.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And EPYC is the only CPU portfolio that leads across all three.\N而EPYC是唯一一个在所有三个领域都领先的CPU产品组合。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:13.69,0:42:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Venice is our newest and most advanced server CPU family, and it's actually designed for the agentic era.\N因此，威尼斯是我们最新、最先进的服务器CPU系列，实际上是为代理时代而设计的。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.15,0:42:25.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're extending Turin's leadership across every single metric.\N我们正在将图灵的领先地位扩展到每一个指标上。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:25.89,0:42:33.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is performance, that's efficiency, that's TCO for cloud, that's enterprise efficiency, that's HPC workloads.\N这是性能，这是效率，这是云服务的总拥有成本，这是企业效率，这是高性能计算工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.43,0:42:37.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Venice starts with our all new Zen 6 core.\N代号威尼斯从我们全新的Zen 6核心开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:38.29,0:42:45.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have higher IPC, higher frequency, and that delivers up to 1.8 times more performance than Turin.\N我们拥有更高的每时钟周期指令数、更高的频率，性能相比图林最高提升1.8倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.73,0:42:49.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is one of the largest generational gains.\N这是历史上最大的一代性能提升之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:49.85,0:42:55.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we have been doing this for six generations, but this is one of the largest generational gains in the history of EPYC.\N我们已经连续六代这么做，但这是EPYC历史上最大的一代性能提升之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.97,0:43:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's 203 billion transistors built on TSMC's newest two nanometer process, and it uses a next generation chiplet that supports up to 512 threads per socket.\N它拥有2030亿个晶体管，采用台积电最新的2纳米工艺制造，采用新一代小芯片架构，每插槽支持高达512个线程。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.33,0:43:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is actually a really important point.\N这实际上是一个非常关键的点。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:10.39,0:43:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to show you why in a few minutes.\N我稍后会向你们展示原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.37,0:43:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This gives us the highest compute density, but it also allows us to double both the memory and the IO bandwidth.\N这使我们实现了最高的计算密度，同时也让内存和I/O带宽翻倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.29,0:43:24.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I have a few more chips to show you, if that's all right.\N如果可以的话，我再向大家展示几款芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:25.29,0:43:29.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what's clear is Venice is not one chip.\N显而易见，威尼斯并非单一芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.43,0:43:33.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Venice is actually an entire family of chips.\N威尼斯实际上是一整套芯片家族。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.91,0:43:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is where our chiplet architecture becomes a huge, huge advantage.\N这正是我们的芯片小片架构发挥巨大优势的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:38.31,0:43:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It lets us take the Zen 6 architecture and build a whole portfolio around it.\N它让我们能够基于 Zen 6 架构构建一整套产品组合。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:44.83,0:43:46.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's start with this guy.\N那么我们先从这个开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.15,0:43:50.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is Venice HF.\N这是 Venice HF。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.23,0:43:56.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the highest performing CPU that drives AI host nodes.\N这是驱动 AI 主机节点性能最高的 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.63,0:44:07.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has eight compute chiplets, each with 12 cores, running at up to 5 gigahertz with the IO and memory bandwidth to keep the GPUs completely fed.\N它拥有八个计算小片，每个小片配备 12 个核心，最高运行频率达 5 吉赫兹，并具备足够的 I/O 和内存带宽，确保 GPU 充分供能。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:07.27,0:44:11.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is the CPU that I showed you before shipping inside Helios.\N这就是我之前在 Helios 内部展示过的 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.89,0:44:23.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, this is its bigger brother.\N现在这是它的升级版。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.21,0:44:26.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's Venice 256 core.\N这是拥有 256 个核心的 Venice。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.93,0:44:30.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the chip that's built for agentic sandboxes.\N这颗芯片专为智能体沙盒设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:30.79,0:44:35.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it also has eight compute chiplets, but each of the chiplets now has 32 cores.\N它同样拥有八个计算小片，但每个小片现在拥有 32 个核心。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.97,0:44:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it scales all the way to 512 threads.\N因此它可扩展至 512 个线程。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:39.35,0:44:42.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it is the highest compute density in the industry.\N这是业界最高的计算密度。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:49.06,0:44:54.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Customers get more agent capacity per watt, per dollar, per rack, bar none.\N客户在每瓦特、每美元、每机架的算力上都获得了最大提升，毫无例外。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:58.27,0:45:00.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, and then one more member of the family.\N好的，接下来再介绍一位家族成员。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:01.49,0:45:04.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,This one is Venice 128 core.\N这款是威尼斯 128 核。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.65,0:45:07.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this guy is optimized for enterprise and general purpose servers.\N这款专为企事业单位和通用服务器优化。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.51,0:45:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the same leadership performance per core, but it's in a lower cost, lower power design for enterprise applications.\N每核性能保持领先，但采用了成本更低、功耗更低的设计，适用于企业应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.63,0:45:22.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this one is really tuned to give customers the best performance per dollar across a wide range of configurations.\N这款产品在各种配置下，为客户实现了每美元性能的最佳表现。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:23.01,0:45:27.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can see really the power of the family as they come together.\N所以你可以真正看到整个产品家族协同带来的强大优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.37,0:45:33.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in addition with these guys, I can tell you that next year we're adding a few other chips to the family.\N此外，这些产品之外，明年我们还将为这个家族新增几款芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.13,0:45:38.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're adding Verano, which is the next generation for AI host nodes.\N我们将推出 Verano，这是下一代 AI 主机节点。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.17,0:45:46.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what that adds is a more power efficient, low power memory, as well as faster interconnect between the CPU and the GPU.\N它带来了更省电、低功耗的内存，以及 CPU 和 GPU 之间更快的互连。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.75,0:45:55.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we're also adding for our high performance computing, our technical computing, Venice X, which is using our 3D vCache stacking technology.\N此外，我们还将为高性能计算和专业技术计算推出威尼斯 X，它采用了我们的 3D vCache 堆叠技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:55.51,0:46:04.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're really the first to stack memory chiplets right below the compute chiplets to accelerate performance, even for those types of workloads.\N我们是首个将内存小芯片直接堆叠在计算小芯片下方的公司，从而加速性能，即使是针对这类工作负载也是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.33,0:46:06.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can see one architecture.\N所以你可以看到一种架构。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:06.43,0:46:08.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,A CPU is not a CPU.\NCPU 并不都是 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:09.57,0:46:11.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are many different types of CPUs.\N存在多种不同类型的 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.95,0:46:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for us, one architecture spans dozens of different chips.\N对我们而言，一种架构覆盖了数十种不同的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.13,0:46:20.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that breadth is someone that no other CPU vendor can match.\N这种广度是其他任何 CPU 厂商都无法匹敌的。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.45,0:46:24.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's what makes 6th Gen EPYC the best CPU in the data center.\N这正是第六代 EPYC 成为数据中心最佳 CPU 的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.98,0:46:36.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now you're going to bear with me because I'm going to take you through some performance because the numbers are just incredible.\N现在请耐心听我说，我将带你们看看一些性能数据，因为这些数字实在太惊人了。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.00,0:46:40.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So looking at AI workloads, right?\N所以我们来看一下 AI 工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.16,0:46:46.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Again, you have different use cases and different workloads, starting first with GPU servers.\N再次强调，存在不同的使用场景和工作负载，首先是 GPU 服务器。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:47.02,0:46:52.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Many of the largest frontier models require you to move data between the CPU and the GPU.\N许多最前沿的模型需要在 CPU 和 GPU 之间移动数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.80,0:47:02.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in that scenario, Venice moves the data faster than the best competitive x86 processor, delivering up to 1.8 times more tokens per second.\N在这种场景下，Venice 的数据传输速度比最佳的竞争对手 x86 处理器更快，每秒可处理多达 1.8 倍的词元。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.68,0:47:12.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at the agentic CPU servers and sandboxes, because of our density, Venice delivers more than twice the agents per watt for agent sandboxes.\N当你观察代理型CPU服务器和沙盒时，由于我们的密度优势，威尼斯在代理沙盒中每瓦特的代理数量超过两倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.28,0:47:18.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for general purpose applications, in this case, we're standardizing on a 100 kilowatt rack.\N对于通用应用，我们在此情况下采用100千瓦机架的标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:18.88,0:47:22.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Venice delivers more than twice the performance per watt.\N威尼斯每瓦特的性能超过两倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.36,0:47:25.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So pretty incredible results.\N因此结果非常惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.48,0:47:30.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the gap is even wider if you look at ARM processors.\N如果你再看ARM处理器，差距会更大。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:31.24,0:47:40.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you look at the leading ARM processors, when we're comparing at the chip level, Venice supports up to 2.8 times more agents per watt.\N因此，当我们在芯片层面进行比较时，威尼斯每瓦特支持的代理数量最多可达领先ARM处理器的2.8倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:40.86,0:47:47.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at the rack level, Venice is delivering up to 3.3 times more performance per watt.\N而在机架层面，威尼斯每瓦特的性能最高可达3.3倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.80,0:47:56.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what that means is at the data center scale, you can just get a lot more agents in the same power envelope.\N这意味着在数据中心规模上，你可以在相同的功耗范围内部署更多代理。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.30,0:48:12.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, there's been a lot of talk about what matters most for agentic AI, with some saying that per-core performance under load is the only thing that counts.\N近来关于代理型AI最关键的因素有很多讨论，有人认为负载下的每核性能才是唯一重要的。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.34,0:48:24.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,But that's really only part of the story, because agentic AI actually runs as a distributed platform, and that is across databases and vector stores and orchestration.\N但这只是故事的一部分，因为代理型AI实际上是一个分布式平台，涉及数据库、向量存储和编排。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.90,0:48:27.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that has to happen at once.\N所有这些必须同时发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:27.48,0:48:37.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that requires not just raw speed, but you absolutely need density, efficiency, and per-core performance all together.\N这不仅需要原始速度，更需要密度、效率和每核性能三者兼备。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.06,0:48:42.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what I'm happy to say is that Venice leads across every one of them.\N我很高兴地告诉大家，威尼斯在所有这些方面都处于领先地位。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:43.22,0:48:52.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you compare Venice against the highest performing ARM CPU from our competition, EPYC delivers 20% higher per-core performance.\N因此，当您将威尼斯与竞争对手最高效的ARM CPU进行对比时，EPYC的单核性能高出20%。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.90,0:48:54.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when we...\N当我们将这一点……
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.69,0:49:01.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like that number.\N我喜欢这个数字。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:01.79,0:49:02.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like that number.\N我喜欢这个数字。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.27,0:49:09.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when we pair that with leadership core density, we're delivering 2.2 times more performance at the socket level.\N再加上领先的核心密度，我们在插槽级别实现了2.2倍的性能提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.45,0:49:17.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the main point is, whether a customer needs per-core or per-socket performance, Venice is the leader.\N所以核心要点是，无论客户需要单核性能还是单插槽性能，威尼斯都是领导者。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:18.39,0:49:21.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And there's one more point that a benchmark doesn't really capture,\N还有一点，基准测试其实很难体现，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.63,0:49:31.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,because when you think about what agentic AI is, it's really like you're adding thousands of employees to your enterprise, to your traditional workflow.\N因为当你思考代理式AI时，实际上就像是为企业和传统工作流程增加了数千名员工。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.77,0:49:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that software, enterprises have been running on for years.\N以及企业多年来一直在运行的软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.79,0:49:39.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,The truth is, that software runs on x86.\N事实上，这些软件运行在x86架构上。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.61,0:49:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So Venice runs all of it.\N而威尼斯可以运行所有这些软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:42.31,0:49:44.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is where x86 has an advantage.\N这正是 x86 的优势所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.73,0:49:46.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,You must have the best performance.\N你必须拥有最佳性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:46.37,0:49:47.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,You must have the best density.\N你必须拥有最佳密度。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.97,0:49:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,But having that software compatibility is a big, big plus.\N但拥有软件兼容性是一个巨大的优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.89,0:49:55.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So customers scale up their agents on the stack that they already have.\N因此，客户可以在他们现有的系统上扩展其代理。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:56.87,0:49:59.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, let me just show you what that means at the rack level.\N现在，让我来展示一下这在机架层面意味着什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:00.23,0:50:04.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So at the rack level, what we find is density is super important.\N在机架层面，我们发现密度至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:04.05,0:50:06.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone's trying to optimize their data center.\N每个人都在优化他们的数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.31,0:50:08.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone's trying to optimize their power envelope.\N每个人都在优化他们的功耗范围。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:09.07,0:50:15.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with Venice, every major server OEM is offering a broad spectrum of racks for agentic AI.\N有了 Venice，各大服务器 OEM 都提供了广泛多样的机架，以支持代理式 AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:16.09,0:50:22.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what that means is we have the full spectrum from 25,000 cores to 50,000 cores.\N这意味着我们从 25,000 个核心到 50,000 个核心，覆盖了完整范围。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.19,0:50:25.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's more agents per rack.\N这意味着每台机架可以支持更多代理。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:25.25,0:50:27.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that gives customers the choice.\N这为客户提供了选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.95,0:50:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The key is, every data center is different.\N关键在于，每个数据中心都各不相同。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:30.25,0:50:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with that, the flexibility allows you to pick the right cooling, the right space requirements for what you're trying to do in your data center.\N有了这一点，灵活性使您能够根据数据中心的实际需求，选择合适的冷却方式和空间要求。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.75,0:50:40.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there you have it.\N所以，情况就是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:41.55,0:50:44.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Venice, the best server CPU in the industry.\N威尼斯，业界最强的服务器CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.62,0:50:55.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm very happy to say also today that Venice is in full production.\N我很高兴地宣布，今天威尼斯已全面投入生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.20,0:50:57.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Customer demand is incredible.\N客户需求非常强劲。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.30,0:51:01.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the strongest we've ever seen for a new EPYC generation.\N这是我们有史以来见过的最强新代EPYC产品需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:06.99,0:51:18.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're seeing every major server OEM, every major cloud provider on track to begin rolling out in the fourth quarter as we start with making the broadest EPYC launch we've ever had.\N我们看到所有主要服务器OEM厂商和主要云服务提供商都已按计划，将在第四季度开始推出，而我们将开启有史以来最广泛的EPYC发布。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:19.45,0:51:26.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,So with that, I want to turn to my next guest, who runs some of the largest and most advanced compute infrastructure in the world.\N接下来，我想介绍下一位嘉宾，他负责管理世界上最大、最先进的计算基础设施之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:26.81,0:51:33.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's really been our privilege to partner with them as they've deployed multiple generations of both EPYC and Instinct.\N我们非常荣幸能与他们合作，见证他们部署了多代EPYC和Instinct产品。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:34.07,0:51:40.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,To share more about our work together, please welcome to the stage Meta's Head of Infrastructure, Santosh Janardhan.\N为了进一步分享我们合作的成果，请欢迎Meta基础设施负责人桑托什·贾纳德汉登台。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.75,0:51:52.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is so great to have you here.\N很高兴你们能来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.47,0:51:53.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for being here.\N感谢你们的到来。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:54.55,0:51:56.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Santosh is a true friend.\N桑托什是一位真正的朋友。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.83,0:52:01.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have to say it's been a tremendous opportunity over the last few years.\N我必须说，过去几年里这是一次非凡的机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:01.47,0:52:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,My story about Santosh is the first time I sat in his office.\N我和桑托什的故事，是我第一次坐在他的办公室里。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.41,0:52:09.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,He said to me, Lisa, we're going to deploy a lot of CPUs.\N他对我说，丽莎，我们要部署大量CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.35,0:52:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Please make sure they work.\N请确保它们能正常工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.91,0:52:15.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I said, I will, I will.\N我说，我会的，我一定会。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:15.01,0:52:16.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you lift it up.\N然后你把它举起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.07,0:52:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I try. I try.\N我试了，我一直在试。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:18.99,0:52:24.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,But look, Santosh, Meta operates, you operate some of the most advanced infrastructure in the world.\N但你看，桑托什，Meta在运营，你们也在运营着世界上一些最先进的基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.11,0:52:27.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's happening in the data center world?\N数据中心领域正在发生什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.81,0:52:28.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's happening in your world?\N你的世界里发生了什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.81,0:52:33.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tell us a little bit about the architecture and what you're working on.\N请简单介绍一下架构以及你正在做的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.81,0:52:34.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure. First of all, thank you.\N当然。首先，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.87,0:52:35.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:35.59,0:52:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is like a hardware geek's paradise, right?\N这简直就像硬件极客的天堂，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:38.17,0:52:42.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You come in, you're talking about transistors, you're talking about hardware, talking about cooling.\N你一进来，就在聊晶体管，聊硬件，聊散热。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.79,0:52:43.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is sort of the gem.\N这才是真正的亮点。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.69,0:52:44.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like it.\N我喜欢。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.25,0:52:47.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think there's an audience that's receptive to it.\N我觉得有一群观众是愿意接受这些内容的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.25,0:52:49.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,I usually talk to audiences.\N我通常会面对观众演讲。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:50.17,0:52:54.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have usually either not been to a data center or not really seen a chip ever.\N他们通常要么没去过数据中心，要么根本没见过芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:54.45,0:52:56.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is refreshing, I have to say.\N所以这让人耳目一新，我必须这么说。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:57.47,0:52:58.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,The thing I'll say about...\N我想说的是……
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.81,0:53:01.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Listen, we are seeing demand go through the roof.\N听着，我们正看到需求飙升。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:02.59,0:53:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you look at inference, training, recommendation system, that's how a newsfeed works.\N从推理、训练、推荐系统来看，这就是新闻推送的工作原理。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.01,0:53:08.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Content creation.\N内容创作。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.39,0:53:11.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,The demand for that is just exponential right now.\N目前对这方面的需求正呈指数级增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.65,0:53:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when I think about sort of the overall...\N当我思考整体情况时……
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.17,0:53:22.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mark has this vision of delivering personal super intelligence to billions of people.\N马克有一个愿景，就是为数十亿人提供个人超级智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.43,0:53:33.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you go to sort of Facebook or Instagram or WhatsApp or whatever surface you go to, the idea is that we'll meet you there and we'll deliver super personalized intelligence right wherever you are.\N所以无论你去的是 Facebook、Instagram 还是 WhatsApp，或者任何其他平台，我们的想法都是在你所在的地方与你相遇，为你提供高度个性化的超级智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:34.17,0:53:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why we established this Meta compute initiative and because it's a top level thing, Mark himself oversees.\N这就是我们设立 Meta 计算计划的原因，而且这是最高优先级的事项，由马克本人亲自负责。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.75,0:53:46.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now what it means is that we are now moving away from an area where we used to take servers, optimize it.\N现在这意味着我们正从过去那种方式转变，我们过去会采购服务器并进行优化。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.03,0:53:53.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is what the conversation we were having many years ago, that, hey, I'm deploying a CPU, I really need to maximize performance out of it.\N这就是多年前我们讨论过的内容，当时我说，我正在部署 CPU，真的需要最大化它的性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.65,0:53:54.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's different now.\N现在情况不同了。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:54.99,0:53:58.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,You talked about how we should be thinking about the whole system end to end.\N你们谈到了我们应该如何从头到尾地思考整个系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:59.27,0:54:05.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are at a point where we have to look about the whole data center and think about it as one integrated system.\N我们现在处于一个必须全面审视整个数据中心，并将其视为一个集成系统的阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:05.89,0:54:10.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Servers, hardware, networking, cooling, power, all of that is not optional.\N服务器、硬件、网络、冷却、供电等，这些都不是可选项。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.83,0:54:12.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of that has to work together.\N所有这些都必须协同工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:12.67,0:54:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is where I think there's a huge opportunity for collaboration with partners like AMD because you have to now co-design, co-create systems, not just\N我认为这正是我们与 AMD 这类合作伙伴开展深度协作的巨大机遇，因为现在你必须共同设计、共同创造系统，而不仅仅是
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.91,0:54:24.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,deploy something that comes off the shelf.\N部署一个现成的方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:25.13,0:54:27.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other thing is, by the way, flexibility.\N另外，灵活性也很重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.45,0:54:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The thing I really like about what you said is that this is such a big opportunity in the industry right now.\N我非常认同你所说的，目前这个行业正面临如此巨大的机遇。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.11,0:54:37.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of us need to lean in and work on this together.\N我们所有人都需要积极投入，共同推进。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.45,0:54:39.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it needs to be open.\N因此，它必须是开放的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.93,0:54:41.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,It needs to be heterogeneous.\N它必须是异构的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:41.95,0:54:46.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that's not one company, one partner that works for any one of us.\N我认为这对任何一方来说，都不是某一家公司或某一个合作伙伴就能单独实现的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:47.03,0:54:48.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need to sort of work on this together.\N我们需要一起在这方面努力。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:49.03,0:54:52.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why I think you're one of our most important strategic partners.\N这就是为什么我认为你是我们最重要的战略合作伙伴之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.03,0:54:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Santosh.\N谢谢你，桑托什。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.77,0:54:57.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And look, we completely agree with your philosophy.\N而且，我们完全认同你们的理念。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.49,0:55:07.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, you are actually one of our broadest partners because if you think about our work on CPUs, GPUs, you know, we developed the Rackscale OCP systems together.\N现在，实际上你是我们的广泛合作伙伴之一，因为你们想想我们在 CPU 和 GPU 上的工作，我们共同开发了机架规模的 OCP 系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:08.37,0:55:11.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've deployed lots and lots of CPUs, so millions of CPUs.\N你们部署了大量 CPU，数以百万计的 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.31,0:55:14.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you're a lead partner on Venice.\N你们是威尼斯项目的牵头合作伙伴。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.95,0:55:18.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you just talk a little bit about sort of your CPU and infrastructure and some of our work together?\N你能简单谈一下你们的 CPU 和基础设施，以及我们之间的合作吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.43,0:55:20.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure. It's been many years.\N当然。已经有很多年了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.39,0:55:23.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the story that Lisa was saying was many years ago.\N丽莎刚才说的故事是很多年前的事了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:23.97,0:55:28.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we went from Milan to Bergamo to Turin, now to Venice.\N我觉得我们从米兰，到贝加莫，再到都灵，现在到了威尼斯。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.87,0:55:30.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's at least the fourth generation.\N所以至少已经是第四代了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:30.95,0:55:33.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a long-time partnership, obviously.\N所以这是一段长期的合作，显而易见。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:34.27,0:55:38.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,I actually think the world is changing in the sense that it used...\N我实际上认为世界正在发生变化，这种变化体现在它开始……
Dialogue: 0,0:55:38.79,0:55:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,The world is changing.\N世界正在发生变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.35,0:55:40.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every year is a new world these days.\N如今，每年都是一个全新的世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.99,0:55:41.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like every month.\N就像每个月一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.51,0:55:43.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Months, exactly.\N每个月，正是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.37,0:55:46.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what ends up happening now is that it's not just a GPU game anymore.\N所以现在发生的情况是，这已经不再只是GPU的游戏了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.97,0:55:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's CPUs and GPUs.\N这涉及CPU和GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.43,0:55:52.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,If anything, I think CPUs are becoming at least as important, if not more.\N说到底，我认为CPU的重要性至少与GPU相当，甚至可能更重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.57,0:56:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're looking at a world where sort of the workload is changing because while you have your workhorses and GPUs, at the end of the day, there's agentic workloads.\N你面对的是一个工作负载正在变化的世界，因为尽管你有主力的CPU和GPU，但最终仍存在代理型工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.27,0:56:05.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to run your tools.\N你必须运行你的工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.41,0:56:06.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to run your systems.\N你必须运行你的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.55,0:56:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all the code that's been generated still needs to run somewhere, right?\N所有生成的代码仍然需要在某个地方运行，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:10.81,0:56:12.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I'm super excited to work on Venice.\N所以我非常期待能参与威尼斯项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:12.99,0:56:15.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think there's a lot to come there.\N我觉得那里还有很多值得期待的进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:15.87,0:56:18.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you have to think again.\N你必须重新思考一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.79,0:56:26.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a theme that I'm assuming will go throughout the presentation that you have to start thinking about CPUs and GPUs as conjoined things.\N这是一个贯穿整个演示的主题，即你需要开始把 CPU 和 GPU 当作协同工作的整体来考虑。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:26.05,0:56:27.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,You hand off workloads.\N你将工作负载进行移交。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.21,0:56:29.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Depending on the workload, you employ the right hardware.\N根据工作负载的不同，使用合适的硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.15,0:56:31.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes, absolutely right.\N是的，完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.85,0:56:34.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've gotten a lot of feedback from your technical team.\N我们收到了你们技术团队的大量反馈。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:34.59,0:56:38.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's what I really appreciate about the partnership with Meta.\N我真的很欣赏与 Meta 的合作关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.49,0:56:43.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, clearly, you're deploying lots of GPUs too, a lot of accelerators.\N显然，你们也在大规模部署 GPU 和大量加速器。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:43.77,0:56:48.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you're also one of our deepest partners on the accelerator side, starting with MI300.\N而且你们也是我们在加速器领域最深入的合作伙伴之一，从 MI300 开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.29,0:56:56.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we had a very large strategic partnership announced around up to 6 gigawatts, starting with MI450.\N然后我们宣布了一项非常重大的战略合作，规模高达6吉瓦，从MI450开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:57.59,0:56:59.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we're doing is quite unique with Meta.\N我们与Meta的合作方式相当独特。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:59.53,0:57:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you talk a little bit about the evolution and the MI450 plans?\N所以你能谈谈MI450的发展历程和相关计划吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:06.21,0:57:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Again, multi-year collaboration.\N这是一次多年期的合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.39,0:57:09.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we started with MI300.\N我们最初是从MI300开始的。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.57,0:57:11.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did a bunch.\N我们做了很多工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.43,0:57:12.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,It had really nice memory capacity.\N它拥有非常出色的内存容量。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.03,0:57:14.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I remember talking to you about that, right?\N我记得我们曾讨论过这一点，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.11,0:57:17.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then there's a bunch of pipelining we did.\N我们还进行了大量流水线优化。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.59,0:57:23.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was important to just have deployed that at production scale, sort of get hands-on experience on both sides.\N重要的是，我们已将它部署到生产规模，双方都获得了实际操作经验。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.49,0:57:28.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,350 is the first time we deployed this on our ranking and recommendation systems.\NMI350是我们在排名和推荐系统中首次部署该技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.31,0:57:32.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's now getting into sort of some good numbers.\N现在，数据已经变得相当可观了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.55,0:57:34.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And 450 is, I think, I'm super excited about it.\N450让我非常兴奋，我觉得太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.85,0:57:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just got some of the racks.\N我们刚刚拿到了一些机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.71,0:57:43.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we are going to deploy it across the board because it gives us the opportunity to go and sort of really collaborate.\N我们将全面部署，因为这给了我们机会去真正协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:43.79,0:57:54.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the big difference between the 300, 350, and 450 is that we have had engineers sitting in the same room talking to each other, co-designing, co-creating, like power cooling.\N我认为300、350和450之间的主要区别在于，我们有工程师在同一间房里面对面交流，共同设计、共同创造，比如电源和散热。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.37,0:57:57.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I was saying, it's not just a single thing.\N就像我说的，这不仅仅是一个单一的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:57.79,0:58:00.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we are not shy in feedback.\N我们并不回避反馈。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.49,0:58:01.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're not shy, for sure.\N他们当然也不回避。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.99,0:58:04.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you're very receptive.\N但你们非常乐于接受。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.23,0:58:05.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is true partnership, right?\N所以这才是真正的合作关系，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:06.13,0:58:09.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the point about co-designing and co-creating that, I think.\N这就是共同设计和共同创造的意义所在，我认为。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.15,0:58:14.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And like I was saying, that's a huge sort of deployment coming in.\N就像我说的，这将带来大规模的部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:14.41,0:58:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The more we deploy, the earlier we co-design, the better we are.\N我们部署得越多，越早开始共同设计，我们的表现就越好。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.63,0:58:19.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, absolutely.\N是的，绝对的。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.55,0:58:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really, really appreciate the effort together on MI450.\N真的非常感谢大家在MI450项目上的共同努力。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.45,0:58:26.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now I want to ask you also about your crystal ball.\N现在我还想问问你关于你的水晶球。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.25,0:58:34.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you look out into the future and you see what the next few years really means as you push forward in the AI industry.\N所以你展望未来，看到在推动AI行业发展过程中，未来几年真正意味着什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.59,0:58:37.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,What are the biggest challenges and really opportunities for us?\N我们面临的最大挑战和真正机遇是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:38.01,0:58:39.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the industry ecosystem here.\N这就是这里的产业生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.83,0:58:41.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what should we be focused on as an industry?\N所以作为整个行业，我们应该关注什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:42.71,0:58:45.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Listen, all of you know about the bottlenecks.\N听着，你们所有人都知道这些瓶颈。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.11,0:58:48.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know about the power, the data centers, the silicon.\N你们知道电力、数据中心、硅材料。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:48.87,0:58:52.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these, I think, are choke points that I think the industry is waiting on.\N所有这些，我认为都是行业正在等待突破的瓶颈。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:53.49,0:58:56.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,But those are things I'm pretty confident we'll sort of work our way through.\N但这些事情，我相当有信心我们会逐步解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:57.25,0:58:59.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the end of the day, I think the demand is immense.\N归根结底，我认为需求是巨大的。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.07,0:59:00.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,People are responding.\N人们正在作出回应。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:01.77,0:59:08.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the thing that I really want to make sure all of us realize is that we should not think about systems in isolation.\N但我真正希望我们所有人都能意识到的是，我们不应该孤立地看待系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:09.51,0:59:12.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I was saying, CPUs and GPUs are one conjoined system.\N就像我刚才说的，CPU 和 GPU 是一个整体系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:12.27,0:59:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,We should start thinking about it that way.\N我们应该这样来思考。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:13.73,0:59:18.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,We really need to co-design things early.\N我们真的需要尽早进行协同设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.75,0:59:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,See, data centers take years to build.\N数据中心的建设需要数年时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:21.35,0:59:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of my favorite stories is Mark comes to me and says, hey, I want a gigawatt worth of data centers.\N我最喜欢的一个故事是，马克来找我，说嘿，我想建一个吉瓦级别的数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:26.35,0:59:27.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, you should have talked to me two years ago.\N你两年前就应该和我谈了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:28.51,0:59:29.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,It takes time.\N这需要时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:29.83,0:59:31.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the same with silicon, right?\N硅片也是如此，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:31.35,0:59:32.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,It just takes time.\N这同样需要时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:32.95,0:59:39.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we need to be starting and sitting down in a room co-designing today for what we need to deploy in 27 and 28.\N所以我们需要从今天开始坐下来，协同设计，为 2027 年和 2028 年要部署的内容做好准备。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:40.55,0:59:44.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,That, I think, is when we truly unlock all sort of powers of the system.\N我认为，那时我们才能真正释放系统的全部潜力。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:44.55,0:59:45.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,The systems are amazing.\N这些系统非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:45.57,0:59:46.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,The specs are amazing, right?\N规格非常惊人，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:47.13,0:59:52.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,But think about how much more you can get out of it if you sit in a room and just co-design it today.\N但想想看，如果你今天能坐在一个房间里，共同设计它，能获得的提升会有多大。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:52.91,0:59:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in 28, we'll be having much better graphs out there.\N到2028年，我们将拥有更出色的图形表现。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.41,0:59:57.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Fantastic.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:58.09,0:59:59.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Santosh, I completely agree with you.\N桑托什，我完全同意你的看法。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.85,1:00:01.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to say again, thank you.\N我想再次表示感谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.73,1:00:08.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are so, so happy with the amazing partnership that we have across the board and, most importantly, with your engineering teams.\N我们对全方位的卓越合作感到无比欣喜，尤其是与你们工程团队的合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:08.87,1:00:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we truly are excited about what we're going to do in the future.\N我们对未来的合作充满期待。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:11.75,1:00:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.\N非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:19.00,1:00:26.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you heard Santosh talk about just the diversity of workloads and really the massive scale that you require with AI.\N所以你们听到了桑托什谈到工作负载的多样性，以及AI所需的巨大规模。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:27.42,1:00:32.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now I want to turn to another part of the inference market where the requirements are actually very different.\N现在我想转向推理市场中的另一个部分，这里的实际需求非常不同。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:33.14,1:00:35.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So lots and lots of workloads.\N有很多很多的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:35.42,1:00:42.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as inference is moving into more products and services, we're actually seeing it segment into different workloads depending on what you're trying to do.\N随着推理逐渐融入更多产品和服务，我们实际上看到它根据你所要实现的目标，分化为不同类型的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:43.36,1:00:45.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some of these are, let's call it, less interactive.\N其中一些可以称为非交互式。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.62,1:00:49.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they're really tuned for, let's call it, maximum throughput or the lowest cost.\N它们主要针对的是最大吞吐量或最低成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:50.90,1:00:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Other of these applications require more balanced throughput, so you have to balance throughput and responsiveness.\N其他一些应用则需要更均衡的吞吐量，因此你必须在吞吐量和响应速度之间取得平衡。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.36,1:01:02.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then there's this new class of applications that actually want very, very fast results.\N然后还有这一类全新的应用，它们实际上需要非常非常快速的结果。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:02.66,1:01:05.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have extremely smart engineers and they don't like to wait.\N你有极其聪明的工程师，他们不喜欢等待。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:06.28,1:01:10.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that is where ultra-low latency or every millisecond actually matters.\N这正是超低延迟发挥作用的地方，每一毫秒都至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:11.72,1:01:15.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these types of workloads requires a different type of compute.\N这些不同类型的工作负载需要不同类型的计算。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:16.38,1:01:21.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of the best ways to reach ultra-low latency today is disaggregated inference.\N如今实现超低延迟的最佳方式之一是解耦推理。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:22.22,1:01:28.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you think about the different pieces, both prefill and decode are two different jobs.\N所以你如果考虑各个组成部分，预填充和解码是两个不同的任务。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:28.72,1:01:30.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So prefill tends to need more compute.\N因此，预填充通常需要更多的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:31.56,1:01:33.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Decode tends to need more memory bandwidth.\N解码通常需要更高的内存带宽。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:34.10,1:01:40.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with Instinct, we have a very balanced machine so that we deliver both great compute and great memory bandwidth.\N而使用Instinct，我们打造了一台非常均衡的机器，能够同时提供出色的计算能力和出色的内存带宽。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:40.84,1:01:42.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you can actually take this a step further.\N但实际上，你可以更进一步。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:42.86,1:01:49.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you know what workloads you're trying to run, you can actually let customers tune each of these pieces independently.\N如果你知道自己要运行的工作负载，实际上可以让客户独立调整这些各个部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:49.94,1:01:54.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to address this market opportunity, we've been working with Cerebras.\N为把握这一市场机遇，我们一直在与Cerebras合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:54.70,1:02:01.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to talk more about what we're building together, please welcome to the stage Cerebras co-founder and CEO Andrew Feldman.\N接下来，让我们欢迎Cerebras联合创始人兼CEO安德鲁·菲尔德曼上台，进一步聊聊我们共同打造的产品。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:10.33,1:02:11.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Andrew, it's great to have you here.\N安德鲁，欢迎你来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:11.95,1:02:14.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's been an exciting few months for you.\N这几个月对你来说一定非常激动人心。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:14.47,1:02:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know that for those who don't know exactly what you've been working on,\N我知道，对于那些还不清楚你具体在做什么的人，
Dialogue: 0,1:02:18.59,1:02:22.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,can you talk a little bit about Cerebras and what problem you've been trying to solve?\N你能简单介绍一下Cerebras，以及你们正在解决什么问题吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:02:23.05,1:02:27.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure. Great to be here and great to be sort of among people who love hardware.\N当然。很高兴来到这里，也很高兴能和一群热爱硬件的人在一起。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:28.81,1:02:30.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes, it's nice.\N是的，这很棒。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:30.65,1:02:37.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Look, I'm thrilled to be here with you and to announce our cool new partnership.\N看，我很高兴能和你们在一起，并宣布我们全新的酷合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:37.87,1:02:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,At Cerebras, we build the world's largest and fastest chip.\N在 Cerebras，我们打造世界上最大、最快的大芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:42.33,1:02:43.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a full wafer.\N这是一整片晶圆。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.81,1:02:52.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we package this into a system into racks and then racks into clusters.\N我们将它封装成系统，再装进机架，然后机架组成集群。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.51,1:02:56.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we deliver them both on-premise and via the cloud.\N我们既提供本地部署，也通过云服务交付。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:57.69,1:03:00.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you've had some of our customers up here already today.\N今天你们已经见过我们的一些客户了。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:01.25,1:03:13.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the Frontier Labs, we serve customers like OpenAI and in the hyperscalers like AWS, in the small agentic and the coding space, leaders like Cognition.\N在 Frontier 实验室，我们服务的客户包括 OpenAI，以及 AWS 这样的超大规模云服务商，还有在小型代理和编程领域中的领军企业，比如 Cognition。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:13.75,1:03:18.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they do this because we're blisteringly fast.\N他们选择我们，是因为我们速度惊人。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.79,1:03:25.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's no question, Andrew, that you have some tremendous innovation with what you've been working on.\N安德鲁，毫无疑问，你在所做项目上的创新非常了不起。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:25.65,1:03:34.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And our teams have been collaborating really closely over the last few years to really have Helios together with the wafer scale engine for ultra low latency inference.\N过去几年里，我们的团队紧密合作，终于将 Helios 与晶圆级引擎结合，实现了超低延迟推理。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:35.15,1:03:37.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you just kind of just educate the audience a little bit?\N你能稍微给观众讲一下吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:37.63,1:03:39.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,What are we trying to do and what does that mean for customers?\N我们正在尝试做什么，这对客户意味着什么？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:39.99,1:03:44.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure, I think what's happened, and you described it previously,\N当然，我认为发生的情况是，正如你之前描述的那样，
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.53,1:03:51.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,is that sort of AI has moved from being a novelty to being useful and then in some domains a necessity.\N人工智能已经从一种新奇事物转变为有用工具，而在某些领域甚至成为必需品。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:52.19,1:03:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when something is a necessity, people want to use it and they want to use it quickly.\N当某样东西成为必需品时，人们就希望使用它，并且希望快速使用。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.91,1:04:09.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to serve this market, this segment of ultra low latency, we sought a partnership that could extend our capabilities and our footprint.\N为了服务这个超低延迟的市场细分领域，我们寻求了一项能扩展我们能力与覆盖范围的合作伙伴关系。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:09.05,1:04:10.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And there was no better answer than AMD.\N没有比 AMD 更合适的答案了。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:11.51,1:04:17.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were already an AMD customer as we use AMD CPUs to surround our systems.\N我们原本就是 AMD 的客户，因为我们使用 AMD 的 CPU 来构建我们的系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:18.11,1:04:32.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we were so excited at the opportunity to build a disaggregated solution that combined AMD CPUs, the cool new Helios rack and the cerebrus wafer scale engine.\N我们非常兴奋能有机会打造一个解耦解决方案，将 AMD 的 CPU、全新的 Helios 机架以及 Cerebrus 芯片级封装引擎结合在一起。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:33.19,1:04:36.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, look, the technology is pretty cool.\N是的，这技术确实很酷。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:36.27,1:04:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So just talk a little bit about how it comes together.\N那就简单说一下它是如何整合在一起的。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:38.67,1:04:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure. So as Lisa described, what you have with Instinct and the Helios rack is that you have the leader in performance and memory capacity.\N好的。正如丽莎所描述的，Instinct 和 Helios 机架的组合，意味着你拥有了性能和内存容量的领导者。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:50.13,1:04:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you marry that with our wafer scale engine, which is the leader in sort of in SRAM and in memory bandwidth.\N再与我们的芯片级封装引擎结合，后者在 SRAM 和内存带宽方面处于领先地位。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:58.49,1:05:04.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that combination allows us to deliver a solution that is unmatched in the industry.\N这种组合使我们能够提供业界无与伦比的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:04.95,1:05:05.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very, very exciting.\N非常非常令人兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:06.05,1:05:08.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know that customers are excited about what we're going to do together as well.\N我知道客户也对我们将要共同完成的事情充满期待。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:09.33,1:05:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when are we going to have it in market?\N那么我们什么时候才能在市场上看到它？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:12.95,1:05:13.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Later this year.\N今年晚些时候。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:14.29,1:05:23.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will be first in the cerebrus cloud and it will be later at a store near you.\N它将首先在Cerebrus云中推出，随后很快就会在您附近的门店上线。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:25.23,1:05:32.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the key thing is we're going to give customers a choice to really put together what is the solution that they want.\N我认为关键在于，我们将为客户提供选择，真正让他们打造自己想要的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:32.85,1:05:35.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think we're very, very happy to be able to do this together with you.\N我认为我们非常高兴能与你们一起实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.69,1:05:40.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think it's a huge step up in terms of what we can do for this ultra low latency segment.\N所以我认为，这在应对超低延迟领域方面是一个巨大的飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:40.83,1:05:41.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's right.\N我认为没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:41.65,1:05:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think until recently, customers sort of, they could have sort of high throughput or they could have extraordinary speed.\N我认为直到最近，客户只能在高吞吐量和超高速之间二选一。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:50.65,1:05:56.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And by bringing together the Helios rack with the cerebrus wafer scale engine,\N通过将Helios机架与Cerebrus晶圆级引擎结合在一起，
Dialogue: 0,1:05:56.73,1:06:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,we give you five times the throughput while continuing to deliver this extraordinary speed.\N我们在保持卓越速度的同时，将吞吐量提升了五倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:03.79,1:06:07.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really something amazing.\N这真的令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:07.81,1:06:08.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Fantastic.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:08.01,1:06:12.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, look, Andrew, huge congratulations to what you and the Cerebras team have done.\N嗯，安德鲁，恭喜你和Cerebras团队所取得的成就。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:12.63,1:06:13.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, I think it's been incredible.\N我觉得这简直难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:13.85,1:06:17.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think you've been clear on what you're trying to accomplish.\N我认为你很清楚自己想要实现的目标。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:17.43,1:06:25.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's really nice to see not only it come together, but us come together to offer a solution that will be very, very compelling to customers.\N看到它最终成型，也看到我们携手合作，提供一个对客户极具吸引力的解决方案，这感觉非常好。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:25.33,1:06:27.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can't wait to get this into customers' hands.\N我们迫不及待想把产品交到客户手中。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:27.79,1:06:29.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Soon. Thank you.\N不久之后。谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:29.19,1:06:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good to see you.\N很高兴见到你。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:29.63,1:06:30.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.\N非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.47,1:06:30.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Andrew.\N谢谢你，安德鲁。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.24,1:06:36.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alright.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.18,1:06:40.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So look, I think we've shown you a lot of hardware this morning.\N所以，我想我们今天早上已经向大家展示了大量的硬件。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:41.30,1:06:43.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,But as we all know, hardware is only part of the story.\N但正如我们所知，硬件只是故事的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:44.26,1:06:49.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's actually software that turns all of this into a platform that developers can really build on.\N真正让这一切变成开发者可以真正基于其构建的平台的，其实是软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:49.82,1:06:56.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to share the progress we're making with ROCm, please welcome AMD Senior Vice President of AI, Vamsi Boppana, to the stage.\N为了分享我们在 ROCm 方面取得的进展，请欢迎 AMD 人工智能高级副总裁瓦姆西·博帕纳登台。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:03.87,1:07:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Lisa.\N谢谢，丽莎。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:04.81,1:07:05.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good morning, everyone.\N大家早上好。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:06.35,1:07:06.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good morning.\N早上好。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:07.41,1:07:09.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's great to be back to talk about software.\N很高兴再次来谈论软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:09.75,1:07:16.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just a few years ago, programming AMD GPUs required deep expertise and significant engineering effort.\N几年前，编程 AMD 显卡需要深厚的专业知识和大量的工程投入。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:17.15,1:07:21.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've come a long, long way in a remarkably short period of time.\N我们在短短的很短时间内，已经走了很长一段路。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:21.37,1:07:31.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Through our open source community collaboration and sustained investment in ROCm, our software stack, AMD Instinct GPUs are powering some of the most\N通过我们开源社区的合作以及对 ROCm 的持续投入，我们的软件栈使 AMD Instinct 显卡正在推动一些最
Dialogue: 0,1:07:31.29,1:07:34.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,important and consequential workloads on the planet.\N地球上最重要且影响深远的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:35.33,1:07:38.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the biggest change is still ahead of us.\N但最大的变革仍在未来等待着我们。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:38.53,1:07:46.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI is transforming how software is getting built, and we are bringing that transformation to ROCm.\N人工智能正在改变软件的构建方式，而我们正将这一变革带到 ROCm。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:46.59,1:07:48.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's what I'm excited to share with you guys today.\N这就是我今天想与大家分享的内容。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:49.69,1:07:53.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our software teams have been moving fast with relentless focus on developers.\N我们的软件团队一直以极快的速度推进，始终专注于开发者。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:54.33,1:08:00.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've invested at every level of the stack in build and test infrastructure so we ship faster.\N我们在堆栈的每个层面都投入了资源，完善构建和测试基础设施，以实现更快的交付。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:01.27,1:08:06.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,ROCm releases now go out every six weeks, not every four months.\NROCm 现在每六周发布一次，而不是每四个月一次。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:06.01,1:08:10.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've continued to expand the work we do with our AI ecosystem partners.\N我们持续扩大与 AI 生态合作伙伴的合作范围。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:11.17,1:08:11.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the result?\N结果如何？
Dialogue: 0,1:08:12.65,1:08:18.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,More features, faster performance, and a significantly better out-of-the-box experience.\N功能更多，性能更快，开箱即用的体验显著提升。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:19.29,1:08:23.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our strategy that has gotten us here has been remarkably consistent.\N带领我们走到今天的战略，一直非常一致。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.35,1:08:25.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's built on two core principles.\N它建立在两个核心原则之上。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:27.37,1:08:35.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Partner deeply with the open source ecosystem and build with the right layers of abstraction to enable developer productivity.\N与开源生态系统深度合作，构建合适的抽象层级，以提升开发人员的生产力。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:35.05,1:08:42.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Open source gives us velocity and scale, and abstraction makes developers more productive.\N开源赋予我们速度与规模，而抽象则让开发人员更加高效。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.21,1:08:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our deep, deep commitment to open source has resonated with the community that has truly embraced AMD.\N我们对开源的深切承诺已深深打动社区，AMD也真正获得了社区的接纳。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:51.21,1:08:55.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,From frameworks and compiler stacks to inference engines and model hubs,\N从框架和编译器栈，到推理引擎和模型库，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.07,1:09:06.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,AMD is now becoming part of default enablement for the most important AI communities, such as Hugging Face, PyTorch, JAX, vLLM, and SGLang.\NAMD如今已成为最重要的AI社区（如Hugging Face、PyTorch、JAX、vLLM和SGLang）的默认支持平台。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:07.51,1:09:14.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is why new models get Day Zero support and why the world's most important AI workloads run on AMD today.\N这正是新模型能获得Day Zero支持的原因，也是当今全球最重要的AI工作负载运行在AMD上的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:14.95,1:09:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is a big shift.\N这是一个巨大的转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:17.93,1:09:24.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Inspired by engineers seeking productivity, abstractions have evolved to enable work at the right level of detail.\N受追求生产力的工程师启发，抽象层级不断演进，使人们能够在合适的细节层次上开展工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:24.61,1:09:31.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hiding complexity when they want speed, and exposing control when they need performance.\N需要速度时隐藏复杂性，需要性能时则暴露控制权。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:31.83,1:09:40.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,From low-level programming in assembly and C to block programming abstractions like Triton to Pythonic frameworks, we've invested in key abstractions.\N从汇编和C语言的底层编程，到Triton等块级编程抽象，再到Python风格的框架，我们已在关键抽象上投入大量资源。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.79,1:09:49.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Aiter, our kernel library, and Atom, our serving engine, get you peak performance without writing the kernels yourself.\NAiter是我们自己的内核库，Atom是我们的推理引擎，无需自行编写内核即可获得峰值性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:51.23,1:09:59.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,FlyDSL is a brand new Pythonic domain-specific language that gives you low-level control with the performance of hand-tuned C++.\NFlyDSL是一种全新的Python风格领域特定语言，让你在获得手调C++性能的同时，拥有底层控制力。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:00.37,1:10:07.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Mori, our communications library, helps deliver leadership performance on the latest models, like Minimax.\N而且，我们的通信库Mori，帮助我们在最新模型（如Minimax）上实现卓越的领导力表现。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:09.79,1:10:12.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,But look, something very, very exciting is happening.\N但看吧，正在发生一件非常、非常令人兴奋的事。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:13.43,1:10:16.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Over the past year, I've seen something remarkable inside AMD.\N过去一年里，我在AMD内部见证了一些非凡的进展。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:16.59,1:10:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our engineers are using AI models to generate GPU kernels, optimize code, debug issues, and improve performance.\N我们的工程师正在使用AI模型生成GPU内核、优化代码、调试问题并提升性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:25.05,1:10:29.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in some cases, these AI-generated kernels are shockingly good.\N在某些情况下，这些由AI生成的内核表现得令人震惊。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:29.93,1:10:31.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Better than what we expected.\N比我们预期的还要好。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:31.91,1:10:35.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sometimes better than the most manually-tuned versions.\N有时甚至优于那些手工精心调优的版本。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:36.13,1:10:38.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first time you see this, you're a little bit skeptical.\N第一次看到这种情况时，你难免会有些怀疑。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:39.43,1:10:46.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,You run more tests, you try to break it, you look for what went wrong, and then you realize this is real.\N你会进行更多测试，试图找出问题，寻找出错的地方，然后才意识到这确实是真实的。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:46.33,1:10:53.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,What has happened in general software development is coming to significantly transform GPU programming.\N通用软件开发中发生的变化，正在显著改变GPU编程。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:54.11,1:11:03.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to reduce the time it takes to bring up workloads, make optimization automated, and it will remove any remaining barriers to broad adoption.\N这将缩短部署工作负载所需的时间，实现优化自动化，并消除广泛采用的任何剩余障碍。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:04.63,1:11:09.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want to put that capability in the hands of every developer.\N我们希望将这种能力赋予每一位开发者。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:09.85,1:11:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So today, I am excited to introduce ROCm.ai.\N今天，我非常激动地向大家介绍 ROCm.ai。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:22.21,1:11:28.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's an agentic AI platform that brings the capabilities of AI-assisted GPU programming to developers.\N它是一个智能AI平台，将AI辅助GPU编程的能力带给开发者。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:29.15,1:11:37.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,It starts with the simple idea of giving developers access to the power of an AMD ecosystem through the AI coding agents they already use.\N这个平台始于一个简单理念：让开发者通过他们已使用的AI编码代理，访问AMD生态系统的强大能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:37.69,1:11:50.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whether you're using Cursor, Claude, Codex, rocm.ai helps those agents understand AMD platforms, understand ROCm, and helps you build and optimize your workloads.\N无论你使用的是 Cursor、Claude、Codex，ROCm.ai 都能帮助这些代理理解AMD平台、理解ROCm，并帮助你构建和优化工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:50.85,1:11:56.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,In other words, we are making those popular coding agents into ROCm super users.\N换句话说，我们正在把那些流行的编码代理变成ROCm的超级用户。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:57.17,1:12:03.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,You should be able to describe the workload you want to run, the performance target you want to hit, and then let the agents help you get there.\N你应该能够描述你想要运行的工作负载、想要达到的性能目标，然后让这些代理帮你实现。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:04.91,1:12:08.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,For years, we have been building the open software foundation.\N多年来，我们一直在构建开放软件基础。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:09.03,1:12:16.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we are adding an AI-assisted layer that helps developers use that foundation faster and more effectively.\N现在，我们增加了一个AI辅助层，帮助开发者更快、更高效地使用这一基础。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:16.79,1:12:19.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let me show you what is inside ROCm.ai.\N那么，让我来展示一下ROCm.ai内部都有什么。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:20.33,1:12:30.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's built on the foundational capabilities of ROCm, our core software stack, runtime, libraries, compilers, tools, framework integration, all of the\N它建立在ROCm的基础能力之上，包括我们核心的软件栈、运行时、库、编译器、工具、框架集成，以及所有让这一栈正常运行的核心软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:30.73,1:12:32.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,core software that makes the stack work.\N核心软件使整个栈得以运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.45,1:12:39.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,On top of that, we built a layer of AI-assisted optimization called Hyperloom.\N在此基础上，我们构建了一个名为Hyperloom的AI辅助优化层。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:40.13,1:12:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Using Hyperloom, the system can analyze the workload, tune configurations,\N通过 Hyperloom，系统可以分析工作负载，调整配置，
Dialogue: 0,1:12:45.33,1:12:50.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,select and tune kernels, adjust parallelism strategies, and iterate towards performance goals.\N选择并优化内核，调整并行策略，并迭代以达成性能目标。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:51.61,1:12:57.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,To give you an example of the power of Hyperloom, I was talking to the lead developer last week.\N举个 Hyperloom 能力的例子，我上周和首席开发人员聊过。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:57.25,1:13:06.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,He told me they just pushed through a suite of 14,000 models through Hyperloom, optimizing them and creating valuable insights.\N他告诉我，他们刚刚通过 Hyperloom 推送了 14,000 个模型，进行了优化并获得了有价值的洞察。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:06.59,1:13:12.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,This would have been impossible to imagine, even with a large team of engineers before.\N即使在拥有大量工程师团队的情况下，这在过去也是难以想象的。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:12.57,1:13:13.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's the power of Hyperloom.\N这就是 Hyperloom 的力量。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:14.89,1:13:23.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And finally, we provide an AI-native interface for our developers, AI skills that allow coding agents to understand ROCm natively.\N最后，我们为开发者提供了原生 AI 接口，具备 AI 技能，使编码代理能够原生理解 ROCm。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:23.01,1:13:27.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm incredibly excited by what we have built with rocm.ai.\N我对与 rocm.ai 一起打造的成果感到无比兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.49,1:13:31.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to profoundly transform the way developers interact with our platforms.\N它将深刻改变开发者与我们平台互动的方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:32.63,1:13:34.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let me make this concrete for you with an example.\N让我用一个例子来具体说明。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:35.89,1:13:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Imagine you are a developer who wants to optimize Minimax M3 with vLLM on MI355s.\N想象你是一名开发者，想要在 MI355s 上使用 vLLM 优化 Minimax M3。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:42.41,1:13:45.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, there are many things you need to get right.\N今天，你需要掌握许多细节才能成功。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:45.57,1:13:50.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need the right vLLM optimizations, the right model recipes, the right environment variables.\N你需要正确的 vLLM 优化、正确的模型配方和正确的环境变量。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:50.87,1:13:56.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,You may need to write new kernels or optimize kernels, and then you still need to tune all of this.\N你可能需要编写新的内核或优化内核，然后仍然需要对所有这些进行调优。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:57.25,1:14:01.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,With rocm.ai, this interaction becomes much simpler.\N使用 rocm.ai，这种交互变得简单得多。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:02.61,1:14:03.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's see it.\N那么我们来看看。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:03.47,1:14:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can say, optimize Minimax M3 with Hyperloom.\N你可以输入：使用 Hyperloom 优化 Minimax M3。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:08.39,1:14:14.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Enter. And behind the scenes, the agent does what an expert would do.\N按下回车。后台，代理会像专家一样操作。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:15.77,1:14:18.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pulls a known good recipe, runs and profiles the workload.\N调用一个已知可靠的配方，运行并分析工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:18.83,1:14:24.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It creates and tests a bunch of kernel and runtime configurations, and it keeps iterating towards target.\N它会创建并测试大量内核和运行时配置，并持续迭代以达到目标。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:25.97,1:14:30.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can actually watch on screen here rocm.ai write a GPU kernel.\N你实际上可以在这里看到 rocm.ai 编写 GPU 内核的过程。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:31.13,1:14:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,It sees an opportunity to write a more optimized MOE group gem.\N它发现了一个机会，可以编写一个更优化的 MOE 组 gem。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:35.89,1:14:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the result?\N结果如何？
Dialogue: 0,1:14:37.39,1:14:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,rocm.ai delivers a 38% more tokens per second improvement on this specific example.\Nrocm.ai 在这个具体示例中实现了每秒多处理 38% 词元的提升。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:45.11,1:14:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the experience we want for developers.\N这正是我们希望开发者获得的体验。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:47.63,1:14:49.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Simple to start.\N开始使用非常简单。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:52.24,1:14:53.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's pretty cool, huh?\N这挺酷的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:14:57.64,1:15:00.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Simple, simple to start and powerful to optimize.\N简单易上手，强大易优化。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:00.74,1:15:03.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've continued our relentless focus and performance.\N我们持续专注于性能提升。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:03.92,1:15:07.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,With every release, we've delivered significant performance gains.\N每次发布都带来了显著的性能提升。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:07.92,1:15:14.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,On leading models like DeepSeek, rocm.ai delivers 3.3 times speed up over ROCm 7.\N在 DeepSeek 等领先模型上，rocm.ai 相比 ROCm 7 实现了 3.3 倍的加速。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:14.94,1:15:18.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,This has been made possible by innovations at every level of the stack.\N这得益于整个技术栈各层面的创新。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:18.26,1:15:26.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Techniques such as the use of block-scaled fused MOE kernels, KV cache quantization, export parallelism.\N诸如使用块缩放融合 MOE 内核、KV 缓存量化、导出并行等技术。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:26.92,1:15:31.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,But look, the bigger story is how AI agents actually profiled the workload,\N但更值得关注的是，AI 代理实际上对工作负载进行了分析，
Dialogue: 0,1:15:31.48,1:15:35.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,proposed new kernels, tested configurations, and actually validated all of the results.\N提出了新的内核，测试了配置，并验证了所有结果。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:37.36,1:15:41.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,That exact same focus is also on delivering performance gains for training.\N这种同样的专注也体现在训练性能的提升上。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:42.70,1:15:48.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the same hardware, rocm.ai improves training performance by an average of 2.4 times.\N在相同硬件上，rocm.ai 将训练性能平均提升了 2.4 倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:48.24,1:15:55.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Through optimized kernels such as fused flash attention, more efficient checkpointing, and advanced parallelism strategies.\N通过优化的内核，例如融合闪存注意力、更高效的检查点机制以及先进的并行策略。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:57.32,1:16:03.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our engineers have done amazing work to unlock the capabilities of MI455 through rocm.ai.\N我们的工程师通过 rocm.ai 完成了令人惊叹的工作，充分释放了 MI455 的潜力。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:04.06,1:16:07.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I'm delighted to share some incredible results on hardware.\N因此，我很高兴能与大家分享一些在硬件上的惊人成果。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:08.04,1:16:17.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,On running real workloads, we are able to see the system deliver 20 terabytes of memory bandwidth and 20 petaflops of delivered compute.\N在运行真实工作负载时，我们能够看到系统实现了 20TB/s 的内存带宽和 20PFLOPS 的实际计算性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:17.66,1:16:26.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are the highest demonstrated compute plus memory capabilities of any accelerator platform in the industry today.\N这是目前行业内任何加速平台所展示出的最高计算与内存能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:27.10,1:16:28.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not theoretical, there's measured.\N这并非理论推测，而是实测数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:35.38,1:16:37.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Super exciting that we were able to share this on day one.\N我们能在第一天就分享这些成果，令人无比激动。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:38.64,1:16:46.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm also thrilled to share that the leading AI ecosystem partners who have had their hands on MI455 have had a delightful experience.\N我还非常高兴地宣布，那些已经接触过 MI455 的领先 AI 生态合作伙伴，都体验到了令人愉悦的使用感受。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:46.42,1:16:49.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can see here what they've had to say.\N你们可以在这里看到他们的真实反馈。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:49.74,1:16:57.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,From end-to-end PyTorch testing, to ensuring Hugging Face models are getting validated, to vLLM and SGLang running well on MI455.\N从端到端的 PyTorch 测试，到确保 Hugging Face 模型得到验证，再到 vLLM 和 SGLang 在 MI455 上运行良好。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:58.68,1:17:04.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are incredibly encouraged and excited by what the community is about to unlock with MI455.\N我们对社区即将通过 MI455 实现的突破感到无比鼓舞和兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:05.28,1:17:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,This matters because day zero readiness is one of the most important objectives we strive for, and that's what rocm.ai enables.\N这很重要，因为零日就绪是我们努力追求的最重要目标之一，而 rocm.ai 正是实现这一点的关键。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:13.68,1:17:17.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now let's look at rocm.ai in action on Helios.\N现在让我们看看 rocm.ai 在 Helios 上的实际运行情况。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:18.16,1:17:20.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,This time we are going to use a Codex front end.\N这次我们将使用一个 Codex 前端。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:21.30,1:17:27.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's deploy DeepSeek V4 Pro, a 1.6 trillion parameter frontier model on Helios.\N我们在 Helios 上部署 DeepSeek V4 Pro，这是一个拥有 1.6 万亿参数的前沿模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:28.46,1:17:29.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now watch what happens.\N现在请看发生了什么。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:31.40,1:17:42.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,rocm.ai pulls the right recipes, it configures the runtime, it implements the model graph onto hardware, and finally serves up the model.\Nrocm.ai 自动调用合适的配置方案，配置运行时环境，将模型图映射到硬件，并最终提供模型服务。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:43.19,1:17:44.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,There you go.\N看到了吗。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:44.90,1:17:46.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,The model is actually up and running.\N模型实际上已经启动并运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:47.32,1:17:51.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And let's see the model write a simple poem now about advancing AI.\N现在让我们看看模型如何写一首关于推进 AI 的简单诗歌。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:52.78,1:17:53.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's hit enter.\N我们按下回车键。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:55.40,1:17:56.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isn't that a pretty cool poem?\N这首诗是不是很酷？
Dialogue: 0,1:18:02.07,1:18:04.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the experience we want to give our users.\N这正是我们希望为用户带来的体验。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:04.93,1:18:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The developers should not have to manually reason through every layer of model architecture, kernel selection, COM strategy, and rack level deployment.\N开发人员不应再手动分析模型架构的每一层、内核选择、COM 策略以及机架级部署的细节。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:13.55,1:18:20.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI is transforming this experience, and that is a very, very big shift for GPU hardware and software.\N人工智能正在改变这一体验，这对 GPU 硬件和软件而言是一次非常巨大的转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:22.33,1:18:27.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, there are few organizations shaping the frontier of AI as much as OpenAI.\N目前，很少有组织能像 OpenAI 一样推动人工智能的前沿发展。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:27.45,1:18:30.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,You heard Lisa and Sachin talk about our partnership.\N你们已经听到丽莎和萨钦谈过我们的合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:30.79,1:18:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's been truly wonderful collaborating closely with the OpenAI technical team to make rapid progress with ROCm.\N与 OpenAI 技术团队紧密合作，推动 ROCm 快速进展，这真的非常令人愉快。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:37.71,1:18:47.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,To talk about how they are advancing the frontier of software development and our collaboration, I'm delighted to welcome to stage Philippe Tillet from OpenAI.\N为了探讨他们如何推进软件开发的前沿以及我们的合作，我非常高兴地邀请 OpenAI 的菲利普·蒂勒登台。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:56.04,1:18:57.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for joining us here, Philippe.\N欢迎你来到这里，菲利普。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:58.76,1:19:06.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So just so you all know, Philippe is the creator of Triton, one of the most important software innovations in modern AI infrastructure.\N请大家知道，菲利普是 Triton 的创造者，这是现代人工智能基础设施中最重要的软件创新之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:06.28,1:19:07.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a huge privilege having you here.\N你能来到这里，我们深感荣幸。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:08.16,1:19:08.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:12.64,1:19:15.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,OpenAI has always pushed the limits of infrastructure.\NOpenAI 一直都在推动基础设施的极限。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:16.68,1:19:24.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you tell the team a little bit here today as to how your team actually develops GPU software and how have technologies like Triton evolved?\N那么今天你能向团队简单介绍一下你们团队是如何开发 GPU 软件的，以及像 Triton 这样的技术是如何演进的吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:19:25.08,1:19:25.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,For sure.\N当然可以。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:25.52,1:19:27.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, first of all, thanks so much for having me.\N首先，非常感谢邀请我。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:27.92,1:19:29.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was here two years ago.\N我两年前来过这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:29.08,1:19:30.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's my great pleasure to be back now.\N如今再次回到这里，我感到非常荣幸。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:32.36,1:19:40.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,A way of looking at things is there's no one way to fit all applications, and we really try to meet users where they are.\N一种看待问题的方式是，没有一种通用方案适用于所有应用，我们真正努力的是在用户所在的位置满足他们的需求。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:40.02,1:19:43.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for that reason, we've developed multiple solutions.\N因此，我们开发了多种解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:43.92,1:19:50.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for workflows where speed of iterations is more important, we've developed Triton, as you mentioned.\N对于迭代速度更为重要的工作流，我们开发了 Triton，正如你提到的那样。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:50.24,1:19:52.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is typically what researchers will use.\N这通常是研究人员会使用的方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:53.34,1:20:00.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,But more and more, we've been in a case where we've had to hyper-optimize performance, and Triton didn't give us the level of control that we wanted.\N但越来越多的情况下，我们不得不对性能进行超优化，而 Triton 并未提供我们所期望的控制程度。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:00.98,1:20:04.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we've developed Glion for that, which is a lower-level language.\N因此我们开发了 Glion，这是一种更低层级的语言。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:05.56,1:20:10.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this way, we've been really able to optimize our kernels for AMD, among other things.\N通过这种方式，我们真正实现了对 AMD 等平台的内核优化。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:13.50,1:20:19.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our agents have become extremely good at both of them, and we've worked with AMD on both of them as well.\N我们的代理在两者上都变得极为出色，我们也与 AMD 在这两者上都有合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:21.80,1:20:26.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,More and more, what we're seeing is agents slowly taking over.\N越来越多的情况下，我们看到的是代理程序正在逐步接管。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:27.88,1:20:31.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're getting just very good, as you just mentioned, at writing this kind of code.\N正如你刚才提到的，它们在编写这类代码方面变得非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:31.28,1:20:32.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Amazing.\N惊人。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:32.74,1:20:39.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So look, I think the work you have done with Triton and now Glion, it's been really, really moving the ball forward for the entire industry.\N所以，我认为你之前在 Triton 上的工作，以及现在在 Glion 上的工作，真的极大地推动了整个行业的发展。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:40.02,1:20:47.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we began our work together with 300 and extended at 350, but now we're collaborating at a different scale with 450 and Helios.\N我们最初是与 300 合作，后来扩展到 350，但现在我们正以全新的规模与 450 和 Helios 合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:48.24,1:20:53.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I would love to hear your thoughts on how that collaboration has been going, and how has that experience been?\N所以我很想听听你对这次合作进展的看法，以及你的体验如何？
Dialogue: 0,1:20:53.98,1:20:54.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, super well.\N非常顺利。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:54.94,1:20:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,It feels like ages.\N感觉已经过了很久。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:56.80,1:21:00.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we started years ago on hardware co-design.\N我认为我们多年前就开始了硬件协同设计。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:00.36,1:21:10.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, when MI450 was in the very early prototyping stages, I think we were able to work really well together, and it's so nice to see the outcome of that and the\N当 MI450 还处于非常早期的原型阶段时，我们就已经能够很好地协作，现在看到成果，真是太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:10.74,1:21:21.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,chip. And more recently, we've been working very, very deeply on software enablement for MI450, both for our models, but also for the broader ecosystem.\N最近，我们还在 MI450 的软件赋能方面进行了非常深入的合作，不仅针对我们的模型，也面向更广泛的生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:21.74,1:21:24.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a lot of this development has been done open source.\N因此，大量开发工作都是以开源形式完成的。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:25.42,1:21:38.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And yeah, we're collaborating on the full stack now, down to the very low-level LLVM code generation, so that all the nice hardware advances that came with MI450 can\N是的，我们现在正在全栈合作，深入到最底层的LLVM代码生成层面，以便充分利用MI450带来的所有硬件优势，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:38.26,1:21:40.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,be properly leveraged in end-to-end applications.\N在端到端的应用中得到充分应用。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:42.02,1:21:46.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and you got your Helios racks, so tell us a little bit about that.\N是的，你们有Helios机架，跟我们说说那方面的情况吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:46.72,1:21:47.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it worked.\N是的，它运行成功了。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:48.48,1:21:49.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got the chip,\N我们拿到了芯片，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:56.65,1:22:03.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,and very quickly, a single engineer in a few days was able to confirm that everything worked.\N很快，一名工程师在几天内就确认了所有功能都正常。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:03.25,1:22:05.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, we have to optimize performance more.\N当然，我们还需要进一步优化性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:06.29,1:22:09.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we're very confident we can get in a very, very good place.\N但我们非常有信心能取得非常出色的结果。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:09.93,1:22:10.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:10.37,1:22:11.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's awesome to hear.\N听到这个消息真是太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:11.79,1:22:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So look, one of the more amazing things that we've done recently is our teams have collaborated even more closely in terms of using AI to program AMD GPUs.\N说起来，我们最近做得最令人惊叹的一件事是，我们的团队在使用AI编程AMD显卡方面，合作得更加紧密了。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:22.57,1:22:25.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we'd love to hear your thoughts and anything you can share with the audience.\N所以我们很乐意听听您的看法，以及您能与观众分享的任何内容。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:25.85,1:22:35.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, no, I mean, everyone in this room knows how much agents are taking over our jobs, in a sense, as kernel engineers.\N是的，我的意思是，在座的每个人都知道，智能体正在以某种方式逐渐取代我们这些内核工程师的工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:38.57,1:22:45.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's been amazing just to see how much better they've got over just the past six months.\N仅仅过去六个月，它们的进步就令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:45.45,1:22:50.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just now, they're extremely good at generating high-quality GPU kernels in a way that were not before.\N而现在，它们在生成高质量GPU内核方面表现得极为出色，这是以前做不到的。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:51.63,1:23:04.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's been very great collaborating with AMD on just making sure that agents not only are capable enough, but also have all the right context they need to be able\N与AMD合作，确保智能体不仅能力足够，还能获得所有必要的上下文信息，从而做出良好决策和优化，这感觉非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:04.53,1:23:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,to make good decisions and good optimizations.\N这感觉非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:07.41,1:23:08.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's great to hear.\N听起来太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:08.33,1:23:17.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the quality of code that's getting produced by AI-assisted kernel generation has been truly remarkable through our collaboration.\N我认为，通过我们的合作，AI辅助的内核生成所产出的代码质量确实令人瞩目。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:17.47,1:23:18.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very excited.\N非常令人兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:18.01,1:23:27.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, as you look ahead, what crystal ball do you have for us for the future of AI software ecosystem and collaborations like ours?\N现在，展望未来，您对AI软件生态系统的未来以及像我们这样的合作有什么预测吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:23:28.17,1:23:31.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so there's two things that really come to mind.\N是的，有两件事让我印象特别深刻。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:31.37,1:23:36.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,One, as we keep talking, is just how good agents are getting.\N一个是，随着我们持续交流，智能体的能力正在变得越来越强。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:36.83,1:23:46.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the other one is, I think, how much the open approach to software of AMD is enabling, not only for OpenAI, but I think for the industry as a whole.\N另一个则是，我认为AMD在软件上采取的开放策略，不仅为OpenAI，也为我们整个行业带来了巨大推动。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:46.25,1:23:50.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I talked a little bit earlier how we've been collaborating on LLVM co-generation.\N我刚才简单提到了我们如何在LLVM共同生成方面展开合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:51.23,1:23:53.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,LLVM is an open source project.\NLLVM是一个开源项目。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:53.51,1:23:56.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,The entire compiler stack from AMD is open source.\NAMD整个编译器栈都是开源的。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:56.97,1:24:05.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that has allowed us to make our agents really good at very, very low-level co-generation, down to scheduling instructions in assembly.\N这使我们能够将代理在非常非常底层的共同生成方面做到极致，甚至精确到汇编指令的调度。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:05.55,1:24:15.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this has led to very, very significant performance gain that I don't think we'd have been able to achieve in a fully closed source stack.\N这带来了极为显著的性能提升，我认为在完全闭源的架构下我们无法实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:15.15,1:24:20.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's one of the real sort of big value propositions that we have to offer,\N是的，这正是我们能提供的一大核心价值主张。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:21.09,1:24:27.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because everything that we do is in the open, and the fact that AI can actually right? pick that up is a big one.\N因为我们所做的每一件事都是公开的，而AI实际上能够利用这一点，这非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:27.03,1:24:27.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Philippe.\N谢谢你，菲利普。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:27.89,1:24:31.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We truly appreciate the partnership, and we're really excited about what we're going to build together.\N我们真心感谢这次合作，也非常期待我们共同打造的未来。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:32.27,1:24:32.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, my pleasure.\N我也很荣幸。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:32.97,1:24:33.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for having me.\N非常感谢您邀请我。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:39.39,1:24:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,What you just heard is extremely important.\N你们刚才听到的内容非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.39,1:24:51.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we combine better abstractions with AI-assisted development and closed hardware software co-design, we can create some incredibly powerful capabilities,\N当我们把更优的抽象技术与AI辅助开发及软硬件一体化设计相结合时，就能创造出一些极其强大的能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:51.81,1:24:54.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that's exactly aligned with our strategy.\N这正好符合我们的战略。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:55.39,1:25:04.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, everything I have shown you so far has been about AI, but ROCm is also a great stack for developing high-performance and scientific computing applications.\N到目前为止，我向你们展示的都是关于人工智能的内容，但 ROCm 也同样适用于开发高性能和科学计算应用。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:04.87,1:25:08.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,From frontier models to climate simulation, we use the same ROCm,\N从前沿模型到气候模拟，我们均采用相同的ROCm，
Dialogue: 0,1:25:09.21,1:25:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,the same library, same tools, same AI-assisted development, one open stack for every single workload.\N相同的库，相同的工具，相同的AI辅助开发，每个工作负载都使用一个开放的堆栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:15.43,1:25:22.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in fact, when you look at our roadmap, we have retained that very strong focus on HPC and scientific computing.\N事实上，查看我们的路线图就会发现，我们依然保持着对高性能计算和科学计算的高度重视。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:22.85,1:25:35.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just like MI455 leads in AI compute with FP4 and memory performance, MI430X leads HPC compute with FP64 and memory performance, two platforms purpose-built\N正如MI455凭借FP4和内存性能在AI计算领域领先，MI430X则凭借FP64和内存性能在高性能计算领域领先，这两款平台均为特定用途而打造。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:35.89,1:25:37.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,for two very different classes of workload.\N适用于两类截然不同的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:39.17,1:25:50.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,The MI430X is built by leveraging our modular chiplet architecture to deliver a purpose-built variant with native FP64 hardware, giving customers leadership\NMI430X 基于我们的模块化小芯片架构打造，提供具备原生 FP64 硬件的专用版本，为客户带来领先地位
Dialogue: 0,1:25:50.81,1:25:55.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,performance across AI and HPC in a single platform.\N单一平台上的人工智能与高性能计算性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:55.79,1:25:58.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is hardware double precision, not emulation.\N这是硬件双精度计算，而非模拟。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:59.89,1:26:02.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,For the scientific community, that distinction is everything.\N对科学界而言，这种区别至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:03.71,1:26:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,This product delivers 288 teraflops of FP64 compute, nearly nine times better than competition.\N该产品提供288万亿次FP64浮点计算性能，比竞争对手高出近九倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:10.63,1:26:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the same leadership, memory capacity, and bandwidth of MI455.\N同样具备MI455的领导地位、内存容量和带宽。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:16.91,1:26:21.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,The MI430X ships in the first half of 2027.\NMI430X将于2027年上半年出货。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:23.03,1:26:27.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is why leaders in sovereign AI love this product.\N这就是主权AI领域的领导者为何青睐此产品的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.11,1:26:34.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first sovereign exascale AI factories in both US and Europe are being built on the MI430X.\N美国和欧洲首个主权级艾克斯级AI工厂正基于MI430X建造。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:35.03,1:26:40.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Discovery at Oak Ridge National Labs and Alice Recoque with Cines and Genci in Europe.\N田纳西州橡树岭国家实验室的发现，以及欧洲Cines和Genci的Alice Recoque项目。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:42.07,1:26:45.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So look, as we look ahead, let me leave you with this thought.\N所以，展望未来，让我用这个想法与大家共勉。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:46.23,1:26:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every so often, our industry goes through inflection points.\N我们行业每隔一段时间就会经历转折点。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:50.61,1:26:58.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've all felt it when neural networks first started recognizing cats and dogs, when transformers changed what was possible with AI.\N当神经网络首次开始识别猫和狗时，当变换器架构改变了AI的可能边界时，我们都曾感受到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:58.53,1:27:07.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,I believe we are experiencing another one right now, a real inflection in the ability of AI to program complex hardware systems.\N我认为我们正经历另一个转折点，AI在编程复杂硬件系统方面的能力正在发生真正变革。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:08.07,1:27:19.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Building on the surface area that's been exposed from open source software and leveraging the power of abstracted interfaces, AI is making it dramatically easier to program AI systems.\N借助开源软件所暴露的表面积，以及抽象接口的强大能力，AI正使编程AI系统变得容易得多。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:20.57,1:27:23.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We cannot wait what you will build with it.\N我们迫不及待想看看你们将用它创造出什么。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:24.13,1:27:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:33.62,1:27:37.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, AI is getting pervasively infused into all forms of computing.\N现在，人工智能正被广泛融入各种计算形式中。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:37.84,1:27:41.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Enterprises are experiencing the same shift with their own unique requirements.\N企业也正经历着同样的转变，但有着各自独特的需求。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:42.52,1:27:53.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to tell us more about that transformation, please welcome to stage Senior Vice President and General Manager of Compute and Enterprise AI, Dan McNamara.\N为了让我们更深入了解这一转型，请欢迎英伟达计算与企业人工智能高级副总裁兼总经理丹·麦克纳马拉登台。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:00.53,1:28:03.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Vamsi, and good morning, everyone.\N谢谢瓦姆西，大家早上好。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:04.05,1:28:11.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a great pleasure for me to bring to you the third pillar of our strategy, which is powering AI everywhere.\N很荣幸能向大家介绍我们战略的第三大支柱，即赋能 everywhere 的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:11.33,1:28:16.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the vision behind this has remained the same for several years for us,\N这一愿景多年来一直保持不变，
Dialogue: 0,1:28:17.29,1:28:32.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,to deliver the right compute engine to the right workload, and then continuously drive optimization points across our entire portfolio, from CPUs, GPUs, networking, and FPGAs.\N为合适的任务匹配合适的计算引擎，并持续优化我们整个产品组合，涵盖 CPU、GPU、网络和 FPGA。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:33.13,1:28:43.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So building on what we've already shared, I'll cover how our strategy comes together across our enterprise portfolio and how the foundation we built with the CPU\N基于我们此前分享的内容，我将介绍我们的战略如何在企业产品组合中实现整合，以及我们以 CPU 业务为基础所建立的根基，
Dialogue: 0,1:28:43.31,1:28:50.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,franchise has truly positioned us for the next era of AI across multiple deployment models.\N如何真正让我们为多种部署模式下的下一阶段人工智能做好准备。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:51.51,1:29:00.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So Lisa talked about the frontier model and hyperscale landscape and just the rapid and massive advances we've seen over the last 6 to 12 months.\N丽莎谈到了前沿模型和超大规模场景，以及过去 6 到 12 个月我们所见证的快速而巨大的进步。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:01.57,1:29:05.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And those advances are driving the adoption of AI well beyond the cloud.\N这些进步正推动人工智能的采用远远超出云端。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:05.59,1:29:17.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as AI continues to grow, it will demand compute beyond the massive purpose-built data centers that we all know and love, extending into enterprise, personal, and physical AI.\N随着人工智能持续发展，其对算力的需求将超越我们所熟知和喜爱的大型专用数据中心，延伸至企业、个人和物理AI领域。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:17.35,1:29:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And each of these brings a new or unique set of requirements.\N而每一类都带来了新的或独特的算力需求。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:22.85,1:29:25.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Enterprises are usually constrained by power and cooling.\N企业通常受限于电力和散热能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:26.15,1:29:31.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Personal AI usually must operate within a fairly limited compute and memory footprint.\N个人AI通常必须在相对有限的算力和内存空间内运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:31.59,1:29:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And physical AI must perform reliably in real-world demanding environments.\N而物理AI必须在现实世界中严苛的环境中稳定运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:38.59,1:29:45.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And AMD is the only company delivering a complete portfolio that spans all of these development models.\N而AMD是唯一一家能够提供覆盖所有这些开发模式的完整产品组合的公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:46.67,1:29:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I just mentioned that our journey began in the data center with our CPU franchise, and I want to touch on it a bit.\N我刚才提到，我们的征程始于数据中心的CPU业务，我想稍作展开。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:53.77,1:29:58.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,With each generation of EPYC, our strategy has been to listen to our customers,\N每一代EPYC的策略都是倾听客户的声音，
Dialogue: 0,1:29:58.23,1:30:06.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,address their evolving needs, and deliver the highest performance, lowest total cost of ownership, and the fastest time to value.\N满足他们不断变化的需求，并提供最高性能、最低总体拥有成本以及最快的价值实现时间。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:07.65,1:30:16.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,As Lisa mentioned earlier, we've introduced many industry-firsts across our generations that our enterprise customer has actually asked for.\N正如丽莎之前提到的，我们在各代产品中推出了许多行业首创功能，这些正是企业客户所要求的。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:17.19,1:30:24.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that customer focus has brought us to where we are today, with EPYC as the leader in enterprise computing.\N正是这种以客户为中心的专注，让我们今天能够成为企业计算领域的领导者，EPYC稳居首位。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:24.55,1:30:32.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over the last three years, there's been very, very strong adoption across the enterprise, with the world's largest companies moving more and more workloads to AMD.\N过去三年里，企业领域的采用势头非常强劲，全球最大的企业正越来越多地将工作负载迁移至AMD。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:33.79,1:30:36.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's reflected in a number of places.\N而这一点在多个方面都有体现。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:36.23,1:30:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,First, public cloud, where our VM consumption has grown at 76% CAGR over the last three years.\N首先是在公共云领域，过去三年我们的虚拟机使用量年复合增长率达到了76%。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:43.37,1:30:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And on-prem deployments with our OEM and ODM partners is growing quite aggressively across key industries.\N在本地部署方面，通过我们的OEM和ODM合作伙伴，我们的业务在关键行业正迅速扩张。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:51.95,1:31:01.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,But just as important, this position allows us to understand truly the diversity of the workloads that our enterprise customers run every day.\N但同样重要的是，这一地位使我们能够真正理解企业客户每天运行的工作负载的多样性。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:03.11,1:31:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And each workload faces new demands on the CPU.\N每种工作负载对CPU都提出了新的要求。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:08.09,1:31:16.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some require maximum thread count, some depend on per-core performance, while others depend on memory bandwidth, cache efficiency, or I/O.\N有些需要最大线程数，有些依赖单核性能，而另一些则依赖内存带宽、缓存效率或I/O性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:16.49,1:31:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,performance.\N性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:17.81,1:31:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,The really important point is that there is no single SKU that solves every enterprise application.\N真正关键的一点是，没有单一的SKU能够解决所有企业应用。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:25.87,1:31:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why our EPYC portfolio with Venice spans 8 to 256 cores, with a range of power, frequencies, and I/O.\N这也正是我们EPYC威尼斯系列产品覆盖8到256核的原因，具备多种功耗、频率和I/O配置。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:33.99,1:31:43.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,capabilities, giving customers the flexibility to choose the right solution for their workload, and most importantly, at the most optimized cost.\N这些能力让客户能够灵活选择最适合其工作负载的解决方案，最重要的是，实现成本最优。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:45.07,1:31:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Lisa mentioned this earlier, and now we all know, we covered Venice,\N所以，丽莎之前提到过这一点，现在我们都知道了，我们已经介绍了威尼斯。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:51.07,1:31:57.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,and she showed how we have strong leadership across AI host nodes and the agentic workflows.\N她展示了我们在AI主机节点和代理工作流方面强大的领导地位。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:58.65,1:32:08.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I wanted to show you how Venice actually leads across the general purpose workloads of the enterprise and these workloads that are running our customers' line every day.\N但我想要向你们展示威尼斯实际上如何在企业通用工作负载中领先，以及这些每天运行客户业务流程的工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:08.97,1:32:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you can see, we have a minimum of 2.5x the performance across our competition, across these very, very important enterprise workloads.\N如你所见，我们在这些非常重要的企业工作负载上，性能比竞争对手至少高出2.5倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:20.23,1:32:27.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now, as we all know, agentic AI is really the next major transition for the enterprise.\N因此，正如我们所知，代理型AI确实是企业面临的下一次重大转型。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:27.55,1:32:33.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it truly is a force multiplier for enterprises, and adoption is accelerating.\N它确实能成为企业的倍增器，采用速度正在加快。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:33.65,1:32:41.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, the latest data here shows that nearly every enterprise next year will have some form of agentic deployments.\N事实上，最新数据显示，明年几乎每个企业都将部署某种形式的代理型AI。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:42.53,1:32:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as enterprises move from pilots to production deployments, we've talked to CIOs all the time, and they are looking at three major things.\N当企业从试点转向生产部署时，我们经常与首席信息官交流，他们关注三个主要方面。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:52.71,1:32:56.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,First, predictable infrastructure cost and token cost.\N首先，可预测的基础设施成本和词元成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:57.67,1:33:00.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Secondly, making sure the data is secure.\N其次，确保数据安全。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:01.05,1:33:08.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then lastly, and sometimes this is overlooked, right, integrating AI into their existing infrastructure.\N最后，有时这一点被忽视，即如何将AI集成到现有基础设施中。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:08.97,1:33:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not all greenfield out there for the enterprise customer.\N企业客户并非所有场景都是从零开始的。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:13.23,1:33:21.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to solve these problems, we truly believe that this is going to be a distributed deployment model that leverages frontier models, cloud services,\N为解决这些问题，我们坚信这将采用一种分布式部署模式，利用前沿模型、云服务、本地基础设施，以及当然还有AI客户端。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:22.27,1:33:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,on-prem infrastructure, and of course, AI clients.\N本地部署的基础设施，以及当然还有AI客户。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:25.67,1:33:39.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as AI has moved from chatbots responding to prompts to agents doing real work, writing code, summarizing documents, and running complex flows, the requirements have evolved also.\N随着人工智能从响应提示的聊天机器人，发展到能够完成实际工作、编写代码、总结文档和运行复杂流程的智能体，其需求也随之演变。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:40.47,1:33:45.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And those are exactly the requirements we've been designing for for multiple years.\N这些正是我们多年来一直在设计和应对的需求。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:45.75,1:33:54.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,So while AI will be deployed across all these environments, the on-prem deployments in our enterprise customers have fairly unique constraints.\N因此，尽管人工智能将被部署到所有这些环境中，但企业客户在本地部署时面临相当独特的限制。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:55.09,1:33:56.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,First and foremost, power/cooling.\N首当其冲的是电力和散热。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:57.73,1:33:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really big challenge in space.\N空间问题带来了真正的挑战。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:59.63,1:34:08.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course, costs remain top of the list for CIOs that are trying to drive things forward in the AI world.\N当然，对于希望在人工智能领域推进工作的首席信息官而言，成本依然是首要考虑因素。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:09.05,1:34:15.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then lastly, the full solutions they need to be easy to deploy.\N最后，他们需要的解决方案必须易于部署。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:15.97,1:34:22.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's been common for many, many years for the enterprise, but that's something we're very, very focused on.\N这对企业来说多年来一直如此，但这是我们非常专注的领域。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:22.93,1:34:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to address these constraints, thank you, Laura, I'm very happy to announce the launch of the Instinct MI350P.\N为应对这些限制，感谢劳拉，我很高兴宣布 Instinct MI350P 的发布。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:39.75,1:34:48.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So today, every enterprise wants AI in the data center, but the challenge is how do you add those capabilities without starting over?\N如今，每个企业都希望在数据中心部署人工智能，但挑战在于如何在不重新开始的情况下添加这些能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:48.61,1:34:51.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's exactly what the 350P was designed to solve.\N这正是 MI350P 所被设计解决的问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:51.93,1:34:59.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's an air-cooled GPU designed to fit within the power and cooling of enterprise servers today without a facilities upgrade.\N它是一款风冷 GPU，专为适配当前企业服务器的功耗和散热需求而设计，无需升级基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:59.81,1:35:05.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Making it easy to bring LLM scale inference into today's enterprise data center.\N使企业数据中心轻松实现大语言模型规模的推理。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:05.63,1:35:09.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at the same time, there's no compromise in capability.\N同时，性能上没有任何妥协。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:09.57,1:35:19.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,A single MI350P can support up to 260 billion parameters, allowing customers to run the majority of enterprise AI workloads on a single GPU.\N一块 MI350P 可支持高达 2600 亿个参数，使客户能够在单个 GPU 上运行大部分企业 AI 工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:20.29,1:35:24.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the economics are actually even better and more compelling.\N经济性实际上更加优越且更具吸引力。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:25.01,1:35:30.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The 350P delivers more than four times the tokens per second per dollar than the competition.\NMI350P 每美元每秒处理的词元数量是竞争对手的四倍以上。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:32.13,1:35:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's pretty cool.\N这真的很棒。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:36.10,1:35:43.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it actually turns the customer's existing data center into an AI data center.\N它实际上将客户现有的数据中心转变为 AI 数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:43.98,1:35:49.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we all know that benchmarks are one part of the equation, right?\N现在，我们都知道基准测试只是方程的一部分，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:35:49.36,1:35:56.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other part is really evaluating, does the advantage hold up across the actual workload you run and how your business runs?\N另一部分是真正评估，这种优势是否在您实际运行的工作负载以及业务运作中依然成立？
Dialogue: 0,1:35:56.82,1:36:02.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we tested a set of workloads, enterprise use cases, using production models.\N因此我们使用生产模型测试了一组工作负载和企业应用场景。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:02.88,1:36:12.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the 350P delivers much higher productivity than the competition, delivering up to two to five times faster tokens per second than the competition.\NMI350P 的生产力远超竞争对手，每秒词元处理速度最高比竞争对手快两到五倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:13.72,1:36:24.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you think about that, that's more tokens per second, more work completed, more users supported, all at a lower cost for the business.\N所以如果你这么想，那就是每秒处理更多词元，完成更多工作，支持更多用户，同时企业成本更低。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:26.46,1:36:32.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So another area that I wanted to talk about is, our earliest customer is our own AMD IT team.\N另一个我想谈的领域是，我们最早的客户就是我们自己的 AMD IT 团队。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:34.16,1:36:37.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they're a tough group to work with, even for us.\N他们是一群很难对付的团队，甚至对我们来说也是如此。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:38.46,1:36:41.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,But they put us through our paces.\N但他们确实让我们经受了严苛的考验。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:41.70,1:36:48.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And really, this has been our model from day one is, we want to put our technology into our own data center first.\N从第一天起，我们的模式就是，首先将我们的技术投入我们自己的数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:48.88,1:36:59.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like many companies, many enterprises, we're looking at how to deliver AI service to our employee base, but also manage costs and protect our data, manage and control the data.\N和许多公司、许多企业一样，我们正在思考如何向员工群体提供 AI 服务，同时控制成本并保护数据，管理并控制数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:00.02,1:37:04.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we focused on two use cases that we wanted to try out.\N因此我们聚焦于两个想要尝试的用例。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:04.72,1:37:07.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And first was autonomous threat detection.\N第一个是自主威胁检测。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:07.44,1:37:12.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that is probably one of the faster-growing agentic applications that we're seeing today.\N这可能是我们目前看到的增速最快的代理类应用之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:12.94,1:37:16.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the second was a personalized AI assistant running on OpenCloth.\N第二个是在 OpenCloth 上运行的个性化 AI 助手。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:17.64,1:37:29.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So both of these run route requests through the router, and the gateway sort of tests the complexity, the sensitivity of the information, and the service level requirements.\N这两个应用都会将请求通过路由器，网关会测试信息的复杂度、敏感性以及服务等级要求。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:30.96,1:37:38.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So some requests are sent to the Frontier model, while others are routed to OpenWeights models running on EPYC and an MI350P.\N一些请求被发送到 Frontier 模型，而另一些则被路由到运行在 EPYC 和 MI350P 上的 OpenWeights 模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:39.46,1:37:50.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So with intelligent routing, we reduced our token costs by 43%, while delivering up to 3x faster response times for the workloads running locally.\N通过智能路由，我们将词元成本降低了 43%，同时使本地运行的工作负载响应速度最快提升了 3 倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:50.94,1:37:55.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we believe this is how enterprise AI will be deployed.\N因此我们认为，这就是企业级AI的部署方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:57.84,1:38:06.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we also know that, from our history here with EPYC, that enabling enterprise takes a whole lot more than great silicon.\N但我们也知道，从我们在此与EPYC的历史来看，赋能企业远不止需要出色的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:07.24,1:38:10.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,It requires a complete ecosystem of software and solutions.\N它还需要一个完整的软件和解决方案生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:10.90,1:38:16.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over the last several years, we've truly grown significantly and expanded our enterprise AI ecosystem.\N在过去几年里，我们真正实现了显著增长，并扩展了企业AI生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:17.02,1:38:27.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we support numerous AI ISVs, provide zero-day support for all of the industry's leading open models, and deliver robust frameworks that help\N如今，我们支持众多AI独立软件供应商，为所有行业领先的开源模型提供零日支持，并提供强大的框架，
Dialogue: 0,1:38:27.16,1:38:31.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,customers bring AI into production as fast as possible.\N帮助客户尽可能快速地将AI投入生产。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:32.20,1:38:38.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's all built on trusted platform software and OEM partnerships that enterprises rely on every single day.\N所有这一切都建立在企业每天依赖的可信平台软件和OEM合作伙伴关系之上。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:39.92,1:38:55.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, everything I just shared comes down to one goal for us, and that's helping customers deploy AI where it creates the most value for them, whether it's in the cloud, on-premise, or at the edge.\N现在，我刚才分享的所有内容都归结为一个目标，那就是帮助客户在能为其创造最大价值的地方部署AI，无论是在云端、本地还是边缘。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:56.36,1:39:03.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to bring this to life, I'd like to welcome Jeremy Legg, Chief Technology Officer at AT&T.\N为了生动展现这一点，我邀请AT&T首席技术官杰里米·莱格登场。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:09.56,1:39:10.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good to see you.\N很高兴见到你。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:11.02,1:39:11.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Jeremy.\N谢谢你，杰里米。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:11.90,1:39:12.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks for having me.\N谢谢你们的邀请。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:13.50,1:39:14.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, this is great.\N是的，这太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:14.48,1:39:15.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of a homecoming.\N这有点像是回家。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:15.54,1:39:17.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,I grew up in the East Bay, so it's good to be back.\N我在东湾区长大，所以能回来感觉很好。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:18.28,1:39:18.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, fantastic.\N是的，太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:19.04,1:39:20.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We really appreciate you joining us today.\N我们非常感谢您今天加入我们。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:20.82,1:39:26.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So look, I think everyone knows AT&T as the largest communications company,\N众所周知，AT&T 是最大的通信公司之一，
Dialogue: 0,1:39:27.14,1:39:34.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,one of the largest in the world, and I'm sure half of them out there probably have AT&T network right now.\N也是全球最大的公司之一，我敢说在座的有一半人现在可能正使用 AT&T 的网络。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:34.94,1:39:36.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hopefully more than half.\N希望超过一半。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:38.78,1:39:46.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But AI is touching way more than the network, and you and your team are really doing a fair amount of work driving it.\N但人工智能的影响远超网络范畴，你们和你们的团队正在积极推动这一领域的发展。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:46.28,1:39:51.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you share with us sort of the opportunities you approach, you're working on, and your experience to date?\N那您能和我们分享一下您正在关注的机会、正在进行的工作以及至今的经验吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:39:52.40,1:39:53.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure, happy to.\N当然可以，很乐意。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:53.58,1:40:02.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,At AT&T, we're now burning about a trillion-plus tokens per month, and that number has gone up pretty dramatically.\N在 AT&T，我们现在每月处理的词元数量已超过一万亿，这个数字增长得非常迅速。
Dialogue: 0,1:40:02.74,1:40:08.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's moving up double digits, and so this is now becoming very pervasive inside of the enterprise.\N它正以两位数的速度增长，因此现在这在企业内部变得非常普遍。
Dialogue: 0,1:40:09.50,1:40:15.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got over 100 Gen A models in production across our enterprise as well,\N我们的企业中已有超过100个生成式AI模型在生产环境中运行，
Dialogue: 0,1:40:15.86,1:40:25.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,and those are stretching from things that I think a lot of folks are doing in customer care, things that we're doing in fraud, but also things that you wouldn't\N这些应用涵盖了我所认为很多人正在做的客户关怀工作、我们用于欺诈检测的工作，以及一些你可能不会想到的领域，
Dialogue: 0,1:40:25.12,1:40:33.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,necessarily think about, like where's the best place to place a cell tower or a RAN that is the most effective use of it inside of a network?\N比如在网络中放置基站或无线接入网（RAN）的最佳位置，以实现最高效的利用？
Dialogue: 0,1:40:34.18,1:40:40.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So all of these things are happening across our enterprise, but they're happening at a scale that is not necessarily normal.\N所有这些都在我们企业内部发生，但其规模并非寻常。
Dialogue: 0,1:40:41.44,1:40:44.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We get over 300,000 calls a day.\N我们每天处理超过30万通电话。
Dialogue: 0,1:40:44.52,1:40:53.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,The transcription of those calls is an enormous workload, and then driving the insights out of those calls that we then bring back to the business is another set of insights.\N这些电话的转录工作量巨大，而从这些通话中提取洞察并反馈给业务，又是一套全新的洞察。
Dialogue: 0,1:40:54.38,1:41:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's really an interesting thing, and now we're beginning to actually rebuild entire workflows inside of the company beyond just the point use of a use\N这确实非常有趣，现在我们开始真正地重建公司内部的整个工作流程，而不仅仅是针对某个具体应用场景。
Dialogue: 0,1:41:04.28,1:41:13.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,case. So as we think about HR, as we think about finance, and we think about different kinds of things that each of those organizations do, cash forecasting,\N因此在思考人力资源、财务，以及这些部门各自开展的不同工作时，比如现金流预测，
Dialogue: 0,1:41:14.28,1:41:19.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,things that we do on onboarding employees as examples, we're now agentifying those entire workloads.\N以及入职员工时我们所做的一些事情，我们现在正在将这些整个工作负载进行代理化。
Dialogue: 0,1:41:20.00,1:41:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so we work closely with your team, and we've had many conversations.\N是的，我们与你们团队紧密合作，也进行了多次交流。
Dialogue: 0,1:41:26.18,1:41:35.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's truly amazing the number of actual opportunities you're addressing with AI, so a super broad range of use.\N真的令人惊叹，你们用AI解决的实际机会如此之多，应用范围极为广泛。
Dialogue: 0,1:41:35.92,1:41:45.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you just explain sort of what are the key learnings in moving these to AI at enterprise scale, and then maybe a bit on what we've done together?\N所以你能解释一下，将这些技术迁移到企业级AI时，有哪些关键经验吗？然后也许再谈谈我们双方合作做了些什么？
Dialogue: 0,1:41:45.80,1:41:52.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure. I mean, I'll start at a place that I don't think everybody starts from here, which is the human.\N当然。我想从一个我认为大家未必都从这里开始的地方说起，那就是人。
Dialogue: 0,1:41:53.86,1:41:59.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need world-class teams in order to do this, and you need people that think in workflows.\N你需要世界级的团队才能做到这一点，还需要那些善于思考工作流程的人。
Dialogue: 0,1:41:59.54,1:42:03.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's an enormous amount of what I call racing from stoplight to stoplight.\N有很多所谓的“从一个红绿灯跑到下一个红绿灯”的情况。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:04.40,1:42:11.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Folks are going from 0 to 100, and then they hit the next stage of the workflow, and then there's a red light, and they haven't worked their way all the way through that.\N人们从0做到100，然后进入工作流程的下一个阶段，却遇到了红灯，而他们还没完全打通整个流程。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:12.16,1:42:20.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I would start with people and the quality of the people that you really have across your enterprise in order to do these things.\N所以我建议，首先要关注人，以及你在企业中真正拥有的人员质量，这是完成这些事情的基础。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:20.96,1:42:32.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second point is we are big believers in data sovereignty, and data sovereignty for us means not being tied to a specific chipset, not being tied to a specific\N第二点是我们非常相信数据主权，对我们而言，数据主权意味着不被绑定到特定芯片组，不被绑定到特定
Dialogue: 0,1:42:32.16,1:42:35.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,model or a specific set of development tools.\N模型或特定的一套开发工具。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:35.38,1:42:37.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need, as an enterprise, to manage your data.\N作为企业，你需要掌控自己的数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:38.02,1:42:43.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Your data is your fuel in terms of how you implement AI across that broader enterprise.\N你的数据是你在企业范围内实施AI的燃料。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:43.42,1:42:52.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we've done with AMD, and AMD's been such a great partner in this, is leveraging open source models, leveraging different sets of chipsets,\N我们与AMD合作，AMD在这过程中一直是极好的合作伙伴，我们利用开源模型，使用不同的芯片组，
Dialogue: 0,1:42:52.86,1:42:56.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,building our own models, training other models.\N自主构建模型，训练其他模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:42:56.04,1:43:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're one of the few companies in the world that's actually post-trained a model on AMD and then been able to drive equivalency in terms of performance and\N我们是全球为数不多的在 AMD 上完成模型后训练，并成功实现性能等效的公司之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:04.28,1:43:07.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,accuracy with other more expensive chipsets in the marketplace.\N与其他市场上更昂贵的芯片组相比，精度相当。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:08.44,1:43:17.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,So as we have done that, we've been able to drive down token costs, essentially through money-balling across all of these different models and leveraging that human\N因此，我们通过在所有这些不同模型间进行资金优化，并利用人力，成功降低了词元成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:17.34,1:43:20.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,capital in a way that's made a big difference to our company.\N在某种程度上，这种资本投入对我们公司产生了重大影响。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:21.22,1:43:30.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so increasingly, even though token consumption is going up, we're able to manage that underlying token cost at enterprise scale, which is not a small\N因此，尽管词元消耗在增加，我们仍能有效控制企业规模下的底层词元成本，这并非小事。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:30.32,1:43:33.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,thing. Yeah, it's a bunch of great work.\N事情。是的，这是一系列出色的工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:33.58,1:43:41.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another key area that's sort of groundbreaking, which is exciting also, is you're the first telecom company to actually train a model on AMD.\N另一个颇具突破性的关键领域也令人振奋，那就是你们是首家在 AMD 上实际训练模型的电信公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:41.58,1:43:45.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also, you're driving fully open source models in telecom.\N而且，你们还在电信领域全面使用开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:45.86,1:43:48.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So tell us about that experience and why you felt like that was needed.\N所以跟我们说说那段经历，以及你为什么觉得有必要这么做。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:49.72,1:43:56.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We felt like the industry was moving down a path where folks were only going to use closed source models to solve solutions.\N我们感觉整个行业正朝着一个方向发展，人们只会使用闭源模型来解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:43:57.24,1:44:05.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And while closed source models are an important ingredient in that, we didn't want to lose sight of the fact that open source models were going to be a very significant part of the solution.\N虽然闭源模型是其中一个重要组成部分，但我们不想忽视一个事实，那就是开源模型将是解决方案中非常关键的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:05.88,1:44:09.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we announced what we call OTEL 1.0.\N所以我们宣布了我们称之为 OTEL 1.0 的产品。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:09.16,1:44:13.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's the open telco AI model a bit over a year ago or so now.\N这是大约一年前推出的开放电信AI模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:13.90,1:44:18.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we had over 18 million downloads of that model since then.\N自那时以来，该模型的下载量已超过1800万次。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:19.26,1:44:26.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're excited to announce today the launch of OTEL 2.0, which is a more advanced set of models that we have trained on AMD.\N今天我们很高兴宣布推出OTEL 2.0，这是我们在AMD上训练的更先进的模型集合。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:27.02,1:44:31.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're now making that available via open source across the broader industry.\N现在，我们将通过开源方式向整个行业提供该模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:32.12,1:44:40.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it, I think, is going to give folks an opportunity to see that not only do you need to think about leveraging models, but you also need to think about training\N我认为，这将为人们提供一个机会，让他们意识到，不仅需要考虑如何利用模型，还必须思考模型的训练方式及其在企业内部的运作。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:40.10,1:44:42.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,those models and how they work across your enterprise.\N以及它们如何在您的企业中协同工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:43.82,1:44:44.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's just great.\N所以这真是太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:44.76,1:44:46.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We certainly appreciate the partnership.\N我们非常感谢这次合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:46.68,1:44:49.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, we really feel like this is germane to the conversation.\N而且，我们觉得这与当前的讨论密切相关。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:50.04,1:44:52.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's exactly what we've been talking about today.\N这正是我们今天一直在谈论的内容。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:52.40,1:44:55.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I just want to thank you again for joining us and the partnership.\N我再次感谢您加入我们并建立合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:55.70,1:44:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:56.36,1:44:57.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're a big part of it.\N你是其中的重要部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:44:57.88,1:44:58.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:02.86,1:45:05.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so let me close with one last point.\N好的，让我用最后一点来结束。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:06.46,1:45:15.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've established ourselves as a leader in enterprise computing by listening to our customers and delivering the right solutions for their workloads.\N我们通过倾听客户的需求，并为他们的工作负载提供合适的解决方案，确立了在企业计算领域的领导地位。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:15.62,1:45:21.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we're extending that leadership to help customers accelerate their AI journey.\N如今，我们将这一领导力延伸，帮助客户加速他们的AI进程。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:22.58,1:45:25.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is our vision for powering AI everywhere.\N这就是我们为实现AI everywhere所描绘的愿景。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:26.66,1:45:33.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to expand a little bit beyond the data center into physical and client AI,\N为了将我们的布局从数据中心进一步拓展到物理AI和客户端AI，
Dialogue: 0,1:45:34.38,1:45:39.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's my pleasure to introduce Mr. Jack Huynh, who leads our computing and graphics group.\N很荣幸向大家介绍杰克·黄，他负责我们的计算与图形业务部门。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:39.84,1:45:40.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:45.82,1:45:46.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Dan.\N谢谢，丹。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:48.08,1:45:52.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's great to see so many friends, partners, and developers here in San Francisco.\N很高兴在旧金山见到这么多朋友、合作伙伴和开发者。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:53.18,1:45:59.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we have seen how AMD is building the compute foundation for AI in a data center.\N今天，我们看到了AMD如何在数据中心构建AI的计算基础。
Dialogue: 0,1:45:59.68,1:46:03.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the full AI transformation requires two more ingredients.\N但完整的AI转型还需要两个要素。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:03.78,1:46:08.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Intelligence that becomes personal, and intelligence that can understand and act in a physical world.\N一种能个性化的智能，以及一种能理解并作用于物理世界中的智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:09.44,1:46:12.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Those are the two frontiers I want to explore with you here today.\N这两个前沿领域正是我今天想与大家探讨的。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:12.60,1:46:14.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's begin with personal AI.\N让我们从个人AI开始。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:15.70,1:46:21.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Enterprise AI is already reshaping the data center, but agentic AI will extend far beyond it.\N企业AI已经重塑了数据中心，但代理AI将远远超越它。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:22.24,1:46:25.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Agents are the next great productivity multiplier.\N代理是下一个巨大的生产力倍增器。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:26.02,1:46:30.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,The jump from software that responds to software that completes work.\N从响应式软件到能完成工作的软件的飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:30.84,1:46:33.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,A personal agent can double what one person can do.\N一个个人代理可以将一个人的效率翻倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:34.32,1:46:36.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,A team of agents can multiply that by 10.\N一组代理可以将这一效率提升十倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:37.04,1:46:41.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as agents gain more capabilities, the opportunity can grow exponentially.\N随着代理能力的增强，机遇将呈指数级增长。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:41.42,1:46:44.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,But that promise has a compute consequence.\N但这一承诺也带来了计算上的后果。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:44.80,1:46:57.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unlike a single AI query, as agent reasons, calls tools, and coordinates to other agents, and run nonstop, agents become more capable and pervasive.\N与单次AI查询不同，当代理在推理、调用工具、与其他代理协调并持续运行时，它们会变得越来越强大且无处不在。
Dialogue: 0,1:46:57.88,1:47:05.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,So will token consumption, meaning that demand will require every layer of the computing ecosystem to scale together.\N词元消耗也将随之增加，这意味着需求将要求计算生态系统的每一层协同扩展。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:05.92,1:47:10.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Data centers remain the foundation for frontier AI in the most demanding workloads.\N数据中心仍然是应对最严苛工作负载的前沿人工智能的基础。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:10.70,1:47:20.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,But edge-inclined systems can extend that capacity, putting more intelligence closer to where data is created and where the work gets done.\N但偏向边缘的系统可以扩展这种能力，将更多智能置于数据生成和工作执行的附近。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:21.20,1:47:27.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,The PC is already one of the most powerful compute engines ever placed in the hands of an individual.\N个人电脑已经是个人手中最强大的计算引擎之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:27.60,1:47:36.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Across billions of devices, enormous computing capability is already deployed every single day, yet its potential remains largely untapped.\N在数十亿设备上，巨大的计算能力每天都在被部署，但其潜力仍大多未被开发。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:37.32,1:47:40.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Putting that capacity to work changed the economics of computing.\N将这种能力投入使用，改变了计算的经济性。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:41.34,1:47:51.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,More workloads can run on systems that are already in place, reducing overall infrastructure costs and allowing data centers to focus on the largest, most demanding task.\N更多工作负载可以在现有系统上运行，从而降低整体基础设施成本，并让数据中心能够专注于最大、最严苛的任务。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:52.02,1:47:54.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And local computing brings inherent advantages.\N本地计算带来了固有的优势。
Dialogue: 0,1:47:55.18,1:48:04.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Your data stays with you, your applications remain responsive, and your system keeps working, even when your network does not.\N你的数据始终在你身边，你的应用程序保持响应，即使网络中断，你的系统仍能正常运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:04.46,1:48:11.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And thanks to a new generation of smaller, more capable AI models, we're beginning to unlock that potential.\N由于新一代更小、更强大的AI模型，我们正开始释放这种潜力。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:12.84,1:48:16.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the unlock is happening faster than anyone expected.\N这种潜力的释放速度比任何人预期的都要快。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:17.28,1:48:25.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Last August, GPT OSS needed 120 billion parameters to score 80 on GPQA.\N去年八月，GPT OSS 需要1200亿参数才能在GPQA上获得80分。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:25.90,1:48:32.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just seven months later, Qwen 3.5 scored even higher, with only 9 billion.\N仅七个月后，Qwen 3.5 的得分更高，参数量仅为 90 亿。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:32.86,1:48:36.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Better performance, with 13 times fewer parameters.\N性能更优，参数量仅为之前的十三分之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:36.38,1:48:39.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is not an incremental improvement.\N这并非渐进式改进。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:39.94,1:48:44.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a dramatic shift in the compute required to deliver advanced intelligence.\N它标志着实现先进智能所需计算能力的显著转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:45.50,1:48:48.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is a trend, not an outlier.\N这是一种趋势，而非偶然现象。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:49.06,1:48:54.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Smaller, open models are closing the frontier gap at extraordinary speed.\N更小、开源的模型正以惊人的速度缩小与前沿模型之间的差距。
Dialogue: 0,1:48:54.82,1:49:10.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Qwen 3.6, 27 billion parameters now outperforms leading frontier models from the previous generation on graduate-level reasoning, at a fraction of the size and cost. That changes what is possible.\NQwen 3.6 目前拥有 270 亿参数，在研究生级推理任务上已超越上一代领先前沿模型，体积和成本仅为它们的几分之一。这改变了可能的边界。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:11.72,1:49:19.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Workloads once reserved for the cloud can now run on powerful compute engines designed for personal AI compute.\N过去仅限于云端的负载，如今可在专为个人 AI 计算设计的强大计算引擎上运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:20.64,1:49:25.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's map these model performance breakthroughs to any platforms.\N让我们把这些模型性能突破映射到各类平台。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:26.12,1:49:38.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ryzen AI 400 supports models up to 24 billion parameters, more than enough for Qwen 3.5, 9 billion, with substantial headroom.\NRyzen AI 400 支持高达 240 亿参数的模型，远超 Qwen 3.5 的 90 亿参数，且留有充足余量。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:38.92,1:49:47.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ryzen AI Max extends that capacity to models as large as 200 billion parameters, running natively on a personal system.\NRyzen AI Max 将这一能力扩展至高达 2000 亿参数的模型，可在个人系统上原生运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:48.56,1:49:52.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,This has not reduced AI, compressed to fit on a PC.\N这并未将 AI 压缩到仅适合 PC 的程度。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:52.60,1:49:59.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a new class of personal computing built to run powerful models where the work actually happens.\N这是一种全新的个人计算平台，专为在实际工作地点运行强大模型而设计。
Dialogue: 0,1:49:59.94,1:50:04.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is exactly what led us to build Ryzen AI Halo.\N这正是我们决定打造锐龙AI光环的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:50:05.20,1:50:12.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,We wanted to give developers a platform powerful enough to run these models locally, yet simple enough to use every day.\N我们希望为开发者提供一个足够强大以在本地运行这些模型，同时又足够简单以便日常使用的平台。
Dialogue: 0,1:50:13.40,1:50:27.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,With 120 gigabytes of unified memory and support for models up to 200 billion parameters, developers can build, test, and iterate locally directly on their desk.\N拥有120GB统一内存并支持高达2000亿参数的模型，开发者可以直接在桌面上本地构建、测试和迭代。
Dialogue: 0,1:50:28.18,1:50:37.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ryzen AI Halo embodies the future of personal AI for everyone, a future that shortens the distance between an idea and a working model.\N锐龙AI光环体现了每个人都能享有的个人AI未来，一个缩短了从想法到可用模型之间距离的未来。
Dialogue: 0,1:50:38.22,1:50:45.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,For developers, that means a dramatically more efficient and optimized path from experimentation to deployment.\N对开发者而言，这意味着从实验到部署的路径实现了显著更高的效率和优化。
Dialogue: 0,1:50:46.46,1:50:53.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as Vamsi showed earlier, rocm.ai is making hardware programming radically more accessible.\N正如瓦姆西此前展示的那样，rocm.ai 正使硬件编程变得前所未有的易用。
Dialogue: 0,1:50:54.22,1:51:02.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Developers can understand, modify, and optimize code for ROCm, even without deep ROCm expertise.\N开发者无需深入掌握ROCm知识，也能理解、修改和优化ROCm代码。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:03.36,1:51:09.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And better yet, the same open software foundation extends across all of AMD's hardware.\N更棒的是，这一开放软件基础覆盖了AMD全部硬件。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:10.20,1:51:21.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Developers can use the frameworks and tools they already know, start locally on Ryzen AI Halo, and scale across the full AMD compute platform without rebuilding their work.\N开发者可以使用他们已熟悉的框架和工具，在锐龙AI光环上本地启动，然后无缝扩展到整个AMD计算平台，无需重新构建工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:22.06,1:51:23.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're not stopping there.\N我们不会止步于此。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:23.74,1:51:32.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we're expanding our partnership with Hugging Face to bring the open AI ecosystem directly on Ryzen AI Halo.\N今天，我们正扩大与Hugging Face的合作，将开放AI生态直接带入锐龙AI光环。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:33.32,1:51:44.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Powerful compute only creates value when developers can quickly access the right models, optimize them for the platform, and turn them into real applications.\N只有当开发者能够快速获取合适的模型、针对平台进行优化并将其转化为实际应用时，强大的算力才能创造价值。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:45.00,1:51:53.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Together, AMD and Hugging Face will deliver Halo optimized performance for open models and agentic workflows.\NAMD 和 Hugging Face 将共同提供针对开源模型和代理工作流优化的 Halo 性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:56.18,1:51:58.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,How cool is that?\N这太酷了。
Dialogue: 0,1:51:59.40,1:52:08.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And along with co-engineered libraries and toolkits designed to help developers spend less time configuring infrastructure and more time building.\N同时，还有共同设计的库和工具包，帮助开发者减少配置基础设施的时间，更多地专注于开发。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:08.86,1:52:20.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And later this year, every Ryzen AI Halo box will include a full year of Hugging Face Pro, putting the power of partnership in developers' hands from day one.\N今年晚些时候，每一台 Ryzen AI Halo 电脑都将包含一整年的 Hugging Face Pro，从第一天起就将合作的力量交到开发者手中。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:21.52,1:52:24.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Freedom and more power to the user.\N给用户更多自由和更强的能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:25.14,1:52:29.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is how we accelerate innovation in the AI era.\N这就是我们在 AI 时代加速创新的方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:30.30,1:52:34.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're already pushing that vision further with Gorgon Halo.\N我们已经通过 Gorgon Halo 进一步推进了这一愿景。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:35.76,1:52:41.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And seeing is believing, look at how small and beautiful this box is.\N眼见为实，看看这个盒子是多么小巧精致。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:46.08,1:52:53.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've increased unified memory from 128 to 192 gigabytes.\N统一内存已从 128GB 提升至 192GB。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:53.54,1:52:56.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,The largest unified memory pool in this class.\N这个级别中最大的统一内存池。
Dialogue: 0,1:52:56.92,1:53:01.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And increased model support from 200 billion to 300 billion parameters.\N模型支持参数量从 2000 亿提升至 3000 亿。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:03.20,1:53:03.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Laura.\N谢谢你，劳拉。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:06.87,1:53:10.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is no longer limited to a single platform form factor.\N这已不再局限于单一平台形态。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:11.05,1:53:17.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Together, with the world's leading OEMs, AMD now powers the broadest portfolio of personal AI systems.\N与全球领先的OEM厂商合作，AMD如今为最广泛的个人AI系统提供了动力。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:18.27,1:53:22.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,From laptops and workstations to mini PCs and developer platforms.\N从笔记本电脑和工作站，到迷你电脑和开发者平台。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:23.17,1:53:30.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That means developers, enterprises, and creators can choose the right system for the way they want to build and work.\N这意味着开发者、企业及创作者可以根据自己的构建和工作方式选择合适的系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:31.61,1:53:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Personal AI is not a concept.\N个人AI不是一个概念。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:33.69,1:53:37.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a category and is available right now on AMD.\N它是一个类别，现在已在AMD上可用。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:38.83,1:53:40.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,We now have all the pieces.\N我们现在已具备所有要素。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:41.65,1:53:43.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Models are efficient enough.\N模型已足够高效。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:43.77,1:53:45.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hardware is powerful enough.\N硬件已足够强大。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:45.97,1:53:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Software stack is open and ready.\N软件栈开放且已准备就绪。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:48.31,1:53:53.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And open harnesses like Lemonade Server can route workloads to the right model and right compute.\N开放式框架如Lemonade Server可将工作负载导向正确的模型和正确的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:54.05,1:53:55.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,The technology is here.\N这项技术已经到来。
Dialogue: 0,1:53:55.93,1:54:01.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next challenge is taking it from one developer's desk to thousands of users across an enterprise.\N下一个挑战是将它从一名开发者的桌面推广到企业中的数千名用户。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:02.11,1:54:05.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cisco sees and believes in that future the same way we do.\N思科和我们一样，看到了那个未来，并且相信它。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:05.63,1:54:09.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,To take us deeper into how we turn that vision into enterprise scale reality,\N为了更深入地了解我们如何将这一愿景变为企业规模的现实，
Dialogue: 0,1:54:10.33,1:54:15.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,please join me in welcoming to the stage Jeetu Patel, President and Chief Product Officer at Cisco.\N请和我一起欢迎思科公司总裁兼首席产品官杰图·帕特尔登台。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:19.45,1:54:20.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jeetu, how are you doing?\N杰图，你好吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:54:20.87,1:54:21.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,How are you?\N你好。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:21.35,1:54:21.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,You look great.\N你看起来状态很好。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:21.93,1:54:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for joining me here today.\N感谢你今天来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:24.27,1:54:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.\N恭喜你。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:25.23,1:54:26.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, thank you.\N谢谢，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:26.47,1:54:28.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now Jeetu, you and I talk how we're at an inflection point.\N现在杰图，你我都知道我们正处在一个转折点。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:29.35,1:54:34.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for the past few years, industry has spent time just building intelligence.\N过去几年里，产业界一直在专注于构建智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:34.79,1:54:38.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next phase is how we deploy this technology at scale enterprises.\N下一阶段是如何将这项技术大规模部署到企业中。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:38.75,1:54:42.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You spent so much of your time talking to CIOs, technology leaders.\N你花了大量时间与首席信息官和技术领导者交谈。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:42.85,1:54:43.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,What are they telling you?\N他们告诉了你什么？
Dialogue: 0,1:54:43.61,1:54:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's changing?\N有哪些变化？
Dialogue: 0,1:54:44.77,1:54:47.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, firstly, it's a really exciting time to be alive in tech.\N首先，现在正处于科技领域一个非常激动人心的时代。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:47.73,1:54:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you just take a step back right now and see what's happening, there's actually a fundamental shift that's happening in the patterns of inferencing.\N如果你此刻退后一步，看看正在发生的事情，实际上在推理模式上正发生根本性转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:54:55.15,1:55:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you think about the patterns of inferencing that existed during the chatbot era that was human-led, it was very, very spiky.\N想想聊天机器人时代的人类主导推理模式，那时的模式非常不规则且波动剧烈。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:01.61,1:55:03.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,You ask a question, you get an answer.\N你提出一个问题，就会得到一个回答。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:03.29,1:55:06.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,What you're starting to see with agents is they're working 7x24.\N你开始看到代理正在全天候、每周七天不间断地工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:07.89,1:55:10.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're very consumptive on bandwidth and on infrastructure.\N它们对带宽和基础设施的消耗非常大。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:10.73,1:55:15.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you're starting to see a much more persistent pattern of kind of demand signal for infrastructure.\N因此，你开始看到基础设施需求信号呈现出一种更加持续的模式。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:16.21,1:55:20.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we usually joke around internally, humans click, but agents swarm.\N你知道，我们内部通常开玩笑说，人类点击，而智能体则成群涌动。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:22.19,1:55:31.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so as you start to see this, what you're going to have is a tremendous amount of and there's two big concerns that are also there, which is one is every\N所以当你开始看到这一点时，你会意识到这将带来巨大的变化，同时也有两个主要担忧，一个是每个
Dialogue: 0,1:55:31.67,1:55:36.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,customer is concerned about security and every customer is concerned about cost.\N客户都关心安全，每个客户都关心成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:36.99,1:55:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what you're starting to see happen is inferencing is not just going to be limited to the data center.\N所以你开始看到的是，推理计算将不再局限于数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,1:55:43.13,1:55:50.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Inferencing is going to be distributed everywhere and there's a whole new class of computing that's emerging with this desk-side computing that you just\N推理计算将分布到各个地方，由此出现了一种全新的计算形态，就像你刚刚宣布的桌面计算那样，将
Dialogue: 0,1:55:50.61,1:55:58.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,announced where there's going to be inferencing that you're going to have a laptop or a desktop where humans work, and they might have a desk-side computer\N出现推理能力，你可能会有一台笔记本电脑或台式机，供人类工作使用，同时可能还有一台桌面级计算机
Dialogue: 0,1:55:58.55,1:56:02.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,where agents are kind of going out and running their jobs on behalf of humans.\N用于智能体代为运行任务。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:02.95,1:56:05.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's what we're seeing, essentially.\N这就是我们正在看到的实质。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:05.29,1:56:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're fully aligned Jeetu and that's exactly the shift we're seeing.\N我们完全认同杰图的观点，这正是我们所看到的转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:09.01,1:56:12.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,If AI is moving closer to employees, compute has to move closer as well.\N如果AI正向员工靠近，计算能力也必须随之靠近。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:12.87,1:56:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,The PC's knowledge as a productivity device becomes an intelligence node in the enterprise but deploying intelligence everywhere creates a new trend for CIOs that you and I talk about so much.\N个人电脑作为生产力设备的知识，将转变为企业的智能节点，但将智能部署到各个地方，也带来了CIO们长期讨论的新趋势。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:24.89,1:56:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you operate thousands of these systems with the security, governance and control enterprises require?\N如何在确保安全、治理和企业所需控制的前提下，管理成千上万的这类系统？
Dialogue: 0,1:56:31.77,1:56:36.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jeetu, how is AMD and Cisco solving this and what are we building together?\N杰图，AMD 和思科是如何解决这个问题的？我们又在共同打造什么？
Dialogue: 0,1:56:36.83,1:56:43.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so this is an exciting time because what you're starting to see is there's a few things that need to really be done.\N是的，现在正是令人兴奋的时刻，因为你们开始看到，有几件事真的需要完成。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:43.21,1:56:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't just go out and deploy your desk-side computers and hope that everything works out in the enterprise.\N你不能只是把桌面电脑搬出去，就指望在企业环境中一切都能顺利运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:49.73,1:56:54.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to make sure that it's governed, it's managed and so there's a few things that are really important.\N你必须确保系统受到管控、得到管理，有几件事特别重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:56:54.53,1:57:01.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Number one, you have to have an appropriate amount of network bandwidth to satiate the needs of the agents that you are going to run locally.\N首先，你必须具备足够的网络带宽，以满足本地运行的代理所需。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:02.01,1:57:09.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this notion of network infrastructure that can get modernized to keep up with the needs that you're going to go out and generate is going to be very important.\N因此，能够升级以跟上你未来生成需求的网络基础设施，将变得非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:10.05,1:57:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's number one.\N这是第一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:10.81,1:57:19.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Number two, like I said, every customer is really worried about token costs and so we need to make sure that we can actually contain the costs of an agent's\N第二点，如我所说，每位客户都十分关注词元成本，所以我们必须确保在代理实际出现异常时，能够真正控制其词元消耗成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:19.25,1:57:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,consumption of tokens when it actually starts to go awry.\N在需要时可以上下调整。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:22.03,1:57:22.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Up and down when needed.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:23.15,1:57:23.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N正是如此。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:24.33,1:57:35.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Number three then is how do we monitor agent behavior for safety and security so that if it does start to do things that we don't want it to do, we can in runtime provide enforcement guardrails.\N第三点则是，我们如何监控代理行为以确保安全与合规，以便一旦它开始做出我们不希望的事情，我们就能在运行时提供强制性的防护机制。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:36.01,1:57:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then fourthly, it's just the overall safety and security that you need to have from an apparatus perspective to get this entire thing humming in the way that you want it to hum.\N第四，从设备的角度来看，你必须具备整体的安全性和可靠性，才能让整个系统按照你期望的方式顺畅运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:44.97,1:57:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes, it's great how you and I think very alike.\N是的，你和我想得非常相似，这太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:47.37,1:57:51.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I mean the opportunity is not just bringing every device as you and I talk.\N我的意思是，机会不仅仅在于像你我这样把每个设备都连接起来。
Dialogue: 0,1:57:51.37,1:57:54.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we enable enterprise to deploy, manage the skill with confidence?\N我们该如何让企业有信心地部署和管理这项技能？
Dialogue: 0,1:57:55.51,1:57:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why don't we take a look at what we've been building the past few weeks and months. Yeah, it's exciting.\N我们何不来看看过去几周和几个月我们一直在构建的东西？是的，这很令人兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:00.19,1:58:04.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So basically what we've done is there's a full stack that you can start to think about.\N基本上我们所做的，是构建了一个完整的技术栈，你可以开始从这个层面进行思考。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:04.65,1:58:10.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what you folks have done with Halo is you've got an isolated secure agent sandbox.\N你们团队在 Halo 上所做的，是创建了一个隔离的、安全的代理沙箱。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:11.27,1:58:12.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've got intelligent routing.\N你们拥有智能路由功能。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:12.97,1:58:18.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've got an MCP kind of core set of integrations.\N你们还拥有类似 MCP 的核心集成套件。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:18.91,1:58:24.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then what we've done above that is we've made sure that you have the right level of security policy enforcement.\N而在这些之上，我们确保了你具备正确的安全策略执行级别。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:24.93,1:58:31.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've also got the right level of observability so that it's an end-to-end resilient infrastructure stack.\N我们还具备恰当的可观测性，从而构建了一个端到端的高韧性基础设施栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:31.49,1:58:36.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's observability of how is your apparatus and the infrastructure working.\N所以，可观测性指的是你的设备和基础设施运行状况如何。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:37.31,1:58:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is the agent behavior being done in the right way?\N代理行为是否以正确的方式进行？
Dialogue: 0,1:58:40.35,1:58:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you observe the agent behavior?\N你能观察到代理的行为吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:58:41.89,1:58:46.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And are the tokenomics within the guidelines that you want them to be?\N且它们的代币经济是否符合你期望的规范？
Dialogue: 0,1:58:46.93,1:58:58.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then what we have is a single unified management plane, a control plane that can look at every single dimension that you have and be managed within one environment.\N然后我们拥有的是一个统一的管理平面，一个控制平面，能够查看你所有的维度，并在单一环境中进行管理。
Dialogue: 0,1:58:59.41,1:59:03.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's kind of the full stack, and we are really, really excited about the partnership.\N这就是完整的全栈解决方案，我们对此次合作感到非常非常兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,1:59:03.79,1:59:05.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Us too, our teams love working with your team Jeetu.\N我们也是，我们的团队非常喜欢与你们团队合作，Jeetu。
Dialogue: 0,1:59:06.31,1:59:07.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,How is this all managed?\N这一切是如何管理的？
Dialogue: 0,1:59:07.39,1:59:09.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,How does the CAO deploy this at scale?\NCAO 如何实现大规模部署？
Dialogue: 0,1:59:09.71,1:59:11.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so let's take a look at what this looks like, right?\N是的，那我们来看看这到底是什么样子，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:59:11.79,1:59:17.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because what we would have is this is Cisco Cloud Control, which is the overall management plane.\N因为我们拥有的是思科云控制，也就是整体的管理平面。
Dialogue: 0,1:59:17.85,1:59:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you happen to have Halo devices on every desktop, which it might actually get to, what you want to make sure that you do is you are able to go out and manage your\N所以如果你的每台电脑上都有 Halo 设备，这实际上可能成为现实，那你必须确保能够走出去管理
Dialogue: 0,1:59:29.95,1:59:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,entire estate of not just your Halo fleet, but also what you have running on the data centers, as well as what you have running in the cloud.\N你所有的资产，不仅包括你的 Halo 设备群，还包括你在数据中心运行的系统，以及你在云上运行的系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:59:38.09,1:59:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can provide full visibility for that entirety of the estate.\N因此你可以对整个资产实现全面的可视化。
Dialogue: 0,1:59:43.23,1:59:49.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then once you've got that, what we also have is this notion of how do we go out and monitor tokenomics?\N然后一旦你有了这些，我们还有另一个概念，就是如何走出去监控词元经济。
Dialogue: 0,1:59:50.29,1:59:58.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so is the agent behaving the way that it needs to behave, or is the agent actually going out and being overly consumptive?\N所以这个代理是否按需表现，还是实际上过度消耗资源？
Dialogue: 0,1:59:58.69,2:00:05.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,At which point, you should be able to isolate any individual Halo device so that you can make sure that you can quarantine it.\N到那时，你应该能够隔离任意一个Halo设备，以确保可以将其隔离。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:05.29,2:00:05.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I love this.\N不，我太喜欢这个了。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:05.83,2:00:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then we can actually see the return on invested capital.\N那么我们实际上可以看到投资资本的回报。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:07.67,2:00:10.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It could pay for itself in three or six months even quicker.\N它甚至可能在三到六个月，甚至更短时间内收回成本。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:10.67,2:00:10.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:10.97,2:00:20.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what you see over here basically is you can tell how every single agent is performing and whether or not they're consuming way too much kind of token\N所以你在这里看到的是，你可以清楚地了解每个代理的性能，以及它们是否消耗了过多的词元成本。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:20.43,2:00:23.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,costs. And if they are, how do you actually contain the costs as you're going through it?\N如果确实如此，那么在过程中你该如何真正控制成本？
Dialogue: 0,2:00:23.99,2:00:24.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I love this Jeetu.\N不，我太喜欢这个了，杰图。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:25.21,2:00:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, everyone else is wondering when can they buy this?\N现在，其他人都在问，他们什么时候能买到这个？
Dialogue: 0,2:00:28.87,2:00:30.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,When is this open for everyone?\N这个什么时候对所有人开放？
Dialogue: 0,2:00:30.85,2:00:34.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, the good news is you can buy the Halo already today.\N好消息是，你今天就可以购买Halo了。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:34.83,2:00:44.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes. And then what we're doing is we're making sure that we provide this entire management apparatus that's currently in early availability for a select set of customers.\N没错。我们现在正在确保为选定客户群体提供目前处于早期可用状态的完整管理架构。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:44.87,2:00:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we'll have it in general availability in the US in early fall.\N但到今年初秋，我们将在美国实现全面可用。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:50.13,2:00:57.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're excited to make sure that we can provide not just the compute, but all of the apparatus that's needed to go out and manage this so that you can have inference\N我们非常期待能够不仅提供计算能力，还能提供所有必要的管理工具，以便您能够顺利部署和管理AI推理。
Dialogue: 0,2:00:57.89,2:01:04.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,running in the cloud, you can have inference running in your data center privately, or you can have inference running on your desk side.\N您可以在云端运行推理，也可以在私有数据中心运行推理，或者在您的桌面端运行推理。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:05.07,2:01:07.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jeetu, we're so grateful to be part of you and Cisco.\N谢图，我们非常感激能与你和思科共同参与。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:07.49,2:01:08.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're so excited.\N我们非常激动。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:08.59,2:01:09.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.\N非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:09.45,2:01:10.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Congratulations. Take care, Jeetu.\N恭喜。保重，谢图。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:10.47,2:01:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:15.45,2:01:22.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,What you just saw brings a vision of scaling AI seamlessly and securely for personal devices all the way to the cloud.\N你们刚刚看到的，展现了从个人设备到云端无缝且安全地扩展AI的愿景。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:22.75,2:01:27.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in the age of AI, intelligence will be pervasive and it will be everywhere.\N但在人工智能时代，智能将无处不在，渗透到每个角落。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:27.83,2:01:32.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next frontier is where AI leaves the screen, enters the world and acts.\N下一个前沿是人工智能走出屏幕，进入现实世界并采取行动。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:33.83,2:01:39.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,That frontier is physical AI, the ultimate application of agentic frameworks.\N这一前沿就是物理 AI，是代理框架的终极应用。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:39.63,2:01:43.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the digital world, an agent plans and completes a task.\N在数字世界中，代理会规划并完成任务。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:43.79,2:01:50.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the physical world, it must also sense motion, navigate uncertainty, and protect people.\N在物理世界中，它还必须感知运动、应对不确定性并保护人类。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:51.37,2:01:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here, intelligence does not just produce an answer, it produces an action.\N在这里，智能不仅产生答案，更会产生行动。
Dialogue: 0,2:01:56.69,2:02:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,When answers become actions, latency becomes safety and reliability becomes trust.\N当答案变为行动，延迟就成为安全，可靠性就转化为信任。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:03.01,2:02:06.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is why the promise of physical AI is so incredibly powerful.\N这正是物理 AI 所蕴含的惊人力量所在。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:06.97,2:02:09.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is not about replacing human potential.\N这并非为了取代人类潜能。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:09.53,2:02:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is about amplifying it, giving surgeons greater precision, keeping people out of harm's way, making farms more productive, supply chains more resilient, and factories more efficient.\N而是放大人类潜能，赋予外科医生更高的精准度，让人员远离危险，提升农场生产力，增强供应链韧性，提高工厂效率。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:24.01,2:02:26.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,The best technology does not make people smaller.\N最好的技术不会让人变得渺小。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:26.97,2:02:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It gives them much greater reach.\N它让人拥有更广阔的影响力。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:29.49,2:02:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,For more than 20 years, AMD has helped power the core capabilities that robotics depend on, from sensing and functional safety to deterministic control and precision motion.\N二十多年来，AMD 一直为机器人技术的核心能力提供支持，从感知和功能安全，到确定性控制和精密运动。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:41.83,2:02:46.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,That foundation is already trusted by millions of companies to find the future of robotics.\N这一基础已获得数百万公司的信赖，助力他们探索机器人的未来。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:46.23,2:02:51.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, that foundation is coming alive in extraordinary ways.\N如今，这一基础正以非凡的方式焕发活力。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:52.67,2:02:54.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are not machines following a script.\N这些并非按照脚本运行的机器。
Dialogue: 0,2:02:55.27,2:03:00.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,They are beginning to perceive the world, reason through uncertainty, and act with purpose.\N它们开始感知世界，推理不确定性，并有目的地行动。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:01.61,2:03:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,The promise of physical AI, already in motion.\N物理 AI 的前景，已然启动。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:06.39,2:03:09.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next era of robotics is not programmed.\N机器人技术的新时代并非由程序编写。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:09.65,2:03:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is autonomous.\N它是自主的。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:11.13,2:03:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,While traditional robots execute instructions, autonomous robots are given an objective.\N传统机器人执行指令，而自主机器人则被赋予目标。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:17.25,2:03:19.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And from there, they determine how to achieve it.\N之后，它们自行决定如何实现目标。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:19.87,2:03:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they do this all at once, and all in real time.\N它们同时且实时地完成这一切。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:23.91,2:03:30.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,The robot must orchestrate intelligence, motion, and safety continuously.\N机器人必须持续协调智能、运动与安全。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:30.11,2:03:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every part must respond at the speed of the world around it.\N每个部分都必须以与周围世界同步的速度作出响应。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:35.29,2:03:38.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,That demands an entirely new kind of robotics brain.\N这需要一种全新的机器人大脑。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:39.53,2:03:43.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to solve that, we rethought its architecture from the ground up.\N为了解决这个问题，我们从零开始彻底重构了其架构。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:44.05,2:03:53.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, I'm so excited to introduce the AMD Kria AI System On Module, powered by Ryzen AI Embedded X100.\N今天，我非常激动地向大家介绍 AMD Kria AI 系统级模块，搭载 Ryzen AI 嵌入式 X100。
Dialogue: 0,2:03:58.79,2:04:08.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,It brings CPU, GPU, NPU, and unified memory together in one compact, open standard architecture.\N它将 CPU、GPU、NPU 和统一内存整合在一个紧凑且开放标准的架构中。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:08.89,2:04:17.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This allows robots to process perception, AI reasoning, and do it all simultaneously and in real time.\N这使得机器人能够同时实时处理感知、AI 推理。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:18.31,2:04:21.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,The architecture is different, but the results are decisive.\N架构虽不同，但结果却至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:22.71,2:04:37.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,In third party testing against NVIDIA Jetson Thor, Kria delivers 3.4 times better real-time results, 2.3 times more concurrent agents, and 1.6 times more CPU capacity.\N在第三方测试中对比英伟达 Jetson Thor，Kria 的实时性能提升 3.4 倍，可并行处理的智能体数量多出 2.3 倍，CPU 性能提升 1.6 倍。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:37.31,2:04:43.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,That means faster reactions, and greater headroom for the robot to take on more complex work.\N这意味着更快的响应速度，以及机器人承担更复杂任务的更大余量。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:44.65,2:04:47.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all this without compromising control or safety.\N而这一切并未牺牲控制性或安全性。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:48.83,2:04:54.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,But to find the next era of robotics takes more than a powerful brain.\N但要开启机器人技术的新时代，光有强大的大脑是不够的。
Dialogue: 0,2:04:55.39,2:05:01.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Developers need a complete path from an idea to a machine operating in the real world.\N开发者需要一条从构想到真实世界运行机器的完整路径。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:02.01,2:05:08.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we are introducing AMD's Kria AI Robotics Developer Platform.\N今天，我们推出了 AMD 的 Kria AI 机器人开发平台。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:13.99,2:05:20.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,The industry's first turnkey open, fully integrated robotic system.\N行业首个开箱即用的开放式全集成机器人系统。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:22.15,2:05:23.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Laura, so much.\N非常感谢你，劳拉。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:27.88,2:05:37.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the center is the Kria AI System on module, paired with a robotics carrier card designed for sensing and connectivity.\N核心是 Kria AI 系统级模块，搭配专为感知和连接设计的机器人载卡。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:37.84,2:05:45.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Built on ROCm and ROS2, this platform gives developers everything they need to move from concept to prototype in days.\N基于 ROCm 和 ROS2，该平台让开发者能在数天内完成从概念到原型的构建。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:46.22,2:05:53.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the same module carries forward into production, with no migration or redesign needed at the finish line.\N该模块可直接用于生产，无需在最终阶段进行迁移或重新设计。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:53.42,2:05:58.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can build faster and move from imagination to deployment with absolute confidence.\N你可以更快地构建，自信地将构想转化为实际部署。
Dialogue: 0,2:05:59.94,2:06:06.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the breadth only AMD can bring to autonomous robotics from the first signal to the final motion.\N这种广度唯有 AMD 能为自主机器人从首个信号到最终动作带来。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:07.72,2:06:15.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,AMD Kria for the brain, Versal for the spine, Zynq for the joints, and Spartan for the sensors.\NAMD Kria 作为大脑，Versal 作为脊柱，Zynq 作为关节，Spartan 作为传感器。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:16.18,2:06:27.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each layer purpose built for its role, working together in one intelligent system, connecting perception and high-level reasoning to real-time control.\N每一层都专为自身角色打造，协同工作于一个智能系统中，连接感知与高层推理至实时控制。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:28.70,2:06:34.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,The future will not be defined by one model, one machine, or one company.\N未来不会由单一模型、单一机器或单一公司定义。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:34.66,2:06:43.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will be built in the open, across silicon, software, systems, and an ecosystem moving forward together.\N它将在开放中构建，跨越芯片、软件、系统和生态系统，共同向前迈进。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:43.94,2:06:52.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,From the cloud to the PC and now into the physical world, AMD continues to build a compute foundation for intelligence everywhere.\N从云端到个人电脑，如今更深入到现实世界，AMD持续构建无处不在智能计算的基础。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:53.30,2:06:59.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll laser focused on the future so our solution can augment and expand what people are capable of achieving.\N我们将聚焦未来，让我们的解决方案增强并拓展人们所能实现的能力。
Dialogue: 0,2:06:59.82,2:07:03.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next era of AI will not just unfold behind the screen.\N下一个AI时代将不仅发生在屏幕背后。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:03.52,2:07:05.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will unfold in the world around us.\N它将发生在我们周围的现实世界中。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:06.02,2:07:12.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, to bring it all together and take us to what comes next, please welcome back Lisa to the stage.\N现在，让我们把这一切整合起来，迈向下一个阶段，请欢迎丽莎再次登台。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:17.86,2:07:18.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi, Lisa.\N你好，丽莎。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:20.46,2:07:21.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alright.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:21.62,2:07:22.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Jack.\N谢谢，杰克。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:22.78,2:07:24.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's been a big day.\N这真是一个重要的日子。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:24.66,2:07:32.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've covered a lot, from our data center products, to enterprise AI, to personal and physical AI, and the software that ties it all together.\N我们涵盖了大量内容，从数据中心产品，到企业AI，再到个人AI和物理AI，以及连接这一切的软件。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:33.22,2:07:36.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the strongest product portfolio in our history.\N这是我们历史上最强的产品组合。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:36.50,2:07:39.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we believe it's the strongest portfolio in the industry.\N我们相信，这也是业内最强的产品组合。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:39.70,2:07:45.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it's really just the beginning, because what our customers count on is not just today.\N但这仅仅是个开始，因为客户所依赖的不仅仅是今天。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:45.76,2:07:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,They really count on us looking ahead and pushing the bleeding edge of technology.\N他们真正依赖的是我们能够前瞻未来，不断推动技术的最前沿。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:50.44,2:07:54.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I want to spend the last few minutes giving you a preview of what we're working on.\N所以我想用最后几分钟，向大家预览一下我们正在开发的内容。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:54.96,2:07:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Starting with CPUs.\N从 CPU 开始。
Dialogue: 0,2:07:56.90,2:07:59.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,In 2028, we're going to introduce Florence.\N到 2028 年，我们将推出 Florence。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:00.56,2:08:03.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Florence brings the next Gen Zen 7 cores.\NFlorence 将搭载下一代 Zen 7 核心。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:04.00,2:08:05.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's leading-edge process technology.\N它采用前沿的制程技术。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:05.86,2:08:11.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a new set of AI compute extensions to really ensure that we have all of the AI capability.\N它配备了一套全新的 AI 计算扩展，以确保我们具备全部的 AI 能力。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:12.18,2:08:14.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it supports the latest memory technologies.\N并支持最新的内存技术。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:14.86,2:08:16.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're not stopping there.\N但我们不会止步于此。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:16.30,2:08:22.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're already deep in development of Ravenna, our eighth-generation EPYC family built on Zen 8.\N我们已经深入开发 Ravenna，这是基于 Zen 8 的第八代 EPYC 系列。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:22.62,2:08:26.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that family is already well under development for 2030.\N而这一系列已经提前进入 2030 年的开发阶段。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:27.40,2:08:33.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, to give you a little bit of a flavor, Florence is again going to extend our biggest advantage with EPYC.\N现在，先给大家一点感觉，弗洛伦萨将继续拓展我们EPYC最大的优势。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:33.76,2:08:41.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's all about product breath and having the right foundation and also the right family for each workload.\N这关乎产品广度，以及为每种工作负载提供正确的基础和合适的系列。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:41.52,2:08:44.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you have Florence, you have Ferrara, you have Fidenza.\N所以你有弗洛伦萨，有费拉拉，有菲登扎。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:45.22,2:08:51.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's really built on a full family of CPUs that is optimized for these different workloads.\N它建立在一套完整的、针对不同工作负载优化的CPU家族之上。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:51.22,2:08:55.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's giving the customers the right CPU for every workload.\N这为客户提供每个工作负载所需的正确CPU。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:55.56,2:08:57.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that is our commitment with EPYC.\N这就是我们对EPYC的承诺。
Dialogue: 0,2:08:58.54,2:08:59.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, moving to Instinct.\N现在转向Instinct。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:00.50,2:09:06.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are continuing our cadence of delivering a new generation every single year.\N我们将继续保持每年发布新一代产品的节奏。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:06.80,2:09:09.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,MI500 brings next-generation HBM.\NMI500带来了下一代HBM。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:10.02,2:09:14.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,It brings a larger scale-up domain because scaling is everything.\N它带来了更大的扩展域，因为扩展至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:14.52,2:09:18.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it introduces new copper and optical interconnects.\N并引入了新的铜质和光互连技术。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:18.56,2:09:25.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with MI600, it's powered by our CDNA Next architecture, and it's already deep in development for 2028.\N而MI600则基于我们的CDNA Next架构，目前已深入开发，目标为2028年推出。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:26.30,2:09:35.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, to give you an idea of what we see from a performance standpoint, every generation of Instinct has delivered a major big step up in performance.\N从性能角度来看，每一代Instinct都实现了性能的显著提升。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:36.56,2:09:43.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with MI455, we've talked a lot about it, delivering 35 times more inference throughput compared to MI355.\N而MI455，我们已经讨论过很多，其推理吞吐量相比MI355提升了35倍。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:44.54,2:09:47.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we're really, really excited about MI500.\N但我们现在真正兴奋的是MI500。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:47.72,2:09:53.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we see is another opportunity to take a major step up and actually bend the curve again.\N我们看到的是一次再次实现重大飞跃的机遇，甚至能再次扭转曲线。
Dialogue: 0,2:09:54.58,2:10:05.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So MI500 will deliver the largest generational leap in the industry of Instinct, putting us on track to deliver more than 2,000 times higher inference throughput in just four years.\N因此，MI500将成为Instinct系列中代际提升最大的产品，让我们有望在短短四年内实现推理吞吐量超过2000倍的提升。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:12.90,2:10:17.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, what I can tell you is we are working with a number of our customers already on this design point.\N目前我可以告诉你们的是，我们已经与多家客户开始合作推进这一设计。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:18.14,2:10:24.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,MI500 is super exciting, and the feedback we're getting from customers is just fantastic.\NMI500令人非常兴奋，客户反馈也极为出色。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:24.76,2:10:32.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, put the CPU, GPU, and the networking roadmaps together, and you can now see a complete cadence of our rack scale systems.\N现在将CPU、GPU和网络技术路线图整合起来，你就能看到我们机架级系统完整的演进节奏。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:33.30,2:10:45.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you should expect from AMD a new Helios system every year delivering more performance, more capacity so that we can run larger models, more agents at better total cost of ownership.\N因此，AMD每年都会推出新一代Helios系统，带来更高的性能和更大的容量，让我们能够运行更大规模的模型，支持更多智能体，同时降低总体拥有成本。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:46.44,2:10:54.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that gives our customers the complete, predictable roadmap to plan and scale their infrastructure for years to come.\N这为我们的客户提供了完整且可预测的技术路线图，便于他们规划和扩展未来数年的基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:54.40,2:10:57.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,So lots of exciting things in store over the next few years.\N未来几年将有大量令人兴奋的进展。
Dialogue: 0,2:10:58.60,2:11:01.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So with that, let me wrap this up for this morning.\N好了，那么今天上午就讲到这里，我来做个总结。
Dialogue: 0,2:11:02.06,2:11:08.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, I hope you saw a little bit about how we're really looking at that compute from every angle.\N今天，我希望你们看到了我们如何从各个角度来审视计算。
Dialogue: 0,2:11:09.14,2:11:22.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So every aspect of AI compute, whether you're talking about Helios or MI455 or Venice for the world's largest AI systems, or you're talking about MI430 and MI350 for Sovereign and Enterprise AI.\N因此，无论是讨论用于全球最大AI系统的Helios或MI455或Venice，还是讨论用于主权和企业AI的MI430和MI350，我们都在关注AI计算的各个方面。
Dialogue: 0,2:11:23.30,2:11:25.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,You saw the passion in Vamsi with ROCm AI.\N你们看到了瓦姆西在ROCm AI方面的热情。
Dialogue: 0,2:11:26.30,2:11:35.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's so good to see how much has come through that platform in terms of making developers make it much, much easier for developers to access the AMD platform.\N看到这个平台在帮助开发者更轻松地接入AMD平台方面取得了如此多的进展，真是太好了。
Dialogue: 0,2:11:36.70,2:11:46.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then Jack talked about Gorgon Halo and our new Kria AI platforms really bringing together the leadership of the end-to-end AI story, including PCs and physical AI.\N然后杰克谈到了Gorgon Halo以及我们的全新Kria AI平台，真正整合了端到端AI故事的领导力，包括个人电脑和物理AI。
Dialogue: 0,2:11:47.36,2:11:56.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So lots of new information, but I want to say a very, very special thank you to all of our partners who joined us today because it is really through those\N今天有很多新信息，但我想特别感谢所有今天加入我们的合作伙伴，因为正是通过这些合作，
Dialogue: 0,2:11:56.20,2:12:00.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,partnerships that we're able to do the most amazing things together.\N我们才能共同完成最了不起的事情。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:01.40,2:12:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if I just leave you with a final thought, when I think about where AI is today, the biggest change that we see is we're no longer talking about what might be possible.\N如果让我留下一个最后的想法，当我思考AI今天所处的位置时，最大的变化是，我们不再只是讨论可能实现什么。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:13.14,2:12:22.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're actually seeing how AI can have real and significant impact across every industry and every part of our lives, our personal lives.\N我们实际上正在看到AI如何在每个行业以及我们生活的方方面面，包括个人生活，产生真实而重大的影响。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:22.56,2:12:32.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I have to say that I've spent my entire career in tech believing that high-performance computing can make the world an incredibly better place.\N我必须说，我整个职业生涯都在科技领域，一直相信高性能计算能让世界变得无比美好。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:32.40,2:12:35.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I have never, ever believed that more than I do today.\N但我从未像今天这样，如此坚定地相信这一点。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:36.40,2:12:48.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,At AMD, what we're focused on is building the technology, the roadmaps, and the partnerships, and there's never been a more exciting moment than today for our 30,000 plus engineers.\N在AMD，我们专注于构建技术、路线图和合作伙伴关系，而对我们三万多名工程师来说，今天是前所未有的激动时刻。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:48.76,2:12:51.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is really the next phase of AI.\N这确实是AI的下一个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,2:12:51.46,2:13:01.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where we make AI, give the AI the opportunity with all the tools and all the capabilities to really bring meaningful real-world impact.\N这里我们将打造AI，赋予AI所有工具和能力，真正实现有意义的现实世界影响。
Dialogue: 0,2:13:01.68,2:13:07.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I can tell you I could not be more excited to build all of that together with you, our ecosystem.\N我可以告诉你们，能与你们——我们的生态系统——共同构建这一切，我感到无比激动。
Dialogue: 0,2:13:08.50,2:13:10.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for joining us today.\N非常感谢大家今天加入我们。
